{"id": "90", "question": "how to prepare blood slide", "gt": "To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\n\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so that it runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\n4. Push the second slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n5. Repeat step 4 to make two smears.\n6. Allow the smears to air dry.\n7. Label the slides clearly.\n8. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.\n\nNote: It is important to sterilize the needle used to obtain the blood sample by heating it with a flame before using it. Additionally, it is essential to wear rubber gloves when handling blood to avoid coming into contact with potentially infectious materials.", "pred": "These steps ensure a proper blood smear for examination.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\n\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\n5. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n6. Make 2 smears.\n7. Allow the smears to air dry.\n8. Label the slides clearly.\n9. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.\n\nThese steps ensure a proper blood smear for examination.", "cot": "[\"To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n5. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n6. Make 2 smears.\\n7. Allow the smears to air dry.\\n8. Label the slides clearly.\\n9. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.\\n\\nThese steps ensure a proper blood smear for examination.\", \"To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.**  \\n   - Ensure the slide is clean and free of any contaminants.\\n\\n2. **Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.**  \\n   - Use a clean dropper or similar tool to place the blood drop carefully.\\n\\n3. **Take another clean slide.**  \\n   - This slide will be used to create the smear.\\n\\n4. **Hold the second slide at an angle of about 45 degrees.**  \\n   - This angle helps in creating a thin layer of blood.\\n\\n5. **Touch the blood on the first slide with one end of the second slide.**  \\n   - Carefully touch the blood to ensure the blood runs along the edge of the second slide by capillary action.\\n\\n6. **Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.**  \\n   - Use gentle pressure to spread the blood evenly and thinly across the slide.\\n\\n7. **Make 2 smears.**  \\n   - This ensures a more even distribution of the blood cells on the slide.\\n\\n8. **Allow the smears to air dry.**  \\n   - Ensure the slides are completely dry before proceeding.\\n\\n9. **Label the slides clearly.**  \\n   - Write any necessary information on the labels to identify the samples.\\n\\n10. **Place the dried slides in the provided slide transport containers.**  \\n    - Use appropriate containers to store the slides safely and protect the samples.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can prepare a blood slide for examination or analysis.\", \"To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n5. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n6. Make 2 smears.\\n7. Allow the smears to air dry.\\n8. Label the slides clearly.\\n9. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.\", \"1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\\n4. Touch the blood on the first slide with one end of the second slide so the blood runs along the edge by capillary action.\\n5. Push the second slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n6. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\\n7. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.\\n\\nAnswer:[Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface, add one small drop of blood to one end, take another slide at a 45-degree angle, touch the blood with the second slide, push the second slide along the first to form a thin smear, make 2 smears, air dry, label clearly, and place in transport containers.]\"]", "time_sec": 28.206, "generation_time_seconds": 28.2022, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0004, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 10549, 264, 6543, 14983, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 10771, 264, 4240, 8991, 14983, 389, 264, 10063, 7329, 624, 17, 13, 2691, 825, 2613, 5943, 315, 6543, 311, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 624, 18, 13, 11778, 2441, 4240, 14983, 323, 3331, 432, 518, 458, 9210, 315, 911, 220, 19, 20, 12348, 624, 19, 13, 19338, 279, 6543, 448, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 773, 279, 6543, 8473, 3156, 2