{"id": "118", "question": "how are water shares transferred", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the process for transferring water shares includes the following steps:\n\n1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate.\n2. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership.\n3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer.\n4. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\n5. An additional fee of $75.00 must be paid when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form, if necessary.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question of how water shares are transferred is: By following the steps outlined above, which include the seller returning the Water Stock Certificate, the new owner providing proof of ownership, and paying the required fees.", "pred": "Water shares are transferred by the seller returning the Water Stock Certificate and signing it to indicate its transfer, the new owner providing proof of ownership, and paying a fee of $75.00 to the company to process the transfer. A new Water Stock Certificate is then issued to the new owner, officially transferring the water shares into their name.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "First, let's identify the steps involved in transferring water shares from the given passages:\n\n1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate.\n2. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership.\n3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer.\n4. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\n\nBased on these steps, the process for transferring water shares involves the following:\n\n1. The seller must relinquish the Water Stock Certificate and sign it to indicate its transfer.\n2. The new owner must present proof of their ownership, which is necessary to prove their right to the water shares.\n3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to the company to process the transfer of the Water Stock Certificate.\n4. After the fee is paid and all necessary documents are in order, a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner, officially transferring the water shares into their name.\n\nAnswer: Water shares are transferred by the seller returning the Water Stock Certificate and signing it to indicate its transfer, the new owner providing proof of ownership, and paying a fee of $75.00 to the company to process the transfer. A new Water Stock Certificate is then issued to the new owner, officially transferring the water shares into their name.", "cot": "[\"First, let's identify the steps involved in transferring water shares from the given passages:\\n\\n1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate.\\n2. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership.\\n3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer.\\n4. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\\n\\nBased on these steps, the process for transferring water shares involves the following:\\n\\n1. The seller must relinquish the Water Stock Certificate and sign it to indicate its transfer.\\n2. The new owner must present proof of their ownership, which is necessary to prove their right to the water shares.\\n3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to the company to process the transfer of the Water Stock Certificate.\\n4. After the fee is paid and all necessary documents are in order, a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner, officially transferring the water shares into their name.\\n\\nAnswer: Water shares are transferred by the seller returning the Water Stock Certificate and signing it to indicate its transfer, the new owner providing proof of ownership, and paying a fee of $75.00 to the company to process the transfer. A new Water Stock Certificate is then issued to the new owner, officially transferring the water shares into their name.\", \"To transfer water shares, the following steps are required:\\n\\n1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate.\\n2. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership.\\n3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer.\\n4. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\\n\\nAnswer:[The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.]\", \"To transfer water shares, the following steps are required:\\n\\n1. **Seller must return the Water Stock Certificate:** The original Water Stock Certificate assigned to the seller must be returned to the company.\\n2. **New owner must provide proof of ownership:** The new owner of the property must present proof of their ownership to the company.\\n3. **Fee of $75.00 must be paid:** A processing fee of $75.00 is required to transfer the Water Stock Certificate.\\n4. **New Water Stock Certificate will be issued:** A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\\n\\nThese steps ensure a legal and formal transfer of the water shares into the new owner's name.\", \"To determine how water shares are transferred, I will analyze the information provided in the passages:\\n\\n1. The first passage states that there is a fee of $75.00 to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer.\\n2. The second passage provides more detailed steps: \\n   - The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate and sign the back of it.\\n   - The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership.\\n   - There is a fee of $75.00 to be paid for processing the transfer.\\n   - A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\\n3. The third passage briefly mentions that there are three types of water rights in Utah and advises understanding the steps for transferring water rights into one's name.\\n\\nBased on this information, the key points for transferring water shares are:\\n- The seller must return the original certificate and sign the back of it.\\n- The new owner must provide proof of ownership.\\n- A fee of $75.00 is required to process the transfer.\\n- A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\\n\\nAnswer: Water shares are transferred by returning the original certificate signed by the seller, providing proof of ownership by the new owner, paying a $75.00 fee, and obtaining a new Water Stock Certificate issued to the new owner of record.\"]", "time_sec": 29.331, "generation_time_seconds": 29.3265, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0003, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [5338, 11, 1077, 594, 10542, 279, 7354, 6398, 304, 49951, 3015, 13248, 504, 279, 2661, 46769, 1447, 16, 13, 576, 22856, 1969, 470, 279, 9959, 12648, 31402, 429, 572, 12607, 311, 1105, 323, 1841, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 15748, 624, 17, 13, 576, 501, 6372, 315, 279, 3343, 1969, 3410, 11064, 315, 15278, 624, 18, 13, 362, 11060, 315, 400, 22, 20, 13, 15, 15, 1969, 387, 7171, 311, 1882, 264, 9959, 12648, 31402, 8317, 624, 19, 13, 362, 501, 9959, 12648, 31402, 686, 387, 10897, 311, 279, 501, 6372, 315, 3255, 382, 28715, 389, 1493, 7354, 11, 279, 1882, 369, 49951, 3015, 13248, 17601, 279, 2701, 1447, 16, 13, 576, 22856, 1969, 84398, 812, 279, 9959, 12648, 31402, 323, 1841, 432, 311, 13216, 1181, 8317, 624, 17, 13, 576, 501, 6372, 1969, 3042, 11064, 315, 862, 15278, 11, 892, 374, 5871, 311, 12118, 862, 1290, 311, 279, 3015, 13248, 624, 18, 