aying a $75.00 fee, and obtaining a new Water Stock Certificate issued to the new owner of record."}], "input_len": 409, "output_tokens": 868, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 43.75, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "129", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "gt": "What are the dimensions of the shed in passage 3?\n\nThe dimensions of the shed in passage 3 are 6 feet long by 4 feet wide.", "pred": "Building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, the site needs to be prepared with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Then, two 4 x 4 skids are cut to the desired length and set on the ground according to the shed building plans. Two 2 x 6 rim joists are also cut, and the floor is assembled and set on the skids. The frame is checked for square and anchored to the skids with four joist clip angles. The walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Step 1: Read the passages carefully to understand the information provided about building a lean-to shed.\n\nStep 2: Identify the key details in the passages. \n- Passages discuss the steps for building a lean-to shed, including preparing the site, cutting and assembling skids, cutting and setting rim joists, and attaching flooring.\n- The dimensions of the shed are mentioned as 6 feet long by 4 feet wide.\n- The passages also mention that the walls are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame.\n\nStep 3: Use the key details to answer the question \"building a lean-to shed.\"\n\nAnswer: Building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, the site needs to be prepared with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Then, two 4 x 4 skids are cut to the desired length and set on the ground according to the shed building plans. Two 2 x 6 rim joists are also cut, and the floor is assembled and set on the skids. The frame is checked for square and anchored to the skids with four joist clip angles. The walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame.", "cot": "[\"Step 1: Read the passages carefully to understand the information provided about building a lean-to shed.\\n\\nStep 2: Identify the key details in the passages. \\n- Passages discuss the steps for building a lean-to shed, including preparing the site, cutting and assembling skids, cutting and setting rim joists, and attaching flooring.\\n- The dimensions of the shed are mentioned as 6 feet long by 4 feet wide.\\n- The passages also mention that the walls are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame.\\n\\nStep 3: Use the key details to answer the question \\\"building a lean-to shed.\\\"\\n\\nAnswer: Building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, the site needs to be prepared with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Then, two 4 x 4 skids are cut to the desired length and set on the ground according to the shed building plans. Two 2 x 6 rim joists are also cut, and the floor is assembled and set on the skids. The frame is checked for square and anchored to the skids with four joist clip angles. The walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame.\", \"Building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Next, cut two 4x4 skids to a length of 6 feet and position them as skids. Cut two 2x6 rim joists to 7 3/4 inches and six joists to 44 3/4 inches. Assemble the floor and set it on the skids as per the lean-to shed plans, ensuring it is square. Anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.\\n\\nAnswer: Building a lean-to shed involves preparing the site with compacted gravel, cutting and positioning skids, and assembling the floor frame with joists and clip angles.\", \"Building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Next, cut two 4 x 4 skids to the required length and set them on a level surface. Then, cut two 2 x 6 rim joists and six joists to the appropriate lengths. Assemble the floor and place it on the skids, ensuring it is square. Anchor the frame to the skids with joist clip angles. For the walls, they are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame. The dimensions of the shed can be easily expanded in increments of 2 or 4 feet.\", \"To build a lean-to shed, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Prepare the Site:** Start by preparing the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel.\\n\\n2. **Cut and Set Skids:** Cut two 4x4 skids to a length of 6 feet each. Set and level these skids according to the shed building plans.\\n\\n3. **Cut and Assemble Joists:** Cut two 2x6 rim joists to a length of 7 3/4 feet and six joists to a length of 44 3/4 feet. Assemble the floor and place it on the skids as described in the floor framing section of the lean-to shed plans. Ensure the frame is square and secure it to the skids with four joist clip angles.\\n\\n4. **Attach Flooring:** Position the frame on the skids and toenail the floor joists to the skids. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame.\\n\\n5. **Construct Walls Separately:** The walls for the shed are built separately and then raised onto the frame.\\n\\n6. **Expand Dimensions:** The shed shown is 6 feet long by 4 feet wide. You can easily expand its dimensions in increments of 2 or 4 feet by following similar framing steps.\\n\\nBy following these detailed steps, you can construct a sturdy and well-anchored lean-to shed.\"]", "time_sec": 27.016, "generation_time_seconds": 27.0119, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0003, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 4457, 279, 46769, 15516, 311, 3535, 279, 1995, 3897, 911, 4752, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 382, 8304, 220, 17, 25, 64547, 279, 1376, 3565, 304, 279, 46769, 13, 715, 12, 9970, 1134, 4263, 279, 7354, 369, 4752, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 11, 2670, 20045, 279, 2747, 11, 14376, 323, 80659, 1901, 3365, 11, 14376, 323, 6243, 30130, 7647, 1671, 11, 323, 71808, 36148, 624, 12, 576, 15336, 315, 279, 24354, 525, 9733, 438, 220, 21, 7541, 1293, 553, 220, 19,