0.3139, -0.925, -1.972, -0.5064, -0.5136, -0.2154, -0.0032, -0.0, -1.8405, -0.0291, -0.0158, -0.0002, -0.0006, -1.1159, -0.0024, -1.0635, -0.252, -0.3696, -0.2744, -1.2034, 0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0048, -0.0003], "cumulative_logprob": -54.576, "norm_logp": -0.1875, "input_len": 447, "output_tokens": 291, "pred": "By following these detailed steps, you can construct a sturdy and well-anchored lean-to shed."}], "input_len": 447, "output_tokens": 822, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 11.27, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "139", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded. The block concept is followed, where assets of the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are grouped together and considered as a single asset. The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, even if it is not used for business or profession in that year and subsequent years.", "pred": "These steps ensure that the treatment of discarded assets is consistent with the block concept and the specific provisions of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "The treatment when an asset is discarded as per Income Tax Act, 1961, involves the following steps:\n\n1. **Identification of the Asset Block**: Under the block concept, all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are grouped together and considered as a single asset.\n\n2. **Section 43(6)**: If an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act allows the scrap value of the asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded.\n\n3. **Adjustment of Block Value**: Any alterations to the value of the block must be made strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\n\n4. **Claiming Depreciation**: The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, which is calculated as the opening WDV (Written Down Value) of the asset less the scrap value.\n\nThese steps ensure that the treatment of discarded assets is consistent with the block concept and the specific provisions of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "cot": "[\"The treatment when an asset is discarded as per Income Tax Act, 1961, involves the following steps:\\n\\n1. **Identification of the Asset Block**: Under the block concept, all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are grouped together and considered as a single asset.\\n\\n2. **Section 43(6)**: If an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act allows the scrap value of the asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded.\\n\\n3. **Adjustment of Block Value**: Any alterations to the value of the block must be made strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\\n\\n4. **Claiming Depreciation**: The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, which is calculated as the opening WDV (Written Down Value) of the asset less the scrap value.\\n\\nThese steps ensure that the treatment of discarded assets is consistent with the block concept and the specific provisions of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\", \"To answer the question \\\"What is the treatment when an asset is discarded as per the Income Tax Act?\\\" using the information provided in the given passages, let's break down the relevant details:\\n\\n1. **Passage 1:** It states that under the block concept, all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are clubbed together and considered as a single asset.\\n\\n2. **Passage 2:** This passage seems to be an illustration and does not directly relate to the treatment of assets when discarded. It mentions income before depreciation and tax, but does not discuss the treatment of assets discarded.\\n\\n3. **Passage 3:** This passage explicitly states that depreciation is allowed under the Income Tax Act, 1961, following the block concept. It also mentions that if an asset is discarded, the assessee (taxpayer) is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of such discarded asset, which is defined as the opening written-down value (WDV) of the asset less the scrap value.\\n\\nBased on the information provided:\\n\\n- The block concept is used to club assets together based on their class and rate of depreciation.\\n- When an asset is discarded, its depreciation can still be claimed based on the block concept, provided the scrap value is subtracted from the opening WDV.\\n\\nTherefore, the treatment when an asset is discarded is as follows:\\n\\n1. The asset is considered as part of a block with other assets of the same class and rate of depreciation.\\n2. The depreciation is calculated based on the block concept.\\n3. If the asset is discarded, the depreciation claim can still be made based on the block concept, but the scrap value must be subtracted from the opening WDV to find the residual value for depreciation purposes.\\n\\nAnswer: The treatment when an asset is discarded as per the Income Tax Act involves treating the asset as part of a block with other assets of the same class and rate of depreciation. The depreciation claim can still be made based on the block concept, but the scrap value must be subtracted from the opening WDV to find the residual value for depreciation purposes.\", \"Step 1: Identify the relevant information in the passages.\\n- Passage 1: \\\"In case an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, section 43(6) permits the scrap value of the asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded.\\\"\\n\\nStep 2: Analyze the information.\\n- The passage states that when an asset is discarded, its scrap value can be reduced from the block in the previous year.\\n\\nStep 3: Formulate the answer based on the information provided.\\n- The treatment when an asset is discarded under the Income Tax Act is to reduce its scrap value from the block in the previous year.\\n\\nAnswer: The treatment when an asset is discarded under the Income Tax Act is to reduce its scrap value from the block in the previous year.\", \"Answer: When an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset is permitted to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. Under the block concept, all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are clubbed together and considered as a single asset. Any alterations to the value of the block have to be strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\"]", "time_sec": 31.325, "generation_time_seconds": 31.3206, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0002, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 6380, 979, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 438, 817, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 11, 17601, 279, 2701, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 95212, 315, 279, 22605, 8362, 95518, 9449, 279, 2504, 7286, 11, 678, 11770, 15679, 2878, 279, 1852, 536, 323, 3832, 311, 279, 1852, 4379, 315, 93089, 525, 40041, 3786, 323, 6509, 438, 264, 3175, 9329, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 9620, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 32295, 25, 1416, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 6147, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 311, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 279, 9329, 374, 43210, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 38616, 478, 315, 8362, 5162, 95518, 5765, 59986, 311, 279, 897, 315, 279, 2504, 1969, 387, 1865, 25470, 304, 18353, 448, 279, 19156, 315, 15585, 16824, 422, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 45544, 287, 4148, 2758, 7101, 95518, 576, 79040, 4060, 374, 19867, 311, 3717, 93089, 389, 279, 32147, 897, 315, 279, 43210, 9329, 11, 892, 374, 16588, 438, 279, 8568, 467, 61971, 320, 35624, 6285, 5162, 8, 315, 279, 9329, 2686, 279, 20843, 897, 382, 9485, 7354, 5978, 429, 279, 6380, 315, 43210, 11770, 374, 12966, 448, 279, 2504,