{"id": "175", "question": "how to soften sugar", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to soften sugar:\n\n1. Place brown sugar in an airtight container with a damp paper towel or napkin on top. Cover tightly and let it sit for a couple of days. Remove the damp paper towel, and the sugar should be soft. (Passage 1)\n2. Preheat the oven to a low temperature (150-200 degrees), place hardened granulated sugar in an ovenproof container, and tap it with a spoon after 15 minutes. If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave it in for an hour or two to dry out completely. Store granulated sugar in an airtight container. (Passage 2)\n3. Keep brown sugar soft by storing it in an airtight container with minimal air space between the sugar and the lid. Pack the sugar into the smallest container possible. (Passage 3)", "pred": "**", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To soften sugar, follow these steps based on the provided passages:\n\n1. **Brown Sugar Softening:**\n   - Place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar.\n   - Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil.\n   - Cover tightly.\n   - Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days.\n\n2. **Granulated Sugar Softening:**\n   - Preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees.\n   - Remove the sugar from the package and put it in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar.\n   - Place the sugar in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes.\n   - Tap the sugar with a spoon.\n   - If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out.\n   - Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container.\n   - Store confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator).\n   - When it gets moist, it develops lumps.\n\n**Final Answer:**\nTo soften sugar, you can follow these methods:\n- For brown sugar, place it in a sealed container with a damp paper towel on top, cover tightly, and remove the paper towel after a couple of days.\n- For granulated sugar, preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, place the sugar in an ovenproof container, and bake it for approximately 15 minutes. Tap the sugar with a spoon, and if it starts to fall apart, continue drying out in the oven for an hour or two. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container and confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location.", "cot": "[\"To soften sugar, follow these steps based on the provided passages:\\n\\n1. **Brown Sugar Softening:**\\n   - Place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar.\\n   - Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil.\\n   - Cover tightly.\\n   - Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days.\\n\\n2. **Granulated Sugar Softening:**\\n   - Preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees.\\n   - Remove the sugar from the package and put it in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar.\\n   - Place the sugar in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes.\\n   - Tap the sugar with a spoon.\\n   - If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out.\\n   - Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container.\\n   - Store confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator).\\n   - When it gets moist, it develops lumps.\\n\\n**Final Answer:**\\nTo soften sugar, you can follow these methods:\\n- For brown sugar, place it in a sealed container with a damp paper towel on top, cover tightly, and remove the paper towel after a couple of days.\\n- For granulated sugar, preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, place the sugar in an ovenproof container, and bake it for approximately 15 minutes. Tap the sugar with a spoon, and if it starts to fall apart, continue drying out in the oven for an hour or two. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container and confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location.\", \"Step 1: Identify the types of sugar mentioned in the passages.\\nThe passages mention brown sugar, granulated sugar, and confectioners sugar.\\n\\nStep 2: Determine the methods to soften each type of sugar.\\n1. Brown sugar:\\n   - Keep it sealed in an airtight container.\\n   - Limit air exposure.\\n   - Pack the sugar into the smallest container possible.\\n2. Granulated sugar:\\n   - Preheat the oven to the lowest temperature (150-200 degrees).\\n   - Place the sugar in an ovenproof container.\\n   - Tap the sugar with a spoon.\\n   - If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out.\\n   - Store granulated sugar in an airtight container.\\n3. Confectioners sugar:\\n   - Store it in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator).\\n   - When it gets moist, it develops lumps.\\n\\nStep 3: Provide the final answer.\\nAnswer: To soften sugar, follow these steps depending on the type of sugar:\\n1. Brown sugar: Keep it sealed in an airtight container, limit air exposure, and pack the sugar into the smallest container possible.\\n2. Granulated sugar: Preheat the oven to the lowest temperature (150-200 degrees), place the sugar in an ovenproof container, tap the sugar with a spoon, and if it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container.\\n3. Confectioners sugar: Store it in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator). When it gets moist, it develops lumps.\", \"To soften sugar, you can use the following methods:\\n\\n1. For brown sugar:\\n   - Place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar.\\n   - Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil.\\n   - Cover tightly.\\n   - Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days.\\n\\n2. For granulated sugar:\\n   - Preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees.\\n   - Remove sugar from the package and put it in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar.\\n   - Place the sugar in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes.\\n   - Tap the sugar with a spoon to help it soften.\\n   - If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out.\\n   - Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container.\\n   - Store confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator).\\n   - When it gets moist, it develops lumps.\", \"Answer: To soften sugar, you can preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, around 150-200 degrees. Remove the sugar from its packaging and place it in an ovenproof container that can hold the sugar. Put the sugar in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. After that, tap the sugar with a spoon. If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container and confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location. When it gets moist, it develops lumps.\"]", "time_sec": 35.861, "generation_time_seconds": 35.8578, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0005, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 79945, 13163, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 3118, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 48388, 30919, 24079, 6019, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 10771, 13876, 13163, 304, 264, 12188, 5476, 448, 264, 2613, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 476, 46399, 916, 279, 13163, 624, 256, 481, 10224, 264, 40269, 5567, 42613, 476, 25859, 7989, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 12188, 14, 98957, 624, 256, 481, 17757, 38969, 624, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 40269, 5567, 42613, 304, 264, 5625, 315, 2849, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 90723, 7757, 30919, 24079, 6019, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 279, 15457, 9315, 11, 220, 16, 20, 1