8, -0.0, -0.0135, -0.0001, -1.0192, -0.0963, -0.0004, -1.0643, -0.0026, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -2.1823, -0.0, -0.0058, -0.0008, -0.0663, -1.1422, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0154, -0.5857, -0.0381, 0.0, -0.0023, -0.0001, -4.1959, 0.0, -2.0659, -0.0567, -0.0101, -0.5447, -0.0247, -0.0, -0.2524, -0.001, -0.3586, -0.0028, -0.253, -0.0006, -0.9552, -2.2512, -0.1751, -0.0004, -0.2843, -0.0502, -0.2678, -0.1997, -0.043, -0.0, -0.2123, -0.0544, -0.0, -0.0077, -1.5146, -0.3499, -2.3973, -0.004, -0.4423, -0.0257, -0.0117, -0.0028, -0.0183, -0.2159, -0.2091, -1.1955, -0.1427, -0.0102, -0.0036, 0.0, -0.0005, -0.0013, -0.7915, -0.0067, -0.0233, -0.0, -4.3079, -0.0361, -0.0033, -0.0767, 0.0, 0.0, -0.7333, 0.0, -0.0056, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0301, -0.004, -0.0104, -0.0414, -0.0013, 0.0, -0.0143, -0.019, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0816, -0.0, -0.0004, 0.0, -0.5956, -0.0678, -0.055, 0.0, -1.2088, -0.1598, -0.0754, -0.0002, -0.0, -1.0537, -0.0049, -0.0001, -0.0029, -0.0, -0.1385, -1.5035, -1.6675, -0.2529, -0.0, -0.0, -9.3751, -0.1206, -0.9176, -0.1023], "cumulative_logprob": -95.0243, "norm_logp": -0.3299, "input_len": 499, "output_tokens": 288, "pred": "Chard is a leafy green vegetable with large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. It is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor. Chard is primarily used for its leaves, which can be consumed either fresh in salads or after cooking."}], "input_len": 499, "output_tokens": 558, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 15.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "214", "question": "how to wash wine glasses properly", "gt": "To properly wash wine glasses, you should scrub them by hand as it's the safest cleaning method. First, lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage. Use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. To clean the inside of a glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles. If hot water and mild detergent can’t get your glasses clean, use baking soda to remove any stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.", "pred": "To wash wine glasses properly, you can follow the steps mentioned in the passages. First, if hot water and mild detergent don't work, you can use baking soda. Dissolve a small amount of soda in hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass. Alternatively, you can use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel. It's important to clean the glasses by hand to avoid chips and spots. Lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water and wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage. Use a small amount of detergent and use it only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To wash wine glasses properly, you can follow the steps mentioned in the passages. First, if hot water and mild detergent don't work, you can use baking soda. Dissolve a small amount of soda in hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass. Alternatively, you can use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel. It's important to clean the glasses by hand to avoid chips and spots. Lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water and wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage. Use a small amount of detergent and use it only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.", "cot": "[\"To wash wine glasses properly, you can follow the steps mentioned in the passages. First, if hot water and mild detergent don't work, you can use baking soda. Dissolve a small amount of soda in hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass. Alternatively, you can use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel. It's important to clean the glasses by hand to avoid chips and spots. Lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water and wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage. Use a small amount of detergent and use it only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\", \"To wash wine glasses properly, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Hand Wash**: The safest method is to wash wine glasses by hand. Lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one glass at a time to avoid damage.\\n\\n2. **Use Detergent**: Use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed — in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. This helps prevent the soap from affecting the taste of your next glass of wine.\\n\\n3. **Protect the Stem**: Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\\n\\n4. **Additional Tips**: \\n   - If hot water and mild detergent don't work, use baking soda to remove stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water, let it stand in the glass for a few minutes, and the soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\\n   - For the inside of the glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles.\\n   - After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\\n   - Editor’s tip: Red wine can leave stains if left overnight.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can ensure that your wine glasses are thoroughly and safely cleaned without damaging them or affecting the taste of your wine.\", \"To wash wine glasses properly, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Prepare the sink: Lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. This helps protect the glasses from scratches.\\n\\n2. Wash the glasses by hand: Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage. Use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed, such as in the bottom of the glass and around the rim.\\n\\n3. Use a stemware brush: Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass.\\n\\n4. Rinsing: After washing, rinse the glasses thoroughly with hot water.\\n\\n5. Drying: Dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\\n\\n6. Prevent stains: Red wine can leave stains if left overnight, so ensure the glasses are dry before putting them away.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can ensure that your wine glasses are properly cleaned and protected from chips and stains.\", \"To properly wash wine glasses, you can use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles, or scrub them by hand. When scrubbing by hand, follow these tips: lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water, wash one glass at a time to avoid damage, use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed (in the bottom of the glass and around the rim), and cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem. If hot water and mild detergent can't get your glasses clean, use baking soda to remove any stubborn wine residue by dissolving a small amount of soda with hot water and letting it stand in the glass for a few minutes.\"]", "time_sec": 28.666, "generation_time_seconds": 28.6617, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0005, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 11369, 13078, 28147, 10277, 11, 498, 646, 1795, 279, 7354, 9733, 304, 279, 46769, 13, 5512, 11, 421, 4017, 3015, 323, 23034, 90134, 1513, 944, 975, 11, 498, 646, 990, 27815, 38862, 13, 51032, 3948, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 38862, 304, 4017, 3015, 323, 1077, 432, 2498, 304, 279, 8991, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 13, 576, 38862, 686, 72639, 894, 32147, 13078, 34951, 287, 311, 279, 8991, 13, 38478, 11, 498, 646, 990, 264, 19101, 1664, 15625, 448, 8413, 12, 824, 309, 1411, 65943, 311, 4240, 279, 4766, 315, 279, 8991, 13, 4636, 96039, 287, 26364, 448, 4017, 3015, 11, 9058, 279, 13078, 28147, 448, 264, 10876, 57920, 12577, 27292, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 8003, 82945, 476, 19828, 52333, 42613, 13, 1084, 594, 2989, 311, 4240, 279, 28147, 553, 1424, 311, 5648, 23595, 323, 18773, 13, 43924, 264, 42613, 304, 279, 19309, 1573, 21274, 448, 4017, 3015, 323, 11369, 825, 13078, 8991, 518, 264, 882, 311, 5648, 5557, 13, 5443, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 90134, 323, 990, 432, 1172, 1380, 432, 594, 4362, 1177, 304, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 8991, 323, 2163, 279, 30130, 13, 4553, 71355, 279, 19212, 315, 279, 8991, 304, 825, 1424, 139