, and cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem. If hot water and mild detergent can't get your glasses clean, use baking soda to remove any stubborn wine residue by dissolving a small amount of soda with hot water and letting it stand in the glass for a few minutes."}], "input_len": 404, "output_tokens": 832, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 85.71, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "227", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Here's a brief answer on how to fix a lift valve in a toilet based on the given passages:\n\nTo fix a lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\n\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n3. Install a new flapper valve and chain for a 1.6 gallon per flush toilet.\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n5. Adjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links if necessary. Cut off any excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\n6. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included, screw it in tightly.\n7. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened.\n8. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "Step 1: Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\nStep 2: Remove the old flapper valve.\nStep 3: Remove the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\nStep 4: Open the water valve to fill the tank.\nStep 5: Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\nStep 6: Adjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\nStep 7: When satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\nStep 8: Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\nStep 9: If a screw is included, screw it in tightly.\nStep 10: Push the lift arm until there is no more give and it is secure.\nStep 11: Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm.\nStep 12: Use pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\nStep 13: Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Step 1: Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\nStep 2: Remove the old flapper valve.\nStep 3: Remove the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\nStep 4: Open the water valve to fill the tank.\nStep 5: Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\nStep 6: Adjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\nStep 7: When satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\nStep 8: Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\nStep 9: If a screw is included, screw it in tightly.\nStep 10: Push the lift arm until there is no more give and it is secure.\nStep 11: Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm.\nStep 12: Use pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\nStep 13: Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.", "cot": "[\"Step 1: Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\\nStep 2: Remove the old flapper valve.\\nStep 3: Remove the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\nStep 4: Open the water valve to fill the tank.\\nStep 5: Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\\nStep 6: Adjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\\nStep 7: When satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\\nStep 8: Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\\nStep 9: If a screw is included, screw it in tightly.\\nStep 10: Push the lift arm until there is no more give and it is secure.\\nStep 11: Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm.\\nStep 12: Use pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\\nStep 13: Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\", \"To fix a lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Shut off the water supply valve**: Before starting the repair, turn off the water supply valve to the toilet to prevent water from flowing into the tank.\\n\\n2. **Remove the old flapper valve**: Carefully remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. This will allow access to the lift chain.\\n\\n3. **Handle the broken lift chain**: Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm. Make sure to remove all fragments to avoid any blockages or issues with the new chain.\\n\\n4. **Prepare the new lift chain**: Take the new lift chain and ensure it is free of any kinks or damage. Check that the chain is the correct length for your toilet model.\\n\\n5. **Install the new lift chain**: Attach one end of the new lift chain to the flush handle. If a screw is included with the new part, screw it in tightly to secure the chain to the flush handle. Make sure it is in the smallest hole to ensure the chain moves correctly.\\n\\n6. **Secure the chain to the lift arm**: Connect the other end of the lift chain to the lift arm. Push the chain through the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm, ensuring it is securely fastened. Use pliers to make sure the chain is tightly attached and won’t come loose.\\n\\n7. **Test the repair**: Turn the water supply valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm. This will ensure the chain moves smoothly and the flapper valve closes properly.\\n\\n8. **Check for correct operation**: Open the water valve to fill the tank and flush the toilet to check for correct operation. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links until the flush is smooth and efficient.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can successfully fix the lift valve in your toilet.\", \"To fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these detailed steps:\\n\\n1. **Turn off the water supply**: Begin by shutting off the water supply valve to the toilet. This prevents water from flowing into the tank during the repair process.\\n\\n2. **Remove the old flapper valve**: Carefully slip the old flapper valve off the mounting arms. Ensure you remove any remnants of the broken lift chain from the lift arm. This step is crucial to prevent any further damage or leakage.\\n\\n3. **Prepare the lift chain**: Open the water valve to refill the tank. Once the tank is full, flush the toilet to test for correct operation. If everything works as it should, proceed to adjust the lift chain. If there are issues, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links. This adjustment helps ensure the chain operates smoothly.\\n\\n4. **Cut off excess chain**: After adjusting the chain, cut off any excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled. This ensures a clean and efficient setup.\\n\\n5. **Install the new flapper valve**: Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included with your repair kit, tighten it securely. The other end of the lift arm should hang freely in the air. \\n\\n6. **Connect the chain**: Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge. Use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened. This step is essential to maintain the proper tension on the chain.\\n\\n7. **Test the flush**: Turn the water valve back on and test the flush of the toilet. If the flush is slow, adjust the chain to make it tighter on the lift arm. This ensures a smooth flush and prevents any leaks.\\n\\nFollowing these steps should effectively fix the lift valve in your toilet, ensuring it operates correctly and efficiently.\", \"To fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Shut off the water supply valve**: Locate the water supply valve near the toilet and turn it clockwise to shut off the water supply.\\n\\n2. **Remove the old flapper valve**: Carefully remove the old flapper valve by sliding it off the mounting arms. Be sure to remove any remaining pieces of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n\\n3. **Prepare the new flapper valve**: If a new flapper valve is being installed, ensure it is properly positioned and ready for installation.\\n\\n4. **Install the new flapper valve**: Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included, screw it in tightly. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure. The other end will hang freely in the air.\\n\\n5. **Connect the chain**: Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened.\\n\\n6. **Turn on the water supply**: Turn the water valve back on.\\n\\n7. **Test the flush**: Test the flush of the toilet to ensure it works correctly. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\\n\\n8. **Check for correct operation**: Open the water valve to fill the tank and flush the toilet to check for correct operation. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links until you are satisfied with the operation.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can effectively fix the lift valve in a toilet.\"]", "time_sec": 43.789, "generation_time_seconds": 43.7833, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0008, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 1417, 27440, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 311, 279, 26214, 624, 8304, 220, 17, 25, 10783, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 624, 8304, 220, 18, 25, 10783, 279, 10865, 11893, 8781, 504, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 8304, 220, 19, 25, 5264, 279, 3015, 31430, 311, 5155, 279, 12896, 624, 8304, 220, 20, 25, 57626, 279, 26214, 311, 1779, 369, 4396, 5666, 624, 8304, 220, 21, 25, 27196, 279, 11893, 8781, 553, 7218, 279, 9317, 12327, 705, 476, 1495, 264, 5625, 315, 7746, 624, 8304, 220, 22, 25, 3197, 19527, 11, 3931, 1007, 279, 13623, 11893, 87