{"id": "331", "question": "how to boil potatoes for easy peeling", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to boil potatoes for easy peeling:\n\n1. Bring a pot of water to a boil.\n2. Score your potatoes all the way around the center with a knife.\n3. Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so.\n4. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water.\n5. Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it’s cool enough to handle.\n6. Remove your potato from the water and remove the skin.\n\nThe ice water bath helps to stop the cooking process and cool down the potatoes quickly, making the skin easier to peel off.", "pred": "Boil potatoes in a pot of water for about 15 minutes, then remove them from the pot and immediately transfer them to a bowl of ice water. Once they are cool enough to handle, remove the skin.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Step 1: Bring a pot of water to a boil.\nStep 2: With a knife, score your potatoes all the way around the center.\nStep 3: Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so.\nStep 4: Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water.\nStep 5: Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it’s cool enough to handle.\nStep 6: Remove your potatoe from the water and remove the skin.\n\nAnswer: Boil potatoes in a pot of water for about 15 minutes, then remove them from the pot and immediately transfer them to a bowl of ice water. Once they are cool enough to handle, remove the skin.", "cot": "[\"Step 1: Bring a pot of water to a boil.\\nStep 2: With a knife, score your potatoes all the way around the center.\\nStep 3: Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so.\\nStep 4: Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water.\\nStep 5: Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it’s cool enough to handle.\\nStep 6: Remove your potatoe from the water and remove the skin.\\n\\nAnswer: Boil potatoes in a pot of water for about 15 minutes, then remove them from the pot and immediately transfer them to a bowl of ice water. Once they are cool enough to handle, remove the skin.\", \"Step 1: Bring a pot of water to a boil.\\nStep 2: With a knife, score your potatoes all the way around the center.\\nStep 3: Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so.\\nStep 4: Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water.\\nStep 5: Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it's cool enough to handle.\\nStep 6: Remove your potato from the water and remove the skin.\\n\\nAnswer: Boil the potatoes until they are tender, then transfer them to an ice water bath. When they are cool enough to handle, use a knife to peel off the skin.\", \"Boil potatoes until they are tender. Then, transfer them to an ice water bath. When they are cool enough to handle, peel off the skin.\", \"To boil potatoes for easy peeling, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Bring a pot of water to a boil.\\n2. Score your potatoes all the way around the center with a knife.\\n3. Place your potatoes in the pot and boil them for about 15 minutes.\\n4. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water.\\n5. Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it's cool enough to handle.\\n6. Remove your potatoes from the water and remove the skin.\\n\\nThese steps will make it easier to peel the potatoes.\"]", "time_sec": 20.886, "generation_time_seconds": 20.8811, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0003, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 39124, 264, 3338, 315, 3015, 311, 264, 43690, 624, 8304, 220, 17, 25, 3085, 264, 21430, 11, 5456, 697, 34167, 678, 279, 1616, 2163, 279, 4126, 624, 8304, 220, 18, 25, 10771, 697, 34167, 304, 279, 3338, 323, 43690, 369, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 476, 773, 624, 8304, 220, 19, 25, 31166, 264, 19212, 315, 9