.3212, -0.0112, -0.0085, -0.0024, -0.0, -0.0, -0.6021, -0.6061, -2.203, -0.0, -0.0, 0.0, -0.024, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.1082, -0.178, -0.001, -1.0547, -0.0001, -0.0024, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.1427, -0.2862, -0.1429, 0.0, -0.0055, -1.5027, -0.5458, -0.0055, -0.0134, -0.0, -0.3113, -0.066, -0.0003, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0004, -0.3362, -2.8017, -0.2011, -1.3633, -1.2099, -0.0539, -0.0171, -0.0, -0.0233, -0.3634, -0.6294, -0.0524, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.5065, -0.0, -0.383, -0.0], "cumulative_logprob": -55.753, "norm_logp": -0.1306, "input_len": 436, "output_tokens": 427, "pred": "[To make ribs, follow these steps: 1. Grill them by heating the grill to medium (350°F to 450°F), brushing with sauce, and cooking for 20 minutes with flipping every 5 minutes. 2. Oven-cook by removing the membrane, covering with BBQ sauce, lining with foil, and baking. 3. Season by brushing with a mustard and liquid smoke mixture, and sprinkling with dry rub.]"}], "input_len": 436, "output_tokens": 1420, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 30.85, "GAVIE-Rel": 4.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "354", "question": "what is company goodwill and why important", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, I can confidently answer the following questions:\n\nWhat is company goodwill?\nCompany goodwill refers to the positive image and reputation of a business that is built over time through providing quality products or services, satisfying customers, and building strong relationships with them. Goodwill is a valuable asset for any business as it helps to attract new customers, retain existing ones, and attract investors.\n\nWhy is goodwill important in business?\nGoodwill is important in business because it helps to build trust and loyalty among customers, which leads to long-term relationships and repeat business. A strong reputation and goodwill can also make a business more attractive to potential investors and buyers. Additionally, goodwill can help a business to stand out from its competitors and establish a unique identity in the marketplace.", "pred": "Company goodwill is the reputation and connection with customers, along with the circumstances that make this connection permanent. It represents the value of the attraction to customers that the name and reputation of the company possess. Goodwill is important in business because it can increase the customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Company goodwill is the reputation and connection with customers, along with the circumstances that make this connection permanent. It represents the value of the attraction to customers that the name and reputation of the company possess. Goodwill is important in business because it can increase the customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.", "cot": "[\"Company goodwill is the reputation and connection with customers, along with the circumstances that make this connection permanent. It represents the value of the attraction to customers that the name and reputation of the company possess. Goodwill is important in business because it can increase the customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.\", \"Company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection with customers that a business maintains over time. This goodwill can be built through providing good service or products, which leads to repeat customers and positive word-of-mouth referrals. Goodwill is important in business because it increases a company's customer base and retains old clients, attracting investors and future buyers. It represents the value of the attraction to customers that the name and reputation of the business possesses.\", \"Company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection a business has with its customers. It is the value that comes from the trust and loyalty customers have in the business, which can be seen through repeat business and positive word-of-mouth referrals. Goodwill is important in business because it can increase customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers. It represents the entire advantage of the reputation and connection with customers together with the circumstances whether of habit or otherwise, which tend to make that connection permanent.\", \"Step 1: Identify the definition of company goodwill.\\nFrom the passages, company goodwill is defined as the whole advantage of the reputation and connection with customers, together with circumstances that tend to make that connection permanent. It represents the value of the attraction to customers that the name and reputation possesses.\\n\\nStep 2: Identify the reasons why company goodwill is important.\\nThe passages state that good will will increase your customer base and retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.\\n\\nStep 3: Identify the examples of reasons why company goodwill is important.\\nThe passages give examples of how good service or product to customers creates a trust, which leads to repeat customers and word-of-mouth promotion, contributing to the company's goodwill.\\n\\nStep 4: Synthesize the information to answer the question.\\nCompany goodwill is the reputation and connection with customers, including the circumstances that make this connection permanent. It is important because it increases customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and attracts future buyers. This is supported by examples of good service or product leading to trust, repeat customers, and word-of-mouth promotion.\\n\\nAnswer: Company goodwill is the reputation and connection with customers, including the circumstances that make this connection permanent. It is important because it increases customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and attracts future buyers. This is supported by examples of good service or product leading to trust, repeat customers, and word-of-mouth promotion.\"]", "time_sec": 23.799, "generation_time_seconds": 23.7933, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0003, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [14491, 81646, 374, 279, 17011, 323, 3633, 448, 6310, 11, 3156, 448, 279, 13161, 429, 1281, 419, 3633, 15330, 13, 1084, 10868, 279, 897, 315, 279, 32364, 311, 6310, 429, 279, 829, 323, 17011, 315, 279, 2813, 15218, 13, 7684, 14387, 374, 2989, 304, 2562, 1576, 432, 646, 5263, 279, 6002, 2331, 11, 14060, 2310, 8239, 11, 9320, 14823, 11, 323, 9320, 3853, 22630, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.4083, -0.0003, -1.671, -0.0313, -0.2109, -0.0104, -0.0058, -0.1058, -0.0003, -0.8676, -1.4515, 0.0, -0.535, -0.0013, -0.0973, -0.598, -0.205, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0104, -0.0164, -0.3789, -0.0001, -0.0433, -0.0003, -0.0115, -0.0006, -0.0057, -0.6931, -0.2398, -0.0354, -0.0763, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.0475, -0.0789, -0.8027, -1.0591, -0.1464, -0.0719, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.002, -0.6038, -0.0, -0.0134, -0.0, -1.2704, -0.00