{"id": "403", "question": "2006 chevy remove door panel", "gt": "To remove the rear door panel in a 2006 Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup and the one in the middle of the inside door handle. You will also need to remove a pin on the outer edge of the door. Once these are removed, you can use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.", "pred": "To remove the rear door panel in a Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup, the one in the middle of the inside door handle, and the pin on the outer edge of the door. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the panel off, remove all screws and clips in the door panel, gently pull the panel away from the frame, and remove any wiring connections.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Step 1: Identify the relevant information from the passages.\nThe passages provide instructions on how to remove the rear door panel in a Chevy HHR.\n\nStep 2: Extract the specific details mentioned in the passages.\n- Remove two screws located inside the door pull cup.\n- Remove one screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\n- Remove a pin on the outer edge of the door.\n- Use a door panel removal tool to pry the panel off.\n- Remove all screws and clips in the door panel.\n- Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\n- Remove any wiring connections.\n\nStep 3: Determine if the information provided is sufficient to answer the question.\nThe passages do not explicitly mention a 2006 Chevy HHR, but they do provide general instructions for removing the rear door panel in a Chevy HHR.\n\nStep 4: Formulate the answer based on the available information.\nAnswer: To remove the rear door panel in a Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup, the one in the middle of the inside door handle, and the pin on the outer edge of the door. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the panel off, remove all screws and clips in the door panel, gently pull the panel away from the frame, and remove any wiring connections.", "cot": "[\"Step 1: Identify the relevant information from the passages.\\nThe passages provide instructions on how to remove the rear door panel in a Chevy HHR.\\n\\nStep 2: Extract the specific details mentioned in the passages.\\n- Remove two screws located inside the door pull cup.\\n- Remove one screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\\n- Remove a pin on the outer edge of the door.\\n- Use a door panel removal tool to pry the panel off.\\n- Remove all screws and clips in the door panel.\\n- Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\\n- Remove any wiring connections.\\n\\nStep 3: Determine if the information provided is sufficient to answer the question.\\nThe passages do not explicitly mention a 2006 Chevy HHR, but they do provide general instructions for removing the rear door panel in a Chevy HHR.\\n\\nStep 4: Formulate the answer based on the available information.\\nAnswer: To remove the rear door panel in a Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup, the one in the middle of the inside door handle, and the pin on the outer edge of the door. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the panel off, remove all screws and clips in the door panel, gently pull the panel away from the frame, and remove any wiring connections.\", \"To remove the rear door panel in your 2006 Chevy, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup.\\n2. Remove the screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\\n3. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.\\n5. Remove all screws and clips in the door panel.\\n6. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\\n7. Remove any wiring connections.\\n\\nAnswer: To remove the door panel, you need to remove two screws inside the door pull cup, one screw in the middle of the inside door handle, and a pin on the outer edge of the door. Then, use a door panel removal tool to pry the panel off, remove all screws and clips, and gently pull it away from the frame, removing any wiring connections.\", \"To remove the rear door panel in your Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup, and there's also one in the middle of the inside door handle. On the outer edge of the door there's also a pin the holds the panel in place, you will need to remove that. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door. An instructional video has also been enclosed below that shows this entire process and where everything's located.\", \"To remove the rear door panel in your Chevy HHR, you will need to remove two screws located inside the door pull cup, one in the middle of the inside door handle, and a pin that holds the panel in place on the outer edge of the door. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door. Remove all screws and clips in the door panel and gently pull the panel away from the frame. Remove any wiring connections, and the panel will come off the frame.\\n\\nAnswer: To remove the rear door panel in your Chevy HHR, you will need to remove two screws located inside the door pull cup, one in the middle of the inside door handle, and a pin that holds the panel in place on the outer edge of the door. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door. Remove all screws and clips in the door panel and gently pull the panel away from the frame. Remove any wiring connections, and the panel will come off the frame.\"]", "time_sec": 30.483, "generation_time_seconds": 30.4792, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0002, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 