{"id": "722", "question": "how to poach an egg using a poachpod", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to poach an egg using a PoachPod®:\n\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\n2. Crack an egg into the silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the yolk.\n3. Gently slide the pod into the boiling water, making sure it stays upright and no water gets in.\n4. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for 6 minutes.\n5. Use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the pod out of the hot water.\n6. Flip the pod upside down over a plate and press the bottom to release the poached egg.\n\nSo, to summarize, the steps to poach an egg using a PoachPod® are:\n\n1. Bring water to a boil.\n2. Crack egg into pod.\n3. Float pod in boiling water.\n4. Cook for 6 minutes.\n5. Remove pod from water.\n6. Release egg onto plate.", "pred": "To poach an egg using a PoachPod®:", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Step 1: Identify the key steps for poaching an egg using a PoachPod® from the provided passages.\n- Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\n- Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the yolk.\n- Float the poaching pod in the boiling water, ensuring the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod.\n- Cover the pot with the lid and let the egg cook for six minutes.\n- Remove the lid and use a slotted spoon or tongs to lift the pod out of the hot water.\n- Flip the pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.\n\nStep 2: Check if additional information is needed from general knowledge or if the provided passages contain all necessary details.\n- The passages contain all the necessary details to poach an egg using a PoachPod®.\n\nAnswer: To poach an egg using a PoachPod®:\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\n2. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the yolk.\n3. Float the poaching pod in the boiling water, ensuring the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod.\n4. Cover the pot with the lid and let the egg cook for six minutes.\n5. Remove the lid and use a slotted spoon or tongs to lift the pod out of the hot water.\n6. Flip the pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.", "cot": "[\"Step 1: Identify the key steps for poaching an egg using a PoachPod® from the provided passages.\\n- Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\\n- Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the yolk.\\n- Float the poaching pod in the boiling water, ensuring the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod.\\n- Cover the pot with the lid and let the egg cook for six minutes.\\n- Remove the lid and use a slotted spoon or tongs to lift the pod out of the hot water.\\n- Flip the pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.\\n\\nStep 2: Check if additional information is needed from general knowledge or if the provided passages contain all necessary details.\\n- The passages contain all the necessary details to poach an egg using a PoachPod®.\\n\\nAnswer: To poach an egg using a PoachPod®:\\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\\n2. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the yolk.\\n3. Float the poaching pod in the boiling water, ensuring the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod.\\n4. Cover the pot with the lid and let the egg cook for six minutes.\\n5. Remove the lid and use a slotted spoon or tongs to lift the pod out of the hot water.\\n6. Flip the pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.\", \"Step 1: Identify the key steps in poaching an egg using a PoachPod®.\\n- Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\\n- Crack an egg and gently slide the egg into your silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the egg's yolk.\\n- Carefully float the poaching pod in the boiling water, making sure the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod.\\n- Cover the pot with the lid and let the egg cook for six minutes.\\n- Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\\n- Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release your poached egg onto the plate.\\n\\nFinal Answer: To poach an egg using a PoachPod®, bring a large pot of water to a boil. Crack an egg and gently slide the egg into your silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the egg's yolk. Carefully float the poaching pod in the boiling water, making sure the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod. Cover the pot with the lid and let the egg cook for six minutes. Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the hot water. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release your poached egg onto the plate.\", \"To poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Prepare the Pod**: Lightly oil the pod to prevent the egg from sticking to it.\\n\\n2. **Crack the Egg**: Crack an egg into the oiled Pod.\\n\\n3. **Float the Pod in Water**: Carefully float the Pod in a saucepan of simmering water. Make sure the Pod stays upright and no water gets into the Pod.\\n\\n4. **Cook the Egg**: Cover the saucepan with a tight-fitting lid and let the egg cook for about 4-6 minutes.\\n\\n5. **Remove the Pod**: Use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the Pod out of the hot water.\\n\\n6. **Release the Egg**: Flip the Pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.\\n\\nThis method ensures that the egg is poached perfectly, with the yolk remaining intact and the egg white set.\", \"To poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Fill a large pot with water and bring it to a boil.\\n2. Crack an egg into the PoachPod, being careful not to break the yolk.\\n3. Gently float the PoachPod in the boiling water, ensuring it stays upright and no water gets into the pod.\\n4. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for 4-6 minutes.\\n5. Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the PoachPod out of the hot water.\\n6. Flip the PoachPod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.\\n\\nThis method allows you to poach an egg in boiling water, similar to how a lily pad floats on a pond.\"]", "time_sec": 41.579, "generation_time_seconds": 41.5676, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0008, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 1376, 7354, 369, 3193, 11829, 458, 18636, 1667, 264, 13808, 610, 23527, 11909, 504, 279, 3897, 46769, 624, 12, 39124, 264, 3460, 3338, 315, 3015, 311, 264, 43690, 624, 12, 54945, 458, 18636, 323, 29273, 14983, 432, 1119, 279, 52925, 3193, 11829, 7509, 11, 1660, 16585, 537, 311, 1438, 279, 379, 22604, 624, 12, 13001, 279, 3193, 11829, 7509, 304, 279, 49837, 3015, 11, 22573, 279, 7509, 26558, 48585, 323, 902, 3015, 5221, 1119, 279, 7509, 624, 12, 17757, 279, 3338, 448, 279, 26334, 323, 1077, 279, 18636, 4296, 369, 4743, 4420, 624, 12, 10783, 279, 26334, 323, 990, 264, 1739, 15521, 45505, 476, 259, 13181, 311, 11893, 279, 7509, 700, 315, 279, 4017, 3015, 624, 12, 40284, 279, 7509, 35841, 1495, 916, 264, 11968, 323, 29273, 3493, 389, 279, 5622, 311, 4879, 279, 3193, 3854, 18636, 8630, 279, 11968, 382, 8304, 220, 17, 25, 4248, 421, 5107, 1995, 374, 4362, 504, 4586, 6540, 476, 421, 279, 3897, 46769, 6644, 678, 5871, 3565, 624, 12, 576, 46769, 6644, 678, 279, 5871, 3565, 311, 3193, 610, 458, 18636, 1667, 264, 13808, 610, 23527, 11909, 382, 16141, 25, 2014, 3193, 610, 458, 18636, 1667, 264, 138