{"id": "16", "question": "wat is dna", "gt": "Based on the given passages, DNA (deoxyribonucleic acid) is a nucleic acid that contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. It is a double helix formed by base pairs attached to a sugar-phosphate backbone, with the base pairs forming the ladder's rungs and the sugar and phosphate molecules forming the vertical sidepieces of the ladder. The order of the nitrogen bases in a DNA sequence forms genes, which provide the instructions for making proteins.", "pred": "DNA, or deoxyribonucleic acid, is a nucleic acid that contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. DNA is made up of molecules called nucleotides, each containing a phosphate group, a sugar group, and a nitrogen base. The four types of nitrogen bases are adenine (A), thymine (T), guanine (G), and cytosine (C). The order of these bases determines the genetic code, which tells cells how to make proteins. DNA has a double helix structure, with base pairs forming the rungs and sugar-phosphate molecules forming the vertical sidepieces of the ladder. DNA's main role is the long-term storage of information.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "DNA, or deoxyribonucleic acid, is a nucleic acid that contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. DNA is made up of molecules called nucleotides, each containing a phosphate group, a sugar group, and a nitrogen base. The four types of nitrogen bases are adenine (A), thymine (T), guanine (G), and cytosine (C). The order of these bases determines the genetic code, which tells cells how to make proteins. DNA has a double helix structure, with base pairs forming the rungs and sugar-phosphate molecules forming the vertical sidepieces of the ladder. DNA's main role is the long-term storage of information.", "cot": "[\"DNA, or deoxyribonucleic acid, is a nucleic acid that contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. DNA is made up of molecules called nucleotides, each containing a phosphate group, a sugar group, and a nitrogen base. The four types of nitrogen bases are adenine (A), thymine (T), guanine (G), and cytosine (C). The order of these bases determines the genetic code, which tells cells how to make proteins. DNA has a double helix structure, with base pairs forming the rungs and sugar-phosphate molecules forming the vertical sidepieces of the ladder. DNA's main role is the long-term storage of information.\", \"DNA, or deoxyribonucleic acid, is a double helix formed by base pairs attached to a sugar-phosphate backbone. It contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. Each nucleotide in DNA contains a phosphate group, a sugar group, and a nitrogen base. The four types of nitrogen bases are adenine (A), thymine (T), guanine (G), and cytosine (C). The order of these bases determines DNA’s instructions, or genetic code, which tells cells how to make proteins. DNA's structure is somewhat like a ladder, with the base pairs forming the ladder's rungs and the sugar and phosphate molecules forming the vertical sidepieces of the ladder. An important property of DNA is that it can replicate, or make copies of itself.\", \"DNA (Deoxyribonucleic acid) is a nucleic acid that contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. The main role of DNA molecules is the long-term storage of information. DNA is made up of molecules called nucleotides, each containing a phosphate group, a sugar group, and a nitrogen base. The four types of nitrogen bases are adenine (A), thymine (T), guanine (G), and cytosine (C). The order of these bases determines the genetic code, which tells cells how to make proteins.\\n\\nAnswer: DNA is a nucleic acid that stores genetic information for the development and functioning of living organisms. It is composed of nucleotides with phosphate, sugar, and nitrogen base groups, and the sequence of these bases determines the genetic code.\", \"DNA, or deoxyribonucleic acid, is a nucleic acid that contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. It is composed of molecules called nucleotides, which consist of a phosphate group, a sugar group, and a nitrogen base. The four types of nitrogen bases are adenine (A), thymine (T), guanine (G), and cytosine (C). The sequence of these bases determines the genetic code, which tells cells how to make proteins. DNA is a double helix structure, with base pairs forming the rungs and the sugar and phosphate molecules forming the vertical sidepieces of the ladder. It is the hereditary material in humans and almost all other organisms, and it can replicate, or make copies of itself.\"]", "time_sec": 26.961, "generation_time_seconds": 26.9199, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0013, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [55320, 11, 476, 409, 60163, 1897, 263, 22147, 292, 13621, 11, 374, 264, 30384, 292, 13621, 429, 5610, 279, 18929, 11221, 1483, 304, 279, 4401, 323, 30201, 315, 678, 3881, 5382, 43204, 323, 1045, 40968, 13, 15552, 374, 1865, 705, 315, 34615, 2598, 30384, 354, 3341, 11, 1817, 8482, 264, 78006, 1874, 11, 264, 13163, 1874, 11, 323, 264, 46403, 2331, 13, 576, 3040, 4494, 315, 46403, 23092, 525, 99113, 482, 320, 32, 701, 270, 1600, 482, 320, 51, 701, 1675, 91256, 320, 38, 701, 323, 9503, 42581, 482, 320, 34, 568, 576, 1973, 315, 1493, 23092, 26569, 279, 18929, 2038, 11, 892, 10742, 7761, 1246, 311, 1281, 27796, 13, 15552, 702, 264, 1990, 11338, 941, 5944, 11, 448, 2331, 13530, 29064, 279