essary to consult a professional locksmith for more detailed assistance."}], "input_len": 587, "output_tokens": 1226, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 24.15, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "38", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to cook pollock:\n\nPreheat the oven to 350°F (175°C). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Place the fillets on a baking sheet lined with parchment paper or aluminum foil. You can also add sliced onions, green peppers, and tomatoes on top of the fillets. Bake for 15 minutes or until the fish flakes easily with a fork. If desired, top with cheese and return to the oven for an additional 3 minutes or until the cheese is melted.\n\nTherefore, the answer is not \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"", "pred": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C), season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they are cooked and flake easily, approximately 15 minutes, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, return the fillets to the oven, and allow the cheese to melt, for about 3 minutes.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "The passage describes the steps to cook pollock:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they are cooked and flake easily, approximately 15 minutes.\n4. Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n5. Return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, for about 3 minutes.\n\nBased on the information provided, the final answer is:\n\nAnswer: Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C), season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they are cooked and flake easily, approximately 15 minutes, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, return the fillets to the oven, and allow the cheese to melt, for about 3 minutes.", "cot": "[\"The passage describes the steps to cook pollock:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they are cooked and flake easily, approximately 15 minutes.\\n4. Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n5. Return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, for about 3 minutes.\\n\\nBased on the information provided, the final answer is:\\n\\nAnswer: Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C), season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they are cooked and flake easily, approximately 15 minutes, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, return the fillets to the oven, and allow the cheese to melt, for about 3 minutes.\", \"Step 1: Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\nStep 2: Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\nStep 3: Place the seasoned pollock fillets on a baking sheet and layer with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\\nStep 4: Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\\nStep 5: Turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\nStep 6: Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.\\n\\nAnswer: To cook pollock, preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C), season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, place the fillets on a baking sheet with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices, bake in the preheated oven until the fish is cooked and flakes easily (about 15 minutes), turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fish to the oven until the cheese melts (about 3 minutes).\", \"To cook pollock, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit (175 degrees Celsius).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Place the seasoned pollock fillets on a baking sheet.\\n4. Layer the fillets with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\\n5. Bake the pollock in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, which should take about 15 minutes.\\n\\nAnswer: Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit, season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, place the fillets on a baking sheet layered with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices, and bake until the fish is cooked and flakes easily.\", \"1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Place the seasoned fillets on a baking sheet.\\n4. Layer the fillets with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\\n5. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes.\\n6. Remove the fillets from the oven and turn off the oven.\\n7. Place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n8. Return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, about 3 minutes.\\n\\nAnswer:[Bake in preheated oven until fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes. Turn oven off, place two slices of cheese on each fillet. Return fish to the oven and allow cheese to melt, about 3 minutes.]\"]", "time_sec": 28.011, "generation_time_seconds": 28.0065, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0003, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 21085, 16555, 279, 7354, 311, 4296, 1471, 1023, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 624, 18, 13, 52074, 279, 1461, 9942, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 807, 525, 29105, 323, 1320, 726, 6707, 11, 13187, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 19, 13, 11999, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 1992, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 624, 20, 13, 3411, 279, 1461, 9942, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28