{"id": "215", "question": "how to wash wine glasses properly", "gt": "To wash wine glasses properly, start by using hot water and mild detergent to clean the outside of the glass. If there are stubborn wine residues, use baking soda to dissolve them by mixing a small amount of soda with hot water and letting it sit in the glass for a few minutes. For cleaning the inside of the glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles. Rinse thoroughly with hot water and dry the glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth. To avoid damage, wash one wine glass at a time, use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed, and cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.", "pred": "By following these steps, you can ensure that your wine glasses are properly cleaned and maintained.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Based on the provided passages, here are the steps to properly wash wine glasses:\n\n1. **Use Baking Soda for Stubborn Residue**: If hot water and mild detergent don't clean the glass, use baking soda. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\n\n2. **Use a Stemware Brush**: To clean the inside of a glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles. This ensures that the glass is thoroughly cleaned.\n\n3. **Rinse with Hot Water**: After scrubbing the glass with the brush, rinse it thoroughly with hot water.\n\n4. **Dry the Glass**: Dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel. This helps to avoid leaving streaks or residue on the glass.\n\n5. **Wash by Hand**: The safest cleaning method for wine glasses is to scrub them by hand. Follow these tips to avoid chips and spots:\n   - Lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water.\n   - Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage.\n   - Use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed – in the bottom of the glass and around the rim.\n   - Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\n\nBy following these steps, you can ensure that your wine glasses are properly cleaned and maintained.", "cot": "[\"Based on the provided passages, here are the steps to properly wash wine glasses:\\n\\n1. **Use Baking Soda for Stubborn Residue**: If hot water and mild detergent don't clean the glass, use baking soda. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\\n\\n2. **Use a Stemware Brush**: To clean the inside of a glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles. This ensures that the glass is thoroughly cleaned.\\n\\n3. **Rinse with Hot Water**: After scrubbing the glass with the brush, rinse it thoroughly with hot water.\\n\\n4. **Dry the Glass**: Dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel. This helps to avoid leaving streaks or residue on the glass.\\n\\n5. **Wash by Hand**: The safest cleaning method for wine glasses is to scrub them by hand. Follow these tips to avoid chips and spots:\\n   - Lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water.\\n   - Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage.\\n   - Use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed – in the bottom of the glass and around the rim.\\n   - Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can ensure that your wine glasses are properly cleaned and maintained.\", \"Step 1: Identify the methods and steps mentioned in the passages for washing wine glasses.\\n\\nFrom Passage 1:\\n- Use baking soda to remove stubborn wine residue.\\n- Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes.\\n- The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\\n\\nFrom Passage 2:\\n- Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles.\\n- Rinse thoroughly with hot water.\\n- Dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\\n\\nFrom Passage 3:\\n- Scrub by hand is the safest method.\\n- Lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water.\\n- Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage.\\n- Use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed – in the bottom of the glass and around the rim.\\n- Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\\n\\nStep 2: Combine the information from all passages to form a comprehensive answer on how to wash wine glasses properly.\\n\\nTo wash wine glasses properly, follow these steps:\\n1. Prepare your workspace by laying a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water.\\n2. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage.\\n3. Use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed – in the bottom of the glass and around the rim.\\n4. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\\n5. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to scrub the glass.\\n6. Rinse the glass thoroughly with hot water.\\n7. Dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\\n8. If there is stubborn wine residue, use baking soda to remove it. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\\n\\nAnswer: To wash wine glasses properly, prepare your workspace by laying a towel in the sink, wash one glass at a time to avoid damage, use a small amount of detergent only where needed, cradle the bowl in one hand while washing, scrub with a stemware brush, rinse thoroughly with hot water, dry with a lint-free cloth, and use baking soda for stubborn residue.\", \"To wash wine glasses properly, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Use hot water and mild detergent to clean the glasses. If hot water and mild detergent can't get your glasses clean, use baking soda to remove any stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\\n\\n2. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass.\\n\\n3. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\\n\\n4. Clean your wine glasses by hand for the safest method. Lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage. Use a small amount of detergent and use it only where it's needed – in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\", \"To wash wine glasses properly, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass. This helps remove any stubborn wine residue effectively.\\n\\n2. After rinsing the glass thoroughly with hot water, dry it using a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel. This ensures that the glass is completely dry, preventing any water spots or streaks.\\n\\n3. For the safest cleaning method, scrub the wine glasses by hand. Lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid any damage to the glasses.\\n\\n4. To prevent the soap from affecting the taste of your next glass of wine, use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed, such as in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\\n\\n5. If hot water and mild detergent don't clean the glasses properly, you can use baking soda to remove any stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water, let it stand in the glass for a few minutes, and the soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can ensure that your wine glasses are thoroughly cleaned and ready for use.\"]", "time_sec": 47.213, "generation_time_seconds": 47.1983, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0006, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 1588, 525, 279, 7354, 311, 10277, 11369, 13078, 28147, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 10253, 425, 1765, 96072, 369, 66611, 15998, 1800, 60607, 95518, 1416, 4017, 3015, 323, 23034, 90134, 1513, 944, 4240, 279, 8991, 11, 990, 27815, 38862, 13, 51032, 3948, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 38862, 448, 4017, 3015, 323, 1077, 432, 2498, 304, 279, 8991, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 13, 576, 38862, 686, 72639, 894, 32147, 13078, 34951, 287, 311, 279, 8991, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 10253, 264, 80848, 1664, 32988, 95518, 2014, 4240, 279, 4766, 315, 264, 8991, 11, 990, 264, 19101, 1664, 15625, 448, 8413, 12, 824, 309, 1411, 65943, 13, 1096, 25351, 429, 279, 8991, 374, 26364, 27722, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 49, 258, 325, 448, 8007, 9959, 95518, 4636, 44901, 7132, 279, 8991, 448, 279, 15625, 11, 73241, 432, 26364, 448, 4017, 3015, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 85215, 279, 20734, 95518, 30841, 279, 13078, 28147, 448, 264, 10876, 57920, 12577, 27292, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 8003, 82945, 476, 19828, 52333, 42613, 13, 1096, 8609, 311, 5648, 9380, 29214, 82, 476, 48132, 389, 279, 8991, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 54, 988, 553, 8536, 95518, 576, 61744, 15826, 1714, 369, 13078, 28147, 374, 311, 44901, 1105, 553, 1424, 13, 11112, 1493, 10414, 311, 5648, 23595, 323, 18773, 510, 256, 481, 43924, 264, 42613, 304, 279, 19309, 1573, 21274, 432, 448, 4017, 3015, 624, 256, 481, 5985, 825, 13078, 8991, 518, 264, 882, 311, 5648, 5557, 624, 256, 481, 5443, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 90134, 1172, 1380, 432, 594, 4362, 1365, 304, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 8991, 323, 2163, 279, 30130, 624, 256, 481, 4553, 71355, 279, 19212, 315, 279, 8991, 304, 825, 1424, 1393, 27686, 311, 6