{"id": "271", "question": "earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy", "gt": "The earliest signs of pregnancy often include mood swings and unusual emotional behavior due to a flood of hormones in the body. Dizziness can also occur as pregnancy causes blood vessels to dilate and blood pressure to drop. Other early symptoms can include a missed period, bloating, spotting, and cramping. Approximately half of all pregnant women experience nausea and vomiting, and around 3 in 10 women experience nausea without vomiting, with these symptoms typically starting around six weeks after their last period.", "pred": "The earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy include mood swings, dizziness, a missed period, bloating, spotting, cramping, and nausea and vomiting.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Step 1: Identify the earliest signs of pregnancy from the provided passages.\nStep 2: Determine the symptoms mentioned that occur in the first weeks of pregnancy.\nStep 3: Compare the information from the passages to common knowledge about pregnancy symptoms.\n\nThe earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy, as mentioned in the passages, include:\n1. Mood swings due to hormonal changes in the body.\n2. Dizziness caused by blood vessel dilation and a drop in blood pressure.\n3. A missed period, which is often not the earliest sign but can be one of the symptoms.\n4. Bloating, spotting, and cramping, which are other common symptoms.\n5. Nausea and vomiting, which can start around six weeks after the last period.\n\nAnswer: The earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy include mood swings, dizziness, a missed period, bloating, spotting, cramping, and nausea and vomiting.", "cot": "[\"Step 1: Identify the earliest signs of pregnancy from the provided passages.\\nStep 2: Determine the symptoms mentioned that occur in the first weeks of pregnancy.\\nStep 3: Compare the information from the passages to common knowledge about pregnancy symptoms.\\n\\nThe earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy, as mentioned in the passages, include:\\n1. Mood swings due to hormonal changes in the body.\\n2. Dizziness caused by blood vessel dilation and a drop in blood pressure.\\n3. A missed period, which is often not the earliest sign but can be one of the symptoms.\\n4. Bloating, spotting, and cramping, which are other common symptoms.\\n5. Nausea and vomiting, which can start around six weeks after the last period.\\n\\nAnswer: The earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy include mood swings, dizziness, a missed period, bloating, spotting, cramping, and nausea and vomiting.\", \"The earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy, as mentioned in the provided passages, can include:\\n\\n1. Missed period: This is a common indicator that a woman may be pregnant.\\n2. Bloating: Many women experience an increase in abdominal size and discomfort.\\n3. Spotting: Light bleeding or spotting can occur, which may be mistaken for a light period.\\n4. Cramping: Similar to menstrual cramps, pregnancy-induced cramping can occur.\\n5. Mood swings: Hormonal changes during pregnancy can lead to mood swings and emotional fluctuations.\\n6. Dizziness: Pregnancy can cause a drop in blood pressure, leading to feelings of dizziness or lightheadedness.\\n7. Nausea and vomiting: Approximately half of pregnant women experience nausea, and about 3 in 10 experience nausea without vomiting.\\n8. Morning sickness: For most women, symptoms of morning sickness typically start around six weeks after their last period.\\n\\nAnswer: The earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy include a missed period, bloating, spotting, cramping, mood swings, dizziness, nausea and vomiting, and morning sickness.\", \"Step 1: Identify the earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy mentioned in the passages.\\n\\nFrom Passage 1:\\n- Mood swings\\n- Dizziness\\n\\nFrom Passage 2:\\n- Missed period\\n- Bloating\\n- Spotting\\n- Cramping\\n\\nFrom Passage 3:\\n- Nausea and vomiting\\n- Nausea without vomiting\\n\\nStep 2: Compare and combine the symptoms to provide a comprehensive list.\\n\\nThe earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy mentioned in the passages include:\\n- Mood swings\\n- Dizziness\\n- Missed period\\n- Bloating\\n- Spotting\\n- Cramping\\n- Nausea and vomiting\\n- Nausea without vomiting\\n\\nAnswer: The earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy, as mentioned in the passages, include mood swings, dizziness, missed period, bloating, spotting, cramping, nausea and vomiting, and nausea without vomiting.\", \"Step 1: Identify the earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy mentioned in the passages.\\n\\nPassage 1 does not mention any specific earliest signs or symptoms of pregnancy.\\n\\nPassage 2 mentions:\\n- A missed period\\n- Bloating\\n- Spotting\\n- Cramping\\n\\nPassage 3 mentions:\\n- Nausea and vomiting\\n- Nausea without vomiting\\n\\nStep 2: Compare the symptoms mentioned in both passages.\\n\\nPassage 2 lists symptoms that are mentioned in Passage 3 as well. Both passages also mention that these symptoms can occur around the same time frame, typically in the first weeks of pregnancy.\\n\\nStep 3: Combine the information from both passages to form a comprehensive answer.\\n\\nThe earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy, as mentioned in the provided passages, include:\\n- A missed period\\n- Bloating\\n- Spotting\\n- Cramping\\n- Nausea and vomiting\\n- Nausea without vomiting\\n\\nAnswer: The earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy, as mentioned in the provided passages, include a missed period, bloating, spotting, cramping, nausea and vomiting, and nausea without vomiting.\"]", "time_sec": 32.687, "generation_time_seconds": 32.6825, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0003, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 29658, 11929, 315, 19636, 504, 279, 3897, 46769, 624, 8304, 220, 17, 25, 29901, 279, 13495, 9733, 429, 12170, 304, 279, 1156