{"id": "287", "question": "how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven", "gt": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, preheat the oven to 325 degrees F. Place the frozen roast in a roasting pan and rub the surface with olive oil and season with salt, pepper, and desired seasonings. Place the roast, uncovered, in the preheated oven. Cook for about 20-30 minutes per pound or until the internal temperature reaches 150 degrees F. Once cooked, cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "pred": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit, place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat facing upwards, cook for about 20-30 minutes per pound, insert a meat thermometer to check the internal temperature, and let it rest for 30 minutes before serving.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit.\n2. Put the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards.\n3. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound.\n4. Insert a meat thermometer and test the meat after cooking.\n5. When the internal temperature of the meat reaches 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven.\n6. Cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.\n\nAnswer: Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit, place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat facing upwards, cook for about 20-30 minutes per pound, insert a meat thermometer to check the internal temperature, and let it rest for 30 minutes before serving.", "cot": "[\"To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit.\\n2. Put the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards.\\n3. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound.\\n4. Insert a meat thermometer and test the meat after cooking.\\n5. When the internal temperature of the meat reaches 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven.\\n6. Cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.\\n\\nAnswer: Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit, place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat facing upwards, cook for about 20-30 minutes per pound, insert a meat thermometer to check the internal temperature, and let it rest for 30 minutes before serving.\", \"First, preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer, and test the meat after cooking. When the internal temperature of the meat is 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil, and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.\", \"To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, start by preheating the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer and test the meat after cooking. When the internal temperature of the meat reaches 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.\\n\\nAnswer:[To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit, place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards, cook for about 20-30 minutes per pound, insert a meat thermometer, and test the meat after cooking. When the internal temperature of the meat reaches 150 degrees Fahrenheit, cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.]\", \"To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat your oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit.\\n2. Place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards.\\n3. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound.\\n4. Insert a meat thermometer and test the meat after cooking.\\n5. When the internal temperature of the meat is 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven.\\n6. Cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.\\n\\nAnswer: Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit, place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat facing upwards, cook for 20-30 minutes per pound, insert a meat thermometer, test the meat after cooking, and cover with aluminum foil for 30 minutes before serving.\"]", "time_sec": 32.661, "generation_time_seconds": 32.655, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0003, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 264, 19690, 35067, 76960, 57685, 304, 279, 23387, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 624, 17, 13, 10224, 279, 19690, 35067, 76960, 304, 264, 25600, 27815, 7215, 389, 1909, 315, 264, 926, 14725, 29659, 448, 279, 8664, 315, 279, 35067, 76960, 12880, 43954, 624, 18, 13, 12514, 279, 35067, 76960, 369, 911, 220, 17, 15, 12, 18, 15, 4420, 817, 30023, 624, 19, 13, 17101, 264, 13041, 92197, 323, 1273, 279, 13041, 1283, 17233, 624, 20, 13, 3197, 279, 5306, 9315, 315, 279, 13041, 24491, 220, 16, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 11, 279, 13041, 374, 5527, 311, 387, 4429, 700, 315, 279, 23387, 624, 21, 13, 17757, 279, 57