{"id": "298", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "gt": "To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is needed. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot, ensuring hot water is always available. Alternatively, recirculating pumps can be used to rapidly pull hot water from a water heater, while simultaneously sending cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused. These systems can be controlled by the push of a button, a timer, or a motion sensor. However, it should be noted that heat loss from the pipes can occur, requiring the water heater to use more fuel.", "pred": "To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. This pump sends cool water from the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. It circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available. Additionally, demand systems can be controlled by the push of a button, a timer, or motion sensor.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Answer: To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. This pump sends cool water from the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. It circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available. Additionally, demand systems can be controlled by the push of a button, a timer, or motion sensor.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. This pump sends cool water from the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. It circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available. Additionally, demand systems can be controlled by the push of a button, a timer, or motion sensor.\", \"Based on the provided passages, the hot water heater circulates through the use of a hot water circulation pump. This pump sends cool water from the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available. The pump helps to keep the water in the system hot by circulating it back and forth between the pipes and the water heater.\", \"To make a hot water heater circulate, a pump is used. This pump, known as a hot water circulation pump, sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. A pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.\", \"In order to make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot, ensuring that hot water is always available. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.\"]", "time_sec": 14.36, "generation_time_seconds": 14.3553, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0001, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 2014, 1281, 264, 4017, 3015, 42238, 4225, 6334, 11, 264, 4017, 3015, 34755, 13834, 374, 1483, 13, 1096, 13834, 21308, 7010, 3015, 504, 279, 31175, 1182, 311, 279, 3015, 42238, 1526, 264, 470, 1555, 13, 1084, 4225, 23156, 419, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 438, 4362, 311, 2506, 432, 4017, 13, 1096, 19259, 6337, 315, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 25351, 429, 4017, 3015, 374, 