{"id": "356", "question": "what is company goodwill and why important", "gt": "Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the positive feelings and loyalty of customers towards a business, gained through providing good services or products, building trust, and creating a strong reputation. Goodwill is important because it can increase customer retention, attract new customers, and make the business more attractive to investors and potential buyers.\n\nAccording to passage 3, goodwill is an intangible asset that represents the value of a business's reputation and customer connections, which can make the connection between the business and its customers permanent.\n\nTherefore, goodwill is important for businesses because it can lead to increased customer loyalty, positive word-of-mouth advertising, and higher sales, ultimately contributing to the long-term success and growth of the business.", "pred": "Step 5: Formulate the answer - Company goodwill is the reputation and connection with customers that tend to make that connection permanent. It represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses. Goodwill is important in business because it increases customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and future buyers.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Step 1: Analyze the question - The question asks for the definition of company goodwill and its importance.\n\nStep 2: Identify relevant information from the passages - The passages provide information on why goodwill is important in business. \n\nStep 3: Extract specific information - The passages mention that goodwill will increase customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and future buyers.\n\nStep 4: Synthesize the information - Company goodwill refers to the reputation and connection with customers that tend to make that connection permanent. It represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses.\n\nStep 5: Formulate the answer - Company goodwill is the reputation and connection with customers that tend to make that connection permanent. It represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses. Goodwill is important in business because it increases customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and future buyers.", "cot": "[\"Step 1: Analyze the question - The question asks for the definition of company goodwill and its importance.\\n\\nStep 2: Identify relevant information from the passages - The passages provide information on why goodwill is important in business. \\n\\nStep 3: Extract specific information - The passages mention that goodwill will increase customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and future buyers.\\n\\nStep 4: Synthesize the information - Company goodwill refers to the reputation and connection with customers that tend to make that connection permanent. It represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses.\\n\\nStep 5: Formulate the answer - Company goodwill is the reputation and connection with customers that tend to make that connection permanent. It represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses. Goodwill is important in business because it increases customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and future buyers.\", \"Goodwill is the reputation and connection with customers that a company has built up over time. This reputation can be a valuable asset for a company because it helps to retain customers and attract new ones. Goodwill can also make it easier for a company to attract investors and future buyers. It is important because it can increase a company's customer base and retain old clients, attract investors and attract future buyers.\", \"Company goodwill refers to the reputation and connection with customers that makes the connection permanent. Goodwill is important because it increases the customer base, retains old clients, and attracts investors and future buyers. It is also a business asset that represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses.\", \"Company goodwill refers to the reputation and connection with customers that makes the connection permanent. It represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses. Goodwill is important in business because it can increase the customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.\"]", "time_sec": 17.704, "generation_time_seconds": 17.7004, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0003, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 37427, 2986, 279, 3405, 481, 576, 3405, 17064, 369, 279, 7271, 315, 2813, 81646, 323, 1181, 12650, 382, 8304, 220, 17, 25, 64547, 9760, 1995, 504, 279, 46769, 481, 576, 46769, 3410, 1995, 389, 3170, 81646, 374, 2989, 304, 2562, 13, 4710, 8304, 220, 18, 25, 22826, 3151, 1995, 481, 576, 46769, 6286, 429, 81646, 686, 5263, 6002, 2331, 11, 14060, 2310, 8239, 11, 9320, 14823, 11, 323, 3853, 22630, 382, 8304, 220, 19, 25, 23153, 26887, 279, 1995, 481, 8188, 81646, 19257, 311, 279, 17011, 323, 3633, 448, 6310, 429, 8376, 311, 1281, 429, 3633, 15330, 13, 1084, 10868, 279, 897, 315, 279, 32364, 311, 279, 6310, 892, 279, 829, 323, 17011, 49226, 382, 8304, 220, 20, 25, 3377, 6334, 279, 4226, 481, 8188, 81646, 374, 279, 17011, 323, 3633, 448, 6310, 429, 8376, 311, 1281, 429, 3633, 15330, 13, 1084, 10868, 279, 897, 315, 279, 32364, 311, 279, 6310, 892, 279, 829, 323, 17011, 49226, 13, 7684, 14387, 374, 2989, 304, 2562, 1576, 432, 12703, 6002, 2331, 11, 51844, 2310, 8239, 11, 60091, 14823, 11, 323, 3853, 22630, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.6583, -0.0002, 0.0, -0.0, -2.1846, -0.0155, -0.0007, -1.09, -2.9471, -0.0506, -0.0003, -0.0789, -