{"id": "491", "question": "how can you tell who liked your tweet", "gt": "You can tell who liked your tweet by using websites such as Favotter.net and Favstar.fm, or by going to Twitter.com and logging in with your Twitter username and password. Once logged in, click on your Twitter name, located on the upper right hand corner of your account's Home page, then click on Settings and finally Blue Notifications link at the top of the screen. By setting this feature, you will receive an email notification whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.", "pred": "To determine who liked your tweet, you can use tools such as Favotter.net or Favstar.fm. These websites allow you to track which tweets you and others have favorited. Additionally, you can set up notifications in your Twitter account to be emailed whenever someone marks one of your tweets as a favorite. However, if you are very popular, you may receive a lot of email notifications.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To determine who liked your tweet, you can use tools such as Favotter.net or Favstar.fm. These websites allow you to track which tweets you and others have favorited. Additionally, you can set up notifications in your Twitter account to be emailed whenever someone marks one of your tweets as a favorite. However, if you are very popular, you may receive a lot of email notifications.", "cot": "[\"To determine who liked your tweet, you can use tools such as Favotter.net or Favstar.fm. These websites allow you to track which tweets you and others have favorited. Additionally, you can set up notifications in your Twitter account to be emailed whenever someone marks one of your tweets as a favorite. However, if you are very popular, you may receive a lot of email notifications.\", \"To determine who liked your tweet, you can use websites like Favotter.net and Favstar.fm to track which tweets you and others are favoriting. These sites provide a list of users who have favorited specific tweets, allowing you to identify other Twitter users who might be interested in your content.\", \"There are a few ways to find out who liked your tweet. One way is to use a website that tracks who favors your tweets. Another way is to check your Twitter settings to see if you're notified via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as a favorite. It's important to note that if you're very popular on Twitter, you may receive a lot of email notifications.\", \"To tell who liked your tweet, you can use websites such as Favotter.net and Favstar.fm. These websites allow you to see who is favoriting your tweets and which tweets that you and others are also favoriting. Additionally, you can set up notifications on Twitter itself by logging in, clicking on your name, selecting the Settings option, and then clicking on the blue Notifications link. This will notify you via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as a favorite.\"]", "time_sec": 16.482, "generation_time_seconds": 16.4737, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0004, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 8253, 879, 14915, 697, 11809, 11, 498, 646, 990, 7375, 1741, 438, 80941, 354, 465, 5071, 476, 80941, 11870, 70485, 13, 4220, 13037, 2138, 498, 311, 3754, 892, 23150, 498, 323, 3800, 614, 4694, 1608, 13, 22406, 11, 498, 646, 738, 705, 21969, 304, 697, 6271, 2692, 311, 387, 48514, 15356, 4325, 15423, 825, 315, 697, 23150, 438, 264, 6930, 13, 4354, 11, 421, 498, 525, 1602, 5411, 11, 498, 1231, 5258, 264, 2696, 315, 2551, 21969, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.2433, -1.1506, -0.0019, -0.0004, -0.0135, -0.0057, -0.0023, -0.0256, -0.0021, -0.0725, -3.5043, -1.0627, 0.0, -0.002, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0, -0.5069, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0237, -0.0049, -0.0997, -0.0148, -0.0024, 0.0, -0.0343, -0.9627, -0.0178, -0.4836, -0.0104, -0.2281, -0.7104, -0.0042, 0.0, -0.8032, -0.7639, -0.0, -0.1611, -0.0001, -0.256, -0.0