logp_list": [-0.8153, -0.0, -0.6095, -0.0155, -0.0245, -0.0057, -0.6575, -1.4199, -3.4829, -0.0021, -0.0197, -0.8534, -0.5246, -2.5173, -0.2514, -0.0802, -0.0476, -2.7091, -1.0167, -0.0029, -1.154, -1.3611, -0.0011, -0.0015, -0.0673, -0.0093, -0.1314, -0.0056, -0.5244, -0.6133, -0.0003, -0.1545, -0.0, -1.223, -0.2794, -0.0014, -0.19, -0.2209, -0.0001, -0.0024, -0.0, -0.0335, -0.2017, -0.1625, -0.0445, -0.2513, -0.5791, -2.5389, -0.035, -0.0017, -0.9662, -0.0003, -0.0086, -0.2966, -0.0068, -1.2034, -0.0, -0.0507, -3.4002, -0.0002, -0.0, -2.1482, -0.8489, -6.4848, -0.013, -0.0001, -0.6029, -1.3651, -0.0194, -0.1348, -0.0591, -0.0351, -0.0026, -0.079, -0.0009, 0.0, -0.0003, -0.0656, -0.2231, -0.3244, -0.0517, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.043, -0.0002, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0244, -1.2168], "cumulative_logprob": -44.5215, "norm_logp": -0.4947, "input_len": 429, "output_tokens": 90, "pred": "Raffles work by selling tickets to a group of people. The group then draws a single winning ticket at the end of the event. The winner of the raffle is the person who holds the winning ticket. The prize money is usually determined by the amount of money collected from ticket sales. For example, if a ticket costs $50 and 100 tickets are sold, the prize money would be $5,000."}], "input_len": 429, "output_tokens": 1009, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 18.84, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "534", "question": "what are safety pins in a first aid box used for", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, safety pins in a first aid box are used for the following purposes:\n\n1. Immobilizing an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to create a makeshift arm sling (Passage 2).\n2. Securing a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg (Passage 2).\n3. Helping to keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances (Passage 2).\n4. Removing splinters (Passage 3).\n\nThe passages mention these specific uses for safety pins in a first aid context, but do not provide any additional information regarding their use in a survival kit.", "pred": "Safety pins are used in a first aid box for immobilizing an arm, securing bandanas over wounds, keeping severe wounds closed, and removing splinters.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Step 1: Understand the context\nThe question asks about the uses of safety pins in a first aid box.\n\nStep 2: Analyze the passages\nPassage 2 specifically discusses safety pins and their uses in first aid. It mentions the following uses:\n- Immobilizing an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling.\n- Securing a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg.\n- Helping to keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances.\n- Removing splinters in the wilderness.\n\nStep 3: Summarize the findings\nBased on the information provided in the passages, safety pins can be used in first aid for immobilizing an arm, securing bandanas over wounds, keeping severe wounds closed, and removing splinters.\n\nFinal answer: Safety pins are used in a first aid box for immobilizing an arm, securing bandanas over wounds, keeping severe wounds closed, and removing splinters.", "cot": "[\"Step 1: Understand the context\\nThe question asks about the uses of safety pins in a first aid box.\\n\\nStep 2: Analyze the passages\\nPassage 2 specifically discusses safety pins and their uses in first aid. It mentions the following uses:\\n- Immobilizing an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling.\\n- Securing a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg.\\n- Helping to keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances.\\n- Removing splinters in the wilderness.\\n\\nStep 3: Summarize the findings\\nBased on the information provided in the passages, safety pins can be used in first aid for immobilizing an arm, securing bandanas over wounds, keeping severe wounds closed, and removing splinters.\\n\\nFinal answer: Safety pins are used in a first aid box for immobilizing an arm, securing bandanas over wounds, keeping severe wounds closed, and removing splinters.\", \"Safety pins are used in a first aid box for various purposes. According to the passage, they can be used to immobilize an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling. They can secure a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg, and they can even be used to help keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances. Additionally, the passage mentions that safety pins can be used to remove splinters in the wilderness.\", \"Step 1: Identify relevant information in the passages.\\nThe passage mentions the uses of safety pins in first aid situations. It provides examples such as immobilizing an arm, securing a bandana over a wounded arm or leg, and keeping a severe wound closed in place of stitches. It also mentions removing splinters using safety pins.\\n\\nStep 2: Synthesize the information.\\nSafety pins in a first aid box are used for immobilizing an arm, securing a bandana over a wounded arm or leg, keeping a severe wound closed in place of stitches, and removing splinters.\\n\\nStep 3: Formulate the answer.\\nSafety pins in a first aid box are used for immobilizing an arm, securing a bandana over a wounded arm or leg, keeping a severe wound closed in place of stitches, and removing splinters.\\n\\nAnswer: Safety pins in a first aid box are used for immobilizing an arm, securing a bandana over a wounded arm or leg, keeping a severe wound closed in place of stitches, and removing splinters.\", \"Safety pins are used in a first aid box for various purposes. According to the passage, they can be used to immobilize an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling. They can also be used to secure a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg. Additionally, they can be used to help keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances.\"]", "time_sec": 23.589, "generation_time_seconds": 23.5832, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0004, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 70894, 279, 2266, 198, 785, 3405, 17064, 911, 279, 5711, 315, 7149, 26944, 304, 264, 1156, 12296, 3745, 382, 8304, 220, 17, 25, 37427, 2986, 279, 46769, 198, 12187, 424, 220, 17, 11689, 34334, 7149, 26944, 323, 862, 5711, 304, 1156, 12296, 13, 1084, 33845, 279, 2701, 5711, 510, 12, 15335, 27929, 4849, 458, 6773, 553, 8983, 1229, 279, 74423, 315, 264, 1293, 36153, 15478, 311, 1181, 15138, 311, 11153, 264, 86080, 6773, 87633, 624, 12, 4520, 1677, 264, 7055, 3362, 916, 264, 27493, 323, 34663, 6773, 476, 2472, 624, 12, 90701, 311, 2506, 264, 15386, 26555, 7877, 304, 1992, 315, 61936, 304, 13207, 13161, 624, 12, 66703, 12503, 49940, 304, 279, 48262, 382, 8304, 220, 18, 25, 8116, 5612, 551, 279, 14613, 198, 28715, 389, 279, 1995, 3897, 304, 279, 46769, 11, 7149, 26944, 646, 387, 1483, 304, 1156, 12296, 369, 76341, 4849, 458, 6773, 11, 40477, 7055, 25908, 916, 33154, 11, 10282, 15386, 33154, 7877, 11, 323, 17592, 12503, 49940, 382, 19357, 4226, 25, 18702, 26944, 525, 1483, 304, 264, 1156, 12296, 3745, 369, 76341, 4849, 458, 6773, 11, 4