{"id": "737", "question": "what is the difference between sms and mms", "gt": "Based on the given passages, SMS stands for Short Message Service and allows you to send a message of up to 160 characters to another device. In contrast, MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows you to send a message including pictures, videos, sounds, text, or any combination of the four. The content of an MMS message has a maximum size of 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, GIF, etc.", "pred": "The difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS is a text messaging service that allows you to send and receive text messages, while MMS is a multimedia messaging service that allows you to send and receive messages including pictures, sounds, videos, and text.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "The difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS is a text messaging service that allows you to send and receive text messages, while MMS is a multimedia messaging service that allows you to send and receive messages including pictures, sounds, videos, and text.", "cot": "[\"The difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS is a text messaging service that allows you to send and receive text messages, while MMS is a multimedia messaging service that allows you to send and receive messages including pictures, sounds, videos, and text.\", \"The difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS only allows you to send text, while MMS allows you to send pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of the four. Additionally, MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, GIF, etc.\", \"SMS stands for Short Message Service and is also commonly referred to as a text message. It allows you to send a message of up to 160 characters to another device. Longer messages will automatically be split up into several parts. Most cell phones support this type of text messaging.\\n\\nMMS stands for Multimedia Messaging Service and is an evolution of SMS. It allows you to send a message including pictures, video, or audio content to another device. MMS is most commonly used to send a photo taken with a camera phone to another phone.\", \"The difference between SMS and MMS lies in the types of content they can transmit. SMS, or Short Message Service, is limited to sending text messages. In contrast, MMS, or Multimedia Messaging Service, can transmit a variety of content including pictures, sounds, videos, and text. MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, Gif, etc.\"]", "time_sec": 17.039, "generation_time_seconds": 17.0281, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0011, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 29909, 323, 386, 4826, 374, 429, 29909, 374, 264, 1467, 29522, 2473, 429, 6147, 498, 311, 3624, 323, 5258, 1467, 6605, 11, 1393, 386, 4826, 374, 264, 56513, 29522, 2473, 429, 6147, 498, 311, 3624, 323, 5258, 6605, 2670, 9185, 11, 10362, 11, 6803, 11, 323, 1467, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.2306, -0.1153, -0.0, -0.0, -0.2091, 0.0, 0.0, -0.6058, -0.0099, -0.0011, -2.469, -1.1198, -0.8544, -1.7236, -0.0002, -0.0271, -0.0429, -0.5358, -0.0, -0.0, -3.8855, -0.0, -0.0242, -0.1791, -0.4311, -0.0107, -0.0, 0.0, -0.1225, -0.0964, -0.011, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0019, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.002, -0.0, -0.6583, -2.9014, -0.1302, -0.0, -0.1948, -0.0, -0.0537, -0.0, -0.1282, -0.0051, -0.005, -0.2489], "cumulative_logprob": -18.0347, "norm_logp": -0.3468, "input_len": 547, "output_tokens": 52, "pred": "The difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS is a text messaging service that allows you to send and receive text messages, while MMS is a multimedia messaging service that allows you to send and receive messages including pictures, sounds, videos, and text."}, {"rollout": 1, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 29909, 323, 386, 4826, 374, 429, 29909, 1172, 6147, 498, 311, 3624, 1467, 11, 1393, 386, 4826, 6147,