{"id": "31", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how to fix a door that won't lock:\n\n1. Check the door stop: According to passage 2, if the door won't lock, try tapping the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Then, place the door stop back on the jamb, setting it back 1/4 inch from its original location. This should allow the door to shut and lock normally.\n2. Adjust the latch hole: If the latch doesn't align with the hole in the strike plate, you may need to enlarge the latch hole in the jamb, as suggested in passage 3. Before doing so, tighten the hinges first. Additionally, you may need to enlarge the strike plate hole and move the strike plate.\n\nIf the passages do not provide sufficient information to answer the question, the response would be: \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"", "pred": "To fix a door that won't lock, you should first close the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb, and pry up on it until it comes loose. Remove the door stop using the chisel. Next, set the door stop back on the jamb, aligning it with a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off, and nail it back in place. If the door latch won't catch, you may have to enlarge the latch hole in the jamb and tighten the hinges first. Enlarge the strike plate hole and move the strike plate to ensure proper alignment. If the latch still doesn't catch, make sure all the door's hinge screws are tight.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To fix a door that won't lock, you should first close the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb, and pry up on it until it comes loose. Remove the door stop using the chisel. Next, set the door stop back on the jamb, aligning it with a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off, and nail it back in place. If the door latch won't catch, you may have to enlarge the latch hole in the jamb and tighten the hinges first. Enlarge the strike plate hole and move the strike plate to ensure proper alignment. If the latch still doesn't catch, make sure all the door's hinge screws are tight.", "cot": "[\"To fix a door that won't lock, you should first close the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb, and pry up on it until it comes loose. Remove the door stop using the chisel. Next, set the door stop back on the jamb, aligning it with a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off, and nail it back in place. If the door latch won't catch, you may have to enlarge the latch hole in the jamb and tighten the hinges first. Enlarge the strike plate hole and move the strike plate to ensure proper alignment. If the latch still doesn't catch, make sure all the door's hinge screws are tight.\", \"Step 1: Identify the problem - The door is not locking properly.\\nStep 2: Look for potential causes - The passage mentions that the door latch may not align with the hole in the strike plate.\\nStep 3: Check for solutions - The passage provides a solution for this issue by suggesting to move the strike plate.\\nStep 4: Verify if the solution is valid - The passage provides clear instructions on how to move the strike plate, ensuring it aligns properly with the latch hole.\\nStep 5: Conclude - Based on the information provided in the passage, the solution to fix a door that won't lock is to move the strike plate to ensure it aligns properly with the latch hole.\\n\\nAnswer: Move the strike plate to ensure it aligns properly with the latch hole.\", \"To fix a door that won't lock, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Close the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\\n\\n2. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\\n\\n3. Lace the door stop back on the jamb. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\\n\\n4. If the door latch won't catch, it could be because the latch doesn't align with the hole in the strike plate. Tighten the hinges first and then enlarge the strike plate hole. Move the strike plate.\\n\\n5. To ensure proper alignment, you can use the \\\"lipstick test.\\\" If the latch contacts the strike plate too high or too low, make sure all the door's hinge screws are tight.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you should be able to fix a door that won't lock.\", \"To fix a door that won't lock, first try to lock the door. If it won't lock, open the door and tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Lace the door stop back on the jamb. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.\"]", "time_sec": 26.73, "generation_time_seconds": 26.7247, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0004, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 498, 1265, 1156, 3265, 279, 6006, 323, 1430, 311, 5296, 432, 13, 1416, 432, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 11, 15239, 279, 835, 315, 264, 521,