{"id": "58", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to keep birds from building nests on your porch:\n\n1. Attach bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch using a staple gun. This will prevent birds from reaching those spaces they often choose to build their nests, which can block your ventilation systems, are made from flammable materials, and bird droppings can transmit disease. (Passage 1:4)\n2. Install bird netting over the top of your light fixture to block the birds' access to it. Choose a netting that is non-flammable and safe to use around light bulbs, and make sure it is installed so that it doesn't entangle birds. (Passage 2:1)\n3. Mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch. The sight of a predator can scare the birds away from the area and keep them from inhabiting your porch. Move the plastic hawk periodically to keep the birds from becoming accustomed to its presence. (Passage 3:1)\n\nTherefore, based on the provided passages, you can keep birds from building nests on your porch by using bird netting, installing bird netting over your light fixture, or mounting a plastic hawk near your porch.", "pred": "Attach bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun. Install bird netting over the top of the light fixture to block the birds' access to it. Mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Attach bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun. Install bird netting over the top of the light fixture to block the birds' access to it. Mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch.", "cot": "[\"Attach bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun. Install bird netting over the top of the light fixture to block the birds' access to it. Mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch.\", \"Based on the provided passages, here are the methods to keep birds from building a nest on your porch:\\n\\n1. **Attach bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun**: This method involves covering the eaves with nonflammable bird netting. The netting should be securely attached to prevent birds from accessing the nesting spots. This is particularly useful if your porch has open rafters.\\n\\n2. **Install bird netting over the top of the light fixture**: This involves covering the light fixture with bird netting to prevent birds from accessing the area. Ensure the netting is installed carefully to avoid entangling birds.\\n\\n3. **Mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch**: A plastic hawk can act as a predator to scare birds away. This method is effective but requires periodic movement of the plastic hawk to keep the birds from getting accustomed to it.\\n\\nThese methods are specifically mentioned in the passages and are designed to prevent birds from nesting on your porch.\", \"To keep birds from building a nest on your porch, you can use various methods:\\n\\n1. **Attach Bird Netting**: Install bird netting around the perimeter of your porch using a staple gun. This netting should be attached to the eves and, if your porch has open rafters, to the top of the porch as well. The netting will prevent birds from accessing those spaces where they often choose to build their nests. This is effective because bird nests can block your ventilation systems, are made from flammable materials, and bird droppings can transmit disease.\\n\\n2. **Install Bird Netting over the Light Fixture**: Place bird netting over the top of the light fixture to block the birds' access to it. Ensure the netting is non-flammable and safe to use around light bulbs. Be cautious not to entangle birds in the netting.\\n\\n3. **Use a Plastic Hawk**: Mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch. The sight of a predator can scare the birds away and prevent them from nesting on your porch. To keep the birds from becoming accustomed to the plastic hawk, move it periodically.\\n\\nBy using these methods, you can effectively deter birds from nesting on your porch and protect your property from potential hazards associated with bird nests.\", \"To keep birds from building a nest on your porch, you can attach bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun. If your porch has open rafters, use the staple gun to attach the netting to the top of the porch. The netting keeps the birds from reaching those spaces they often choose to build their nests. Another method is to install bird netting over the top of the light fixture to block the birds' access to it. Choose a netting that is nonflammable and safe to use around light bulbs. Beware that the netting is installed so that it doesn't entangle birds. If you can't use netting on your light fixture, try placing a plastic hawk on or near your porch. The sight of a predator can scare the birds from the area and keep them from inhabiting your porch.\\n\\nAnswer: Attach bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun. If your porch has open rafters, use the staple gun to attach the netting to the top of the porch. Install bird netting over the top of the light fixture to block the birds' access to it. Choose a netting that is nonflammable and safe to use around light bulbs. Beware that the netting is installed so that it doesn't entangle birds. Place a plastic hawk on or near your porch. The sight of a predator can scare the birds from the area and keep them from inhabiting your porch.\"]", "time_sec": 27.993, "generation_time_seconds": 27.9893, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0004, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [30485, 11958, 4179, 1280, 311, 279, 384, 2342, 2163, 279, 46342, 315, 697, 44647, 448, 264, 48956, 6038, 13, 19242, 11958, 4179, 1280, 916, 279, 1909, 315, 27