{"id": "112", "question": "what is the difference between the leeward and windward islands?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the main difference between the Windward Islands and the Leeward Islands is their exposure to the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies). The Windward Islands are exposed to the wind and are therefore wetter and receive more rainfall, while the Leeward Islands are away from the wind and are drier, but still receive some rainfall. Additionally, the Windward Islands are located southeast of the Caribbean Sea, while the Leeward Islands are located northwest of the Caribbean Sea.", "pred": "The difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Windward Islands are closer to the ocean and experience more rain due to being exposed to the wind, while the Leeward Islands are farther from the ocean and receive less rain but still get some precipitation.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "The difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Windward Islands are closer to the ocean and experience more rain due to being exposed to the wind, while the Leeward Islands are farther from the ocean and receive less rain but still get some precipitation.", "cot": "[\"The difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Windward Islands are closer to the ocean and experience more rain due to being exposed to the wind, while the Leeward Islands are farther from the ocean and receive less rain but still get some precipitation.\", \"The difference between the leeward and windward islands, based on the provided passages, is that the windward islands are exposed to the wind (\\\"windward\\\") of the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies) and get more rain, making them wetter. In contrast, the leeward islands are away from the wind (\\\"lee\\\") and are drier but still receive rain.\", \"The Windward Islands are exposed to the wind, resulting in more rain and being wetter, while the Leeward Islands are away from the wind, making them drier but still receiving some rain. Specifically, the Windward Islands include Martinique, and the Leeward Islands are the northwestern islands of the Lesser Antilles.\", \"The differences between the Leeward and Windward Islands, as detailed in the passages, are as follows:\\n\\n1. **Exposure to Wind**: The Windward Islands are exposed to the wind, specifically the northeast trade winds, while the Leeward Islands are away from the wind. This means the Windward Islands are more directly in the path of the trade winds, whereas the Leeward Islands are not.\\n\\n2. **Rainfall**: The Windward Islands receive more rain due to their exposure to the wind. This is because the wind brings moisture-laden air that condenses and falls as rain. The Leeward Islands, being away from the wind, receive less rainfall.\\n\\n3. **Terrain Impact**: The terrain can also play a role. The Windward side of a mountain is typically wetter because it receives more rainfall due to the wind. Conversely, the Leeward side of a mountain is drier because it is farther from the ocean and thus receives less moisture.\\n\\n4. **Location**: The Windward Islands are southeastern islands of the Caribbean, while the Leeward Islands are northwestern islands of the Lesser Antilles.\\n\\nThese factors combined explain why the Windward Islands are wetter and receive more rainfall than the Leeward Islands.\"]", "time_sec": 17.071, "generation_time_seconds": 17.0677, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0003, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 279, 1967, 24035, 323, 22087, 1606, 22235, 374, 429, 279, 22087, 1606, 22235, 525, 12128, 311, 279, 17951, 323, 3139, 803, 11174, 4152, 311, 1660, 14900, 311, 279, 9956, 11, 1393, 279, 1967, 24035, 22235, 525, 42626, 504, 279, 17951, 323, 5258, 2686, 11174, 714, 2058, 633, 1045, 59950, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.3421, -0.4338, -0.0, 