{"id": "132", "question": "how to roast individual garlic cloves", "gt": "Preheat your oven to 400°F (205° C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, but keep the skins of the individual cloves intact. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves to expose them. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves. Season the garlic cloves to taste with herbs and spices if you like. Roasting time is dependent on the size of the cloves and may take up to 45 minutes or an hour for larger cloves. Once roasted, the garlic cloves can be stored in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.", "pred": "By following these steps, you can successfully roast individual garlic cloves and enhance their flavor with various seasonings.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Preheat the Oven**: Set your oven to 400°F (205°C).\n\n2. **Prepare the Garlic**: Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, but leave the skins of the individual cloves intact. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of each clove to expose the individual cloves of garlic.\n\n3. **Arrange on a Pan**: Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. If you don't have a baking pan, a muffin pan is also suitable as it prevents the garlic bulbs from rolling around.\n\n4. **Oil the Garlic**: Drizzle a couple of teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed garlic head. Use your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\n\n5. **Roast in the Oven**: Bake the garlic in the preheated oven for the appropriate amount of time based on the size of the cloves. Large cloves may take up to 45 minutes or even an hour to soften. Smaller cloves will roast faster, typically in about 20-30 minutes.\n\n6. **Store the Roasted Garlic**: Once roasted, allow the garlic to cool. Store the roasted garlic cloves in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.\n\n7. **Season the Garlic**: If desired, season the roasted garlic cloves with herbs and spices to taste. Choices include cayenne or chipotle pepper powder, Cajun seasoning mix, curry powder, dried oregano, marjoram, thyme, rosemary, tarragon, or basil. Choose seasonings that complement the food you are using the roasted garlic with.\n\nBy following these steps, you can successfully roast individual garlic cloves and enhance their flavor with various seasonings.", "cot": "[\"To roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Preheat the Oven**: Set your oven to 400°F (205°C).\\n\\n2. **Prepare the Garlic**: Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, but leave the skins of the individual cloves intact. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of each clove to expose the individual cloves of garlic.\\n\\n3. **Arrange on a Pan**: Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. If you don't have a baking pan, a muffin pan is also suitable as it prevents the garlic bulbs from rolling around.\\n\\n4. **Oil the Garlic**: Drizzle a couple of teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed garlic head. Use your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\\n\\n5. **Roast in the Oven**: Bake the garlic in the preheated oven for the appropriate amount of time based on the size of the cloves. Large cloves may take up to 45 minutes or even an hour to soften. Smaller cloves will roast faster, typically in about 20-30 minutes.\\n\\n6. **Store the Roasted Garlic**: Once roasted, allow the garlic to cool. Store the roasted garlic cloves in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.\\n\\n7. **Season the Garlic**: If desired, season the roasted garlic cloves with herbs and spices to taste. Choices include cayenne or chipotle pepper powder, Cajun seasoning mix, curry powder, dried oregano, marjoram, thyme, rosemary, tarragon, or basil. Choose seasonings that complement the food you are using the roasted garlic with.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can successfully roast individual garlic cloves and enhance their flavor with various seasonings.\", \"To roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up.\\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\\n\\nAnswer: Roasting individual garlic cloves involves preheating the oven to 400°F, peeling the garlic, cutting the top of the cloves, placing them in a baking pan, and drizzling olive oil over them before roasting.\", \"1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205° C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves.\\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves.\\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. (A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.)\\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\", \"To roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. (A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.)\\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\\n\\nAfter preparing the garlic cloves, roast them in the preheated oven until they are soft and tender, which may take up to 45 minutes or even an hour depending on their size.\"]", "time_sec": 30.562, "generation_time_seconds": 30.558, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0004, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 57685, 3842, 30635, 84288, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 4703, 19963, 279, 86113, 95518, 2573, 697, 23387, 311, 220, 19, 15, 15, 58472, 320, 17, 15, 20, 30937, 3593, 17, 13, 3070, 50590, 279, 94725, 95518, 88594, 323, 37867, 279, 25298, 722, 15955, 13617, 315, 279, 4361, 30635, 45812, 11, 714, 5274, 279, 49950, 315, 279, 3842, 84288, 34439, 13, 12091, 264, 17232, 21430, 11, 3931, 220, 16, 14, 19, 311, 220, 16, 14, 17, 17122, 504, 279, 1909, 315, 1817, 5292, 586, 311, 28141, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 79235, 389, 264, 10990, 95518, 10771, 279, 30635, 14629, 304, 264, 27815, 7215, 11, 3931, 3108, 705, 13, 1416, 498, 1513, 944, 614, 264, 27815, 7215, 11, 264, 54304, 258, 7215, 374, 1083, 14452, 438, 432, 27934, 279, 30635, 53220, 504, 20097, 2163, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 76909, 279, 94725, 95518, 2926, 43137, 264, 5625, 315, 92100, 315, 32113, 5590, 916, 1817, 14900, 30635, 1968, 13, 5443, 697, 19225, 311, 10273, 279, 32113, 5590, 916, 678, 279, 3931, 11, 14900, 30635, 84288, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 38872, 559, 304, 279, 86113, 95518, 52074, 279, 30635, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 369, 279, 8311, 3311, 315, 882, 3118, 389, 279, 1379, 315, 279, 84288, 13, 20286, 84288, 1231, 1896, 705, 311, 220, 19, 20, 4420, 476, 1496, 458, 6460, 