0.0, -0.3284, -0.144, -0.1067, -0.4733, -0.0256, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0003, -1.6696], "cumulative_logprob": -27.655, "norm_logp": -0.1948, "input_len": 499, "output_tokens": 142, "pred": "Chard is a type of leafy green vegetable that is related to beets. It has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive, and some think, bitter flavor. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked, like in pizzoccheri, or sauteed. Their bitterness fades with cooking, leaving a refined flavor which is more delicate than that of cooked spinach. Chard can be harvested when the leaves are young and tender or after maturity when the stalks are larger and have slightly tougher stems."}, {"rollout": 2, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 1376, 17452, 315, 521, 567, 7481, 304, 279, 46769, 624, 12, 20286, 11, 282, 642, 8503, 11, 27582, 5538, 6176, 10901, 198, 12, 81277, 11, 41854, 54872, 82, 198, 12, 21476, 311, 67698, 714, 448, 264, 16245, 11, 803, 2060, 533, 320, 14689, 1744, 11, 25180, 8, 17172, 198, 12, 12199, 7722, 304, 76752, 476, 29105, 198, 12, 2980, 387, 66472, 1393, 3908, 476, 1283, 47161, 198, 12, 92696, 82117, 480, 11, 773, 2506, 29377, 657, 369, 264, 8028, 315, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 2849, 271, 8304, 220, 17, 25, 23768, 521, 567, 311, 1008, 23880, 9733, 304, 279, 46769, 624, 12, 910, 567, 374, 5435, 311, 48012, 2888, 323, 1008, 48012, 26883, 1561, 11, 537, 67698, 198, 12, 1084, 702, 264, 16245, 11, 803, 2060, 533, 17172, 1091, 67698, 271, 8304, 220, 18, 25, 23153, 26887, 279, 1995, 311, 8253, 1128, 521, 567, 374, 624, 1143, 567, 374, 264, 15933, 88, 6176, 35481, 429, 52191, 67698, 304, 11094, 714, 702, 264, 16245, 11, 803, 2060, 533, 17172, 13, 1084, 646, 387, 1483, 7722, 304, 76752, 476, 29105, 11, 323, 374, 66472, 1393, 3908, 476, 1283, 47161, 13, 11445, 10901, 525, 3460, 11, 282, 642, 8503, 11, 323, 27582, 11, 323, 1181, 54872, 