{"id": "388", "question": "what is the normal b natriuretic peptide", "gt": "The normal B-type natriuretic peptide (BNP) level is not specifically mentioned in the given passages. Therefore, it is unable to answer based on the given passages.", "pred": "The normal B-type natriuretic peptide (BNP) level is likely low, but no specific normal value is provided in the given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To determine the normal B-type natriuretic peptide (BNP) level, I'll analyze the information provided in the passages:\n\n1. Passage 1 states: \"BNP values tend to increase with age and are higher in women than men.\" However, it doesn't provide specific normal values.\n\n2. Passage 2 mentions: \"The finding of low levels tends to exclude heart failure.\" This suggests that normal levels are likely low.\n\n3. Passage 3 states: \"Normally, only a low amount of BNP is found in your blood.\" This directly supports the idea that normal levels are low.\n\n4. None of the passages provide exact numerical values for normal BNP levels.\n\nGiven the information, we can conclude that normal BNP levels are likely low, but we cannot specify an exact number. The passages indicate that both normal and abnormal levels tend to be low, with high levels suggesting heart failure.\n\nAnswer: The normal B-type natriuretic peptide (BNP) level is likely low, but no specific normal value is provided in the given passages.", "cot": "[\"To determine the normal B-type natriuretic peptide (BNP) level, I'll analyze the information provided in the passages:\\n\\n1. Passage 1 states: \\\"BNP values tend to increase with age and are higher in women than men.\\\" However, it doesn't provide specific normal values.\\n\\n2. Passage 2 mentions: \\\"The finding of low levels tends to exclude heart failure.\\\" This suggests that normal levels are likely low.\\n\\n3. Passage 3 states: \\\"Normally, only a low amount of BNP is found in your blood.\\\" This directly supports the idea that normal levels are low.\\n\\n4. None of the passages provide exact numerical values for normal BNP levels.\\n\\nGiven the information, we can conclude that normal BNP levels are likely low, but we cannot specify an exact number. The passages indicate that both normal and abnormal levels tend to be low, with high levels suggesting heart failure.\\n\\nAnswer: The normal B-type natriuretic peptide (BNP) level is likely low, but no specific normal value is provided in the given passages.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"The normal brain natriuretic peptide (BNP) level varies by age and gender, but it is generally a low amount found in the blood.\", \"The normal brain natriuretic peptide (BNP) values are just a guide, and the specific normal range can vary depending on the laboratory that performs the test. However, generally, a normal BNP level is considered to be 0-100 pg/mL.\"]", "time_sec": 13.563, "generation_time_seconds": 13.5594, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0002, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 8253, 279, 4622, 425, 10604, 308, 2361, 552, 28050, 71149, 320, 15594, 47, 8, 2188, 11, 358, 3278, 23643, 279, 1995, 3897, 304, 279, 46769, 1447, 16, 13, 98475, 220, 16, 5302, 25, 330, 15594, 47, 2750, 8376, 311, 5263, 448, 4231, 323, 525, 5080, 304, 3198, 1091, 2953, 1189, 4354, 11, 432, 3171, 944, 3410, 3151, 4622, 2750, 382, 17, 13, 98475, 220, 17, 33845, 25, 330, 785, 9271, 315, 3347, 5866, 27236, 311, 21687, 4746, 7901, 1189, 1096, 13230, 429, 4622, 5866, 525, 4363, 3347, 382, 18, 13, 98475, 220, 18, 5302, 25, 330, 94194, 11, 1172, 264, 3347, 3311, 315, 425, 26227, 374, 1730, 304, 697, 6543, 1189, 1096, 5961, 11554, 279, 4522, 429, 4622, 5866, 525, 3347, 382, 19, 13, 2240, 315, 279, 46769, 3410, 4734, 34776, 2750, 369, 4622, 425, 26227, 5866, 382, 22043, 279, 1995, 11, 582, 646, 31094, 429, 4622, 425, 26227, 5866, 525, 4363, 3347, 11, 7