kens": 117, "pred": "To breed a Shugabeats in My Singing Monsters, you need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Obtain the Shugabush Monster from another island.\n2. Turn your Shugabush Monster into an egg by using the Shugabush breeding structure.\n3. Hatch the egg.\n4. Buy the Shugabeats breeding structure.\n5. Use the Shugabush and Furcorn in the Shugabeats breeding structure to get the Shugabeats monster.\n\nIt's important to note that breeding the monsters left or right does not matter."}], "input_len": 496, "output_tokens": 529, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 59.74, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "429", "question": "how do twins happen", "gt": "Twins can happen in two ways: monozygotic (identical) twins occur when one zygote splits into two embryos, while dizygotic (fraternal) twins happen when two different eggs are fertilized by two separate sperm cells. The likelihood of dizygotic twins is influenced by factors such as West African descent, being between 30 and 40 years old, being taller and heavier than average, and having had several previous pregnancies. Conjoined twins occur when the division of the zygote happens within 8 days of fertilization and can result in complications due to shared organs.", "pred": "Twins can happen when a single fertilized egg splits and forms two embryos or when two different eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Twins can happen when a single fertilized egg splits and forms two embryos or when two different eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells.", "cot": "[\"Twins can happen when a single fertilized egg splits and forms two embryos or when two different eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells.\", \"Twins can happen through two primary mechanisms:\\n\\n1. Monozygotic (identical) twins: This occurs when the zygote splits after fertilization, resulting in two embryos developing from a single fertilized egg. This is less common than dizygotic twins.\\n\\n2. Dizygotic (fraternal) twins: This happens when two separate eggs are fertilized by different sperm cells, leading to two embryos developing from two different eggs. These twins are not genetically identical and are more similar to fraternal siblings than to identical twins.\\n\\nThe passage does not provide information on how twins happen, so we need to rely on general knowledge. Twins can occur in two main ways: either by the zygote splitting after fertilization (resulting in identical twins) or by two separate eggs being fertilized by different sperm cells (resulting in fraternal twins).\", \"Twins can happen in two main ways: monozygotic (identical) and dizygotic (fraternal). In monozygotic twins, a single fertilized egg splits into two embryos very early in development, typically within the first 8 days after fertilization. This results in two genetically identical individuals. An example of monozygotic twins is conjoined twins, where the division of the developing zygote into two embryos occurs, leading to shared organs and often resulting in a high mortality rate due to complications.\\n\\nIn dizygotic twins, two separate eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells, resulting in two genetically distinct individuals. Dizygotic twins are not necessarily identical in appearance or genetics. An example of dizygotic twins is when a woman, who meets certain criteria such as being of West African descent, being between the ages of 30 and 40 years, being greater than average height and weight, or having had several previous pregnancies, has a higher likelihood of having dizygotic twins.\", \"Twins happen when a zygote splits into two embryos during early development. This can result in monozygotic twins (identical twins) or dizygotic twins (fraternal twins). Monozygotic twins develop from a single zygote that splits, while dizygotic twins develop from two separate zygotes, each fertilized by its own sperm cell.\"]", "time_sec": 25.305, "generation_time_seconds": 25.2976, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0004, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [22816, 1330, 646, 3537, 979, 264, 3175, 35114, 1506, 18636, 40467, 323, 7586, 1378, 88773, 476, 979, 1378, 2155, 18805, 525, 35114, 1506, 553, 1378, 2155, 39599, 7761, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0095, 0.0, -0.0882, -0.1562, -5.3267, -1.0421, -0.5419, -1.4803, -0.0029, -0.0001, -0.4895, -3.583, -0.2107, -0.0005, -0.0016, -3.3799, -0.0013, -0.0022, -0.9247, -0.0022, -0.007, -0.0129, -0.0, -0.0241, -0.6098, -0.03