{"id": "539", "question": "lyrics he was a friend of mine", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the lyrics \"he was a friend of mine\" are mentioned in the following passages:\n\n* Passage 1: In the context of the Greenbriar Boys recording the song \"He Was a Friend of Mine\" with singer Dian James in 1963.\n* Passage 2: As part of a fragmented repetition of the line \"He was a friend of mine\" in the passage.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question is:\n\nPassage 1 and Passage 2", "pred": "The lyrics \"He was a friend of mine\" are a recurring phrase in the song. This lyric is repeated multiple times throughout the song, emphasizing the deep bond between the narrator and a deceased friend. The lyrics express the narrator's sorrow and the impact of losing this friend, as indicated by the phrase \"Lord, I just can't keep from cryin'.\"", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "The lyrics \"He was a friend of mine\" are a recurring phrase in the song. This lyric is repeated multiple times throughout the song, emphasizing the deep bond between the narrator and a deceased friend. The lyrics express the narrator's sorrow and the impact of losing this friend, as indicated by the phrase \"Lord, I just can't keep from cryin'.\"", "cot": "[\"The lyrics \\\"He was a friend of mine\\\" are a recurring phrase in the song. This lyric is repeated multiple times throughout the song, emphasizing the deep bond between the narrator and a deceased friend. The lyrics express the narrator's sorrow and the impact of losing this friend, as indicated by the phrase \\\"Lord, I just can't keep from cryin'.\\\"\", \"Step 1: Analyze the question\\nThe question asks about the lyrics \\\"he was a friend of mine\\\" and suggests an answer based on the provided passages.\\n\\nStep 2: Identify relevant information\\nPassage 2 contains the lyrics \\\"he was a friend of mine he was a friend of mine.\\\" This is directly related to the question.\\n\\nStep 3: Confirm the answer\\nThe lyrics \\\"he was a friend of mine\\\" appear in Passage 2.\\n\\nAnswer: He was a friend of mine he was a friend of mine.\", \"Step 1: Identify the relevant information about the song \\\"He Was a Friend of Mine\\\" from the passages. \\n\\n- Passage 1: Mentions the song \\\"He Was a Friend of Mine\\\" recorded by various artists in 1963 and 1964, including Dian James, Bobby Bare, and Petula Clark.\\n- Passage 2: Provides the lyrics \\\"He was a friend of mine he was a friend of mine. He died without a penny he didn't have a dime he was a friend of mine. He died neath the midnight sun he died neath the midnight sun.\\\"\\n\\nStep 2: Focus on the lyrics provided in Passage 2.\\n\\nStep 3: Extract and list the lyrics provided in Passage 2.\\n\\nThe lyrics are:\\n- \\\"He was a friend of mine\\\"\\n- \\\"He died without a penny\\\"\\n- \\\"he didn't have a dime\\\"\\n- \\\"he was a friend of mine\\\"\\n- \\\"He died neath the midnight sun\\\"\\n- \\\"he was a friend of mine\\\"\\n\\nStep 4: Provide the answer based on the extracted lyrics.\\n\\nAnswer: The lyrics are:\\n1. \\\"He was a friend of mine\\\"\\n2. \\\"He died without a penny\\\"\\n3. \\\"he didn't have a dime\\\"\\n4. \\\"he was a friend of mine\\\"\\n5. \\\"He died neath the midnight sun\\\"\\n6. \\\"he was a friend of mine\\\"\", \"Step 1: Identify the relevant information in the passages.\\nThe lyrics \\\"He was a friend of mine\\\" are mentioned in passage 2.\\n\\nStep 2: Extract the specific lyrics.\\nThe lyrics are:\\n\\\"He was a friend of mine\\nHe died without a penny\\nHe didn't have a dime\\nHe was a friend of mine\\nHe died neath the midnight sun\\nHe died neath the midnight sun\\\"\\n\\nStep 3: Formulate the answer.\\nAnswer: The lyrics \\\"He was a friend of mine\\\" are part of a song with a melancholic theme about a friend who died without any money and under the midnight sun.\"]", "time_sec": 22.21, "generation_time_seconds": 22.2037