{"id": "608", "question": "how to do employee schedules", "gt": "To do employee schedules, you need to first understand work laws related to overtime and age restrictions, and you may need to consult a lawyer for this. After that, make a list of all your employees and their duties. You can use scheduling software, a word processing program, or a sheet of paper to create a chart of work days and hours for each day. Once the schedule is complete, it can be distributed to employees through printing physical copies or sending digital copies to employee email accounts. It's advisable to keep a master schedule in case changes need to be made. Tools like Microsoft Excel can be used to create these schedules, especially as your business grows.", "pred": "To create employee schedules, make a list of all employees and their duties, create a chart of work days and hours for each day, print out copies for employees or send schedules to their email accounts, keep a master schedule for making any changes, and use a tool like Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To create employee schedules, follow these steps:\n\n1. Make a list of all employees and their duties.\n2. Create a chart of work days and hours for each day.\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to their email accounts.\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\n5. Use a tool like Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing you to continue using the schedule template as your business grows.\n\nAnswer: To create employee schedules, make a list of all employees and their duties, create a chart of work days and hours for each day, print out copies for employees or send schedules to their email accounts, keep a master schedule for making any changes, and use a tool like Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees.", "cot": "[\"To create employee schedules, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Make a list of all employees and their duties.\\n2. Create a chart of work days and hours for each day.\\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to their email accounts.\\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\\n5. Use a tool like Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing you to continue using the schedule template as your business grows.\\n\\nAnswer: To create employee schedules, make a list of all employees and their duties, create a chart of work days and hours for each day, print out copies for employees or send schedules to their email accounts, keep a master schedule for making any changes, and use a tool like Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees.\", \"To create employee schedules, follow these steps:\\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\\n4. Keep a master schedule for any changes.\\n5. Use Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing for continued use of the schedule template as the business grows.\", \"First, make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform. Next, create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day. Finally, print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts. Keep a master schedule for any changes.\", \"To create employee schedules, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to their email accounts.\\n4. Keep a master schedule to make any changes as needed.\\n5. Use a tool like Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, which can be used as your business grows.\\n\\nAnswer: To create employee schedules, you should make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform, create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day, print out copies for employees or send schedules to their email accounts, keep a master schedule to make any changes as needed, and use a tool like Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, which can be used as your business grows.\"]", "time_sec": 22.502, "generation_time_seconds": 22.4992, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0003, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 1855, 9364, 36769, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 7405, 264, 1140, 315, 678, 8256, 323, 862, 21300, 624, 17, 13, 4230, 264, 9487, 315, 975, 2849, 323, 4115, 369, 1817, 1899, 624, 18, 13, 8213, 700, 10993, 369, 8256, 476, 3624, 36769, 311, 862, 2551, 9618, 624, 19, 13, 13655, 264, 7341, 9700, 369, 3259, 894, 4344, 624, 20, 13, 5443, 264, 5392, 1075, 5100, 21029, 311, 1855, 264, 975, 9700, 369, 5248, 8256, 11, 10693, 498, 311, 3060, 1667, 279, 9700, 3811, 438, 697, 2562, 27715, 382, 16141, 25, 2014, 1855, 9364, 36769, 11, 1281, 264, 1140, 315, 678, 8256, 323, 862, 21300, 11, 1855, 264, 9487, 315, 975, 2849, 323, 4115, 369, 1817, 1899, 11, 1173, 700, 10993, 369, 8256, 476, 3624, 36769, 311, 862, 2551, 9618, 11, 2506, 264, 7341, 9700, 369, 3259, 894, 4344, 11, 323, 990, 264, 5392, 1075, 5100, 21029, 311, 1855, 264, 975, 9700, 369, 5248, 8256, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.2178, -0.0582, -0.1732, -0.0, -0.0056, -0.1854, -0.0011, -0.0002, -0.1924, -0.0011, -0.0001, -0.1369, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -2.9697, -0.0008, -0.5946, -0.0062, -0.1121, -0.0001, 0.0, -0.0045, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.2376, -0.0431, -0.0083, -0.0001, -0.044, -0.0161, -0.0, -0.0008, -0.0563, -0.0, 0.0, -0.1034, -0.0128, -0.0007, -0.051, -0.0072, -0.0014, -0.0002, -0.058, -0.0045, -0.2562, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0012, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0649, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0, -0.4297, -0.4393, -0.0351, -0.1432