{"id": "739", "question": "what is the difference between sms and mms", "gt": "Sure! Here's my answer based on the given passages:\n\nThe main difference between SMS (Short Message Service) and MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is that SMS is limited to sending text-only messages, while MMS allows for sending multimedia content such as images, videos, and audio files, in addition to text.\n\nAccording to passage 1, SMS messages are limited to 160 characters and can be split into multiple parts if they are longer. MMS messages, on the other hand, can carry a larger size of content, including pictures, videos, and audio files, with a maximum size of 300KB.\n\nPassage 2 explains that SMS is a premium service offered by mobile companies, while passage 3 highlights the differences between SMS and MMS, stating that SMS only allows for text, while MMS allows for multimedia content.\n\nTherefore, the key differences between SMS and MMS are:\n\n* SMS is limited to text-only messages, while MMS allows for multimedia content.\n* SMS messages are limited to 160 characters and can be split into multiple parts, while MMS messages can carry a larger size of content.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "The difference between SMS and MMS lies in the types of content they can carry. SMS (Short Message Service) is limited to text-only messages, whereas MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows for the sending of images, sounds, videos, and text, or any combination of these. Additionally, MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB in extensions of formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF, which is significantly larger than the 160-character limit of SMS.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "The difference between SMS and MMS lies in the types of content they can carry. SMS (Short Message Service) is limited to text-only messages, whereas MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows for the sending of images, sounds, videos, and text, or any combination of these. Additionally, MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB in extensions of formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF, which is significantly larger than the 160-character limit of SMS.", "cot": "[\"The difference between SMS and MMS lies in the types of content they can carry. SMS (Short Message Service) is limited to text-only messages, whereas MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows for the sending of images, sounds, videos, and text, or any combination of these. Additionally, MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB in extensions of formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF, which is significantly larger than the 160-character limit of SMS.\", \"SMS stands for Short Message Service and is commonly referred to as a text message. With an SMS, you can send a message of up to 160 characters to another device. Longer messages will automatically be split up into several parts. Most cell phones support this type of text messaging. MMS, or Multimedia Messaging Service, is an evolution of the SMS. With a MMS, you can send a message including pictures, video, or audio content to another device. It is most commonly used to send a photo taken with a camera phone to another phone.\", \"The difference between SMS and MMS lies in the type of content that can be sent. SMS is a form of text messaging that allows you to send a message of up to 160 characters to another device. Longer messages will automatically be split up into several parts. On the other hand, MMS is an evolution of SMS and allows you to send a message including pictures, video, or audio content to another device. It is most commonly used to send a photo taken with a camera phone to another phone. In addition, MMS message can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, Gif etc.\", \"Step 1: Identify the key differences between SMS and MMS based on the provided passages.\\n\\n- SMS stands for Short Message Service and allows you to send a message of up to 160 characters to another device. Longer messages will be split into several parts. Most cell phones support this type of text messaging.\\n- MMS stands for Multimedia Messaging Service and allows you to send a message including pictures, video, or audio content to another device. It is most commonly used to send a photo taken with a camera phone to another phone.\\n\\nStep 2: Compare the two services to highlight the differences.\\n\\n- SMS is restricted to sending text-only messages.\\n- MMS allows sending a combination of text, pictures, sounds, and videos.\\n\\nStep 3: Provide specific examples or comparisons if mentioned in the passages.\\n\\n- SMS is restricted to sending text-only messages.\\n- MMS allows sending a combination of text, pictures, sounds, and videos.\\n\\nAnswer: SMS is restricted to sending text-only messages, while MMS allows sending a combination of text, pictures, sounds, and videos.\"]", "time_sec": 24.917, "generation_time_seconds": 24.9111, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0004, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 29909, 323, 386, 4826, 15448, 304, 279, 4494, 315, 2213, 807, 646, 6777, 13, 29909, 320, 12472, 4856, 5362, 8, 374, 7199, 311, 1467, 15382, 6605, 11, 19853, 386, 4826, 320, 40404, 26936, 73170, 5362, 8, 6147, 369, 279, 11628, 315, 5335, 11, 10362, 11, 6803, 11, 323, 1467, 11, 476, 894, 10601, 315, 1493, 13, 22406, 11, 386, 4826, 6605, 646, 6777, 264, 8131, 1379, 315, 2213, 705, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 29862, 304, 19721, 315, 19856, 1075, 88330, 11, 54562, 11, 323, 46766, 11, 892, 374, 11941, 8131, 1091, 279, 220, 16, 21, 15, 79225, 3930, 315, 29909, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.2306, -0.1153, -0.0, -0.0, -0.2091, 0.0, 0.0, -0.8142, -0.003, -0.0103, -1.1166, -0.0004, -0.2522, -0.1189, -0.05, -2.4109, -0.0435, -0.0109, -1.8854, -0.0001, -0.0029, 0.0, -0.0036, -0.2053, -0.7126, -0.0, -1.8399, -0.329