6, -0.1053, -0.8036, -0.3442, -0.0159, 0.0, -0.1429, -0.4991, -0.2101, -0.5597, -2.3504, -0.1994, -0.235, -0.0, -0.0, -1.5491, -1.225, -0.3655, -0.02, -0.5687, -2.9617, -1.6016, -0.0001, -1.0537, -0.2243, -0.0621, -0.0003, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0285, -0.0127, -0.0017, -1.5406, -0.0343, -0.2274, -0.7118, -0.0155, -0.5835, -0.0483, -0.003, 0.0, -2.1119, -0.0001, -0.0, 0.0, -0.5145, -0.0426, -0.0561, 0.0, -0.0006, -0.1822, -0.9518, -0.3471, -0.212, -0.0015, -1.3439, -1.1662, -0.379, -0.1407, -1.711, -0.9414, -0.1665, -0.1415, -0.2674, -0.0394, -1.0888, -0.7037, -0.2698, -0.1711, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.0174, 0.0, 0.0, -0.1117, -0.0, -0.0368, -0.0083, -0.7106, -0.0054, -1.4466, -0.0, -0.106, -0.8681, -0.0001, 0.0, -1.5812, -0.0158, -0.108, -0.0, -1.9162, -0.1255, -1.054, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0251, -0.0, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0021, -0.0024, -0.0343, -0.2543, -1.2158, -0.0189, -0.0645, -0.0004, -0.0006, -0.0, -0.9234, -0.3139, -1.3565, -0.0004, 0.0, -0.0, -0.0059, -0.0528, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0798, -0.0115, -0.5138, -0.0032, -0.2094, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0005, -0.0069, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0504, -0.0173], "cumulative_logprob": -96.1633, "norm_logp": -0.3756, "input_len": 599, "output_tokens": 256, "pred": "By paying attention to these behaviors, you can better understand if your male coworker is flirting with you."}], "input_len": 599, "output_tokens": 1207, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 17.28, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "84", "question": "symptoms and causes of ibs", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Here are the symptoms and causes of irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) based on the given passages:\n\nSymptoms:\n\n* Diarrhea (often described as violent episodes of diarrhea)\n* Constipation\n* Constipation alternating with diarrhea\n* Belly pains or cramps, usually in the lower half of the belly, that get worse after meals and feel better after a bowel movement\n* A lot of gas or bloating\n\nCauses:\n\n* Abnormal gastrointestinal (GI) tract movements\n* Increased awareness of bodily functions\n* Disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract\n* Alterations in the GI tract motility\n* Abnormal nervous system signals\n* Increased sensitivity to pain\n* Food intolerances\n* Poor absorption of sugars or acids in food\n\nIt's worth noting that the exact cause of IBS is still unknown, and it's believed to be a complex interaction of various factors.", "pred": "Symptoms include diarrhea, constipation, alternating constipation and diarrhea, belly pains or cramps, and a lot of gas or bloating. Causes include abnormal GI tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract, alteration in the GI tract motility, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, food intolerances, abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines, hypersensitivity to pain from a full bowel or gas, and food sensitivities.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Symptoms:\n1. **Diarrhea (often described as violent episodes of diarrhea)**\n2. **Constipation**\n3. **Constipation alternating with diarrhea**\n4. **Belly pains or cramps**, usually in the lower half of the belly, that get worse after meals and feel better after a bowel movement\n5. **A lot of gas or bloating**\n\nCauses:\n1. **Abnormal gastrointestinal (GI) tract movements**\n2. **Increased awareness of bodily functions**\n3. **Disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract**\n4. **Alteration in the gastrointestinal (GI) tract motility**\n5. **Abnormal nervous system signals**\n6. **Increased sensitivity to pain**\n7. **Food intolerances**\n8. **Abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines (too fast or slow, or too strong)**\n9. **Hypersensitivity to pain from a full bowel or gas**\n10. **Food sensitivities, possibly caused by poor absorption of sugars or acids in food**\n\nAnswer: Symptoms include diarrhea, constipation, alternating constipation and diarrhea, belly pains or cramps, and a lot of gas or bloating. Causes include abnormal GI tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract, alteration in the GI tract motility, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, food intolerances, abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines, hypersensitivity to pain from a full bowel or gas, and food sensitivities.", "cot": "[\"Symptoms:\\n1. **Diarrhea (often described as violent episodes of diarrhea)**\\n2. **Constipation**\\n3. **Constipation alternating with diarrhea**\\n4. **Belly pains or cramps**, usually in the lower half of the belly, that get worse after meals and feel better after a bowel movement\\n5. **A lot of gas or bloating**\\n\\nCauses:\\n1. **Abnormal gastrointestinal (GI) tract movements**\\n2. **Increased awareness of bodily functions**\\n3. **Disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract**\\n4. **Alteration in the gastrointestinal (GI) tract motility**\\n5. **Abnormal nervous system signals**\\n6. **Increased sensitivity to pain**\\n7. **Food intolerances**\\n8. **Abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines (too fast or slow, or too strong)**\\n9. **Hypersensitivity to pain from a full bowel or gas**\\n10. **Food sensitivities, possibly caused by poor absorption of sugars or acids in food**\\n\\nAnswer: Symptoms include diarrhea, constipation, alternating constipation and diarrhea, belly pains or cramps, and a lot of gas or bloating. Causes include abnormal GI tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract, alteration in the GI tract motility, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, food intolerances, abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines, hypersensitivity to pain from a full bowel or gas, and food sensitivities.\", \"Symptoms of Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS) include diarrhea, constipation, or alternating between the two, belly pains or cramps, and a lot of gas or bloating. Causes of IBS are believed to be due to a number of factors, including alteration in the gastrointestinal (GI) tract motility, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances.\", \"Symptoms and causes of irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) include:\\n\\nCauses:\\n- Abnormal gastrointestinal (GI) tract movements\\n- Increased awareness of bodily functions\\n- Disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract\\n- Alteration in the gastrointestinal (GI) tract motility\\n- Abnormal nervous system signals\\n- Increased sensitivity to pain\\n- Food intolerances\\n- Hypersensitivity to pain from a full bowel or gas\\n- Food sensitivities, possibly caused by poor absorption of sugars or acids in food\\n\\nSymptoms:\\n1. Diarrhea (often described as violent episodes of diarrhea)\\n2. Constipation\\n3. Constipation alternating with diarrhea\\n4. Belly pains or cramps, usually in the lower half of the belly, that get worse after meals and feel better after a bowel movement\\n5. A lot of gas or bloating\", \"Symptoms of irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) include diarrhea, constipation, alternating between the two, belly pains or cramps, especially after meals, and a lot of gas or bloating. The causes of IBS are not fully understood but are thought to result from a combination of abnormal gastrointestinal tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, and a disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract. It is also believed that the condition may be due to alterations in the gastrointestinal tract motility, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances.\"]", "time_sec": 24.179, "generation_time_seconds": 24.1739, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0005, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [27912, 51173, 510, 16, 13, 3070, 21685, 1118, 39933, 320, 60817, 7481, 438, 16401, 17770, 315, 68293, 8, 1019, 17, 13, 3070, 19167, 48586, 1019, 18, 13, 3070, 19167, 48586, 72362, 448, 68293, 1019, 19, 13, 3070, 33, 11896, 50166, 476, 1560, 14647, 97219, 5990, 304, 279, 4722, 4279, 315, 279, 35417, 11, 429, 633, 10960, 1283, 20969, 323, 2666, 2664, 1283, 264, 65258, 7203, 198, 20, 13, 3070, 32, 2696, 315, 6819, 476, 14211, 1095, 56177, 22571, 4776, 510, 16, 13, 3070, 5830, 8252, 79211, 320, 28034, 8, 41829, 19029, 1019, 17, 13, 3070, 96841, 17526, 315, 47031, 5746, 1019, 18, 13, 3070, 4839, 14123, 304, 279, 10535, 1948, 279, 8109, 323, 279, 48509, 41829, 1019, 19, 13, 3070, 74290, 367, 304, 279, 79211, 320, 28034, 8, 41829, 3852, 1403, 1019, 20, 13, 3070, 5830, 8252, 22596, 1849, 17289, 1019, 21, 13, 3070, 96841, 26443, 311, 6646, 1019, 22, 13, 3070, 26746, 71629, 3020, 1019, 23, 13, 3070, 5830, 8252, 19029, 315, 279, 14889, 323, 2613, 38308, 1543, 320, 36127, 4937, 476, 6301, 11, 476, 2238, 3746, 8, 1019, 24, 13, 3070, 39, 1082, 388, 47837, 311, 6646, 504, 264, 2480, 65258, 476, 6819, 1019, 16, 15, 13, 3070, 26746, 73533, 42379, 11, 10767, 8881, 553, 7852, 43125, 315, 69813, 476, 32869, 304, 3607, 56177, 16141, 25, 76317, 2924, 68293, 11, 733, 48586, 11, 72362, 733, 48586, 323, 68293, 11, 35417, 50166, 476, 1560, 14647, 11, 323, 264, 2696, 315, 6819, 476, 14211, 1095, 13, 73005, 