{"id": "142", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the treatment for an asset that is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is as follows:\n\nThe scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded, as per Section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act. The block concept applies to all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation, and any alterations to the value of the block must be made in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act. The assessee can claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset (i.e., opening WDV of such asset less scrap value) even if the asset is not used for business or professional purposes in that year or subsequent years.\n\nTherefore, the treatment for an asset that is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is to reduce the scrap value from the block in the previous year and claim depreciation on the residual value.", "pred": "When an asset is discarded, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year, and depreciation can be claimed on the residual value of the discarded asset, which is the opening WDV minus the scrap value.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Step 1: Identify the relevant information from the passages.\n- Passage 1: If an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, section 43(6) permits the scrap value of the asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded.\n- Passage 3: The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of such discarded asset, which is the opening WDV of such asset less scrap value.\n\nStep 2: Synthesize the information to answer the question.\n- When an asset is discarded, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year (as per section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act).\n- The assessee can claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, which is the opening WDV minus the scrap value.\n\nFinal answer: When an asset is discarded, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year, and depreciation can be claimed on the residual value of the discarded asset, which is the opening WDV minus the scrap value.", "cot": "[\"Step 1: Identify the relevant information from the passages.\\n- Passage 1: If an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, section 43(6) permits the scrap value of the asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded.\\n- Passage 3: The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of such discarded asset, which is the opening WDV of such asset less scrap value.\\n\\nStep 2: Synthesize the information to answer the question.\\n- When an asset is discarded, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year (as per section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act).\\n- The assessee can claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, which is the opening WDV minus the scrap value.\\n\\nFinal answer: When an asset is discarded, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year, and depreciation can be claimed on the residual value of the discarded asset, which is the opening WDV minus the scrap value.\", \"When an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the Income Tax Act allows for the scrap value of the asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is governed by section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961. The block concept, as mentioned in the passages, involves all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation being considered as a single asset. Any alterations to the value of the block must strictly adhere to the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\\n\\nAnswer: The treatment when an asset is discarded as per the Income Tax Act involves reducing the scrap value of the asset from the block in the previous year where the asset was discarded, under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\", \"Step 1: Identify the key aspects of the question.\\nThe question asks about the treatment of an asset when it is discarded according to the Income Tax Act.\\n\\nStep 2: Analyze the relevant passages.\\n- Passage 1 mentions that for the purposes of the Income Tax Act, a previous year is a distinct unit.\\n- Passage 2 provides an illustration related to the Income Tax Act, but it does not directly address the treatment of discarded assets.\\n- Passage 3 discusses depreciation under the Income Tax Act and mentions that an assessee can claim depreciation on the residual value of a discarded asset.\\n\\nStep 3: Synthesize the information from the passages.\\nPassage 3 provides the most relevant information regarding the treatment of discarded assets. It states that an assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of a discarded asset, which is defined as the Opening WDV (Written Down Value) of the asset less its scrap value.\\n\\nStep 4: Formulate the answer.\\nBased on the information provided in Passage 3, the treatment of an asset when it is discarded is that the assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of the asset, which is calculated as the Opening WDV of the asset less its scrap value.\\n\\nAnswer: The treatment when an asset is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is that the assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of the asset, which is the Opening WDV of the asset less its scrap value.\", \"Step 1: Identify relevant information from the passages.\\n\\nThe relevant information from the passages is:\\n- An asset discarded by a business is not sold.\\n- Section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act permits the scrap value of the asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year.\\n- The block concept is used where all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are considered as a single asset.\\n\\nStep 2: Formulate the answer based on the identified information.\\n\\nBased on the information provided in the passages, when an asset is discarded and not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year where such asset is discarded. This reduction is allowed under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\\n\\nAnswer: The treatment for an asset discarded as per the Income Tax Act is that the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year where such asset is discarded.\"]", "time_sec": 30.166, "generation_time_seconds": 30.1574, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0004, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 9760, 1995, 504, 279, 46769, 624, 12, 98475, 220, 16, 25, 1416, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 28690, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 311, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 624, 12, 98475, 220, 18, 25, 576, 79040, 4060, 374, 19867, 311, 3717, 93089, 389, 279, 32147, 897, 315, 1741, 43210, 9329, 11, 892, 374, 279, 8568, 467, 61971, 315, 1741, 9329, 2686, 20843, 897, 382, 8304, 220, 17, 25, 23153, 26887, 279, 1995, 311, 4226, 279, 3405, 624, 12, 3197, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 11, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 646, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 320, 300, 817, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 4292, 12, 576, 79040, 4060, 646, 3717, 93089, 389, 279, 32147, 897, 315, 279, 43210, 9329, 11, 892, 374, 279, 8568, 467, 61971, 27283, 279, 20843, 897, 382, 19357, 4226, 25, 3197, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 11, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 932