-0.0067, -0.0019, -0.0078, -0.0444, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0802, -0.1168, 0.0, -2.3355, -1.2056, -0.0432, -0.6935, -0.0727, -0.0228, -0.3543, -0.0, -2.2632, -0.7566, -0.0004, -4.7294, -0.0006, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.007, -0.3885, -0.0121, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0091, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.4417, -0.0318, -0.4485, -0.0075, 0.0, -0.0193, -0.0364, -1.1953, -0.0002, -0.0024, -4.1997, -0.6934, -0.1651, -0.0577, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0236, -0.0582, 0.0, -1.7025, -1.1944, -0.0016, -0.0238, -3.8756, -0.0001, -6.0786, -1.412, -2.2858, -0.2929, -0.0564, -0.001, -0.0192, -0.2582, -0.0126, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0254, -0.2519, -0.0001, -0.0846, -0.4611, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0823, -0.0024, -0.0351, -0.3199, -0.0, -0.6627, -0.0026, -0.0, -1.8505, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0506, -0.0006], "cumulative_logprob": -118.2935, "norm_logp": -0.4848, "input_len": 588, "output_tokens": 244, "pred": "To make a bar graph for your research, follow these steps:\n1. Decide on the type of data you want to represent. For example, if you're comparing rainfall amounts, you would need data on the amount of rainfall for each month.\n2. Collect your data. Make sure you have all the rainfall data for the months of February 2005 and February 2006.\n3. Choose the right type of graph. In this case, a bar graph is the appropriate choice for comparing rainfall amounts.\n4. Create the bar graph. Title the graph and determine how high the graph needs to go based on the range of your data.\n5. Add visual elements. A nice bar graph will give a great visual representation of your information and add color to your display.\n6. Label your axes and bars. Make sure your x-axis is labeled with the months and your y-axis is labeled with the rainfall amounts. Each bar should be labeled with the month and the corresponding rainfall amount.\n7. Format the graph. Adjust the graph to accommodate any disproportionate responses that may impact the scale of your graph.\nBy following these steps, you can create a clear and effective bar graph for your research."}], "input_len": 588, "output_tokens": 1017, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 24.39, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "181", "question": "psychological effects of hugging", "gt": "Hugging has physiological benefits and can have a similar effect on the body as certain drugs. It can also lead to emotional intimacy and happy relationships. Hugging and touch, even with inanimate objects, can help reduce existential fears and worry about mortality.", "pred": "The psychological effects of hugging include reducing worry and existential fears, promoting emotional intimacy and relationships, improving emotional well-being through the release of endorphins and oxytocin, and providing a sense of comfort and security.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Step 1: Identify the key topics in the passages related to psychological effects of hugging.\n- Physiological benefits of hugging (Passage 1)\n- Empathy and listening skills (Passage 2)\n- Psychological effects (Passage 3)\n\nStep 2: Analyze each passage for specific information about the psychological effects of hugging.\n- Passage 1: Hugging affects the entire body and is equivalent to the effect of many different drugs operating on the body simultaneously.\n- Passage 2: Empathic listening can lead to psychological hugs, implying a positive psychological effect similar to a hug.\n- Passage 3: Hugs and touch significantly reduce worry of mortality, indicating a reduction in existential fears.\n\nStep 3: Synthesize the information from the passages to form a comprehensive answer about the psychological effects of hugging.\n- Hugging can reduce worry and existential fears.\n- It can lead to psychological well-being through the release of endorphins and oxytocin.\n- It can improve emotional intimacy and relationships.\n- It can provide a sense of comfort and security.\n\nFinal Answer: The psychological effects of hugging include reducing worry and existential fears, promoting emotional intimacy and relationships, improving emotional well-being through the release of endorphins and oxytocin, and providing a sense of comfort and security.", "cot": "[\"Step 1: Identify the key topics in the passages related to psychological effects of hugging.\\n- Physiological benefits of hugging (Passage 1)\\n- Empathy and listening skills (Passage 2)\\n- Psychological effects (Passage 3)\\n\\nStep 2: Analyze each passage for specific information about the psychological effects of hugging.\\n- Passage 1: Hugging affects the entire body and is equivalent to the effect of many different drugs operating on the body simultaneously.\\n- Passage 2: Empathic listening can lead to psychological hugs, implying a positive psychological effect similar to a hug.\\n- Passage 3: Hugs and touch significantly reduce worry of mortality, indicating a reduction in existential fears.\\n\\nStep 3: Synthesize the information from the passages to form a comprehensive answer about the psychological effects of hugging.\\n- Hugging can reduce worry and existential fears.\\n- It can lead to psychological well-being through the release of endorphins and oxytocin.\\n- It can improve emotional intimacy and relationships.\\n- It can provide a sense of comfort and security.\\n\\nFinal Answer: The psychological effects of hugging include reducing worry and existential fears, promoting emotional intimacy and relationships, improving emotional well-being through the release of endorphins and oxytocin, and providing a sense of comfort and security.\", \"Step 1: Analyze the information provided in the passages about the psychological effects of hugging.\\n\\nStep 2: Identify key points from the passages:\\n- Hugs make you feel good for a reason.\\n- Hugs affect the entire body and are equivalent to the effect of many different drugs operating on the body simultaneously.\\n- Empathy and listening skills (empathic listening) can lead to a conversation partner feeling like they are receiving a psychological hug.\\n- Hugs and touch significantly reduce worry of mortality.\\n- Even hugging an inanimate object like a teddy bear helps soothe existential fears.\\n\\nStep 3: Synthesize the information to form a coherent answer about the psychological effects of hugging.\\n\\nAnswer: The psychological effects of hugging include feeling good, reducing existential fears, and promoting emotional intimacy. Hugs can be equivalent to the effect of many drugs on the body, and even hugging an inanimate object can help soothe existential fears. Empathy and listening skills, when used during conversations, can also lead to a psychological hug.\", \"Step 1: Identify the key points in the passages about the psychological effects of hugging.\\n- From Passage 1: \\\"It affects the entire body to such an extent that many scientists claim it is equivalent to the effect of many different drugs operating on the body simultaneously.\\\"\\n- From Passage 2: \\\"The use of empathy and listening skills--empathic listening--sometimes leads to good relationships, emotional intimacy, and happy marriages.\\\"\\n- From Passage 3: \\\"hugging -- even if it was just an inanimate object like a teddy bear -- helps soothe individuals' existential fears.\\\"\\n\\nStep 2: Synthesize the information to form a comprehensive answer.\\n- The passages suggest that hugging has significant psychological effects, including affecting the entire body, leading to good relationships, emotional intimacy, and happy marriages, and soothing individuals' existential fears.\\n\\nFinal Answer: The psychological effects of hugging include affecting the entire body, leading to good relationships, emotional intimacy, and happy marriages, and soothing individuals' existential fears.\", \"The psychological effects of hugging, as described in the provided passages, include:\\n\\n1. **Emotional Intimacy**: Hugging can lead to emotional intimacy, which is a crucial component of healthy relationships. This is evident in the mention of \\\"empathic listening\\\" and \\\"good relationships\\\" in the second passage.\\n\\n2. **Happiness in Marriages**: The use of empathy and listening skills, which are associated with hugging, can contribute to happiness in marriages, as stated in the second passage.\\n\\n3. **Reduced Existential Fears**: A study published in the journal Psychological Science found that hugs, including those with inanimate objects like a teddy bear, significantly reduce existential fears, as mentioned in the third passage.\\n\\n4. **Soothing Effect**: Hugging can help soothe individuals, as noted in the third passage, indicating a calming psychological effect.\\n\\nIn summary, hugging can foster emotional intimacy, contribute to happiness in marriages, reduce existential fears, and provide a soothing psychological effect.\"]", "time_sec": 27.679, "generation_time_seconds": 27.6732, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0003, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 1376, 13347, 304, 279, 46769, 5435, 311, 23187, 6239, 315, 305, 35268, 624, 12, 12809, 40214, 7567, 315, 305, 35268, 320, 12187, 424, 220, 16, 340, 12, 13409, 19135, 323, 14289, 7361, 320, 12187, 424, 220, 17, 340, 12, 68969, 6239, 320, 12187, 424, 220, 18, 692, 8304, 220, 17, 25, 37427, 2986, 1817, 21085, 369, 3151, 1995, 911, 279, 23187, 6239, 315, 305, 35268, 624, 12, 98475, 220, 16, 25, 472, 35268, 21501, 279, 4453, 2487, 323, 374, 13578, 311, 279, 2456, 315, 1657, 2155, 10975, 10350, 389, 279, 2487, 24303, 624, 12, 98475, 220, 17, 25, 13409, 587, 292, 14289, 646, 2990, 311, 23187, 79242, 11, 72867, 264, 6785, 23187, 2456, 4428, 311, 264, 29784, 624, 12, 98475, 220, 18, 25, 472, 13299, 323, 5796, 11941, 7949, 10955, 315, 28428, 11, 18860, 264, 13951, 304, 66639, 23209, 382, 8304, 220, 18, 25, 23153, 26887, 279, 1995, 504, 279, 46769, 311, 1352, 264, 15817, 4226, 911, 279, 23187, 6239, 315, 305, 35268, 624, 12, 472, 35268, 646, 7949, 10955, 323, 66639, 23209, 624, 12, 1084, 646, 2990, 311, 23187, 1632, 32751, 1526, 279, 4879, 315, 835, 16347, 