{"id": "209", "question": "what is chard vegetable", "gt": "Based on the given passages, chard is a type of vegetable that belongs to the same subspecies as beetroot and is characterized by its large, fleshy leaves and thick, crisp stalks. It has a stronger, more assertive flavor than spinach and can be used raw in salads or cooked like in pizzoccheri. Chard is a beet that has been selected for leaf production rather than storage root formation and can be harvested when young and tender or after maturity. It is an attractive ornamental that adds color to the vegetable garden, but it is extremely perishable and should be stored in the refrigerator for a maximum of 2-3 days.", "pred": "Chard is a leafy green vegetable that is a cultivated descendant of the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima. It is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor. Chard has large, deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks, and it is often used in salads or cooked dishes. It is a popular choice for adding color to vegetable gardens due to its attractive appearance.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Step 1: Identify the key information about chard from the passages.\n- Chard is a type of vegetable.\n- It is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor.\n- Chard has large, deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks.\n- It is a beet that has been cultivated for leaf production.\n- Fresh chard can be used raw in salads, while mature leaves and stalks are typically cooked.\n- Chard can be harvested while young or after maturity.\n- It is perishable and should be stored properly in the refrigerator.\n\nStep 2: Synthesize the information to form a coherent answer.\nChard is a leafy green vegetable that is a cultivated descendant of the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima. It is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor. Chard has large, deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks, and it is often used in salads or cooked dishes. It is a popular choice for adding color to vegetable gardens due to its attractive appearance.\n\nAnswer: Chard is a leafy green vegetable that is a cultivated descendant of the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima. It is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor. Chard has large, deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks, and it is often used in salads or cooked dishes. It is a popular choice for adding color to vegetable gardens due to its attractive appearance.", "cot": "[\"Step 1: Identify the key information about chard from the passages.\\n- Chard is a type of vegetable.\\n- It is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor.\\n- Chard has large, deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks.\\n- It is a beet that has been cultivated for leaf production.\\n- Fresh chard can be used raw in salads, while mature leaves and stalks are typically cooked.\\n- Chard can be harvested while young or after maturity.\\n- It is perishable and should be stored properly in the refrigerator.\\n\\nStep 2: Synthesize the information to form a coherent answer.\\nChard is a leafy green vegetable that is a cultivated descendant of the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima. It is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor. Chard has large, deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks, and it is often used in salads or cooked dishes. It is a popular choice for adding color to vegetable gardens due to its attractive appearance.\\n\\nAnswer: Chard is a leafy green vegetable that is a cultivated descendant of the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima. It is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor. Chard has large, deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks, and it is often used in salads or cooked dishes. It is a popular choice for adding color to vegetable gardens due to its attractive appearance.\", \"Step 1: Identify the key information about chard from the passages.\\n- Chard is a type of leafy green vegetable.\\n- It is also known as Swiss chard or plain chard.\\n- Chard has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks.\\n- It is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavor.\\n- Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation.\\n- Chard can be harvested while the leaves are young and tender or after maturity when larger and slightly tougher.\\n- Chard is extremely perishable and can be stored for 2 to 3 days.\\n- Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked.\\n- Chard is cultivated descendants of the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima.\\n\\nStep 2: Synthesize the information to form a comprehensive answer about chard.\\nChard is a leafy green vegetable that is closely related to beets. It has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavor. It is a cultivated descendant of the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima. Chard can be harvested while the leaves are young and tender or after maturity when larger and slightly tougher. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked. Chard is extremely perishable and can be stored for 2 to 3 days.\\n\\nAnswer: Chard is a leafy green vegetable that is a cultivated descendant of the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima. It has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavor. It can be harvested while young and tender or after maturity when larger and slightly tougher. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked. Chard is extremely perishable and can be stored for 2 to 3 days.\", \"Chard is a type of vegetable that is closely related to beets. It shares the same subspecies as beetroot and garden beets. Chard is characterized by its large, fleshy, and tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. It is often used in cooking, particularly when the leaves are mature, and can be cooked in dishes such as pizzoccheri or sautéed. Fresh young chard can also be used raw in salads. Chard is an attractive ornamental plant that adds color to the vegetable garden.\", \"Step 1: Identify the main characteristics of chard as described in the passages.\\n- Swiss chard has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks.\\n- Chard is similar to spinach, but with a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavour.\\n- Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads.\\n- Mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked.\\n- Chard is an attractive ornamental that adds color to the vegetable garden.\\n- Chard can be harvested while the leaves are young and tender or after maturity when larger have slightly tougher stems.\\n- Chard is extremely perishable.\\n\\nStep 2: Determine the primary use of chard.\\n- Chard is primarily used for its leaves, which can be eaten raw or cooked.\\n- It is also mentioned as an ornamental plant.\\n\\nStep 3: Formulate the answer based on the information gathered.\\nAnswer: Chard is a leafy green vegetable that can be used both for its fresh leaves and cooked stalks. It is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked. Chard is an attractive ornamental that adds color to the vegetable garden.\"]", "time_sec": 39.041, "generation_time_seconds": 39.0363, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0003, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 1376, 1995, 911, 521, 567, 504, 279, 46769, 624, 12, 910, 567, 374, 264, 943, 315, 3548