{"id": "248", "question": "difference between feha and ada", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's a brief answer to the question:\n\nThe main difference between FEHA and ADA is that FEHA applies to all employers in California, regardless of size or sector, while ADA applies to private employers with 4 to 15 employees and does not cover public employers. Additionally, FEHA has a broader definition of disability, requiring only that a mental or physical disability limit a major life activity, whereas ADA requires a substantial limitation.", "pred": "The FEHA applies to more employees, doesn't distinguish between private and public employers, and requires only that a mental and physical disability limit a major life activity, not a substantial limit. The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector with four to fifteen employees, distinguishes between private and public employers, and requires a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "The FEHA applies to more employees, doesn't distinguish between private and public employers, and requires only that a mental and physical disability limit a major life activity, not a substantial limit. The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector with four to fifteen employees, distinguishes between private and public employers, and requires a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity.", "cot": "[\"The FEHA applies to more employees, doesn't distinguish between private and public employers, and requires only that a mental and physical disability limit a major life activity, not a substantial limit. The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector with four to fifteen employees, distinguishes between private and public employers, and requires a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity.\", \"The difference between FEHA and ADA is that FEHA applies to a broader range of employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers, while ADA applies to private employers with four to fifteen employees and public employers with fifteen or more employees. Additionally, FEHA requires a disability, whereas ADA requires a substantially limiting impairment.\", \"The difference between the FEHA and the ADA is that the ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees, whereas the FEHA affects more employees, and it doesn’t distinguish between private and public employers like the ADA does.\\n\\nAnswer: FEHA and ADA differ in the number of employees affected and in the distinction between private and public employers.\", \"The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA affects more employees and doesn't distinguish between private and public employers like the ADA does. One of the most important differences between the ADA and FEHA is that with FEHA, a disability is required, whereas under the ADA, a physical or mental impairment must substantially limit a major life activity.\"]", "time_sec": 12.414, "generation_time_seconds": 12.4054, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0002, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 27931, 17020, 16790, 311, 803, 8256, 11, 3171, 944, 32037, 1948, 869, 323, 584, 22426, 11, 323, 7460, 1172, 429, 264, 10502, 323, 6961, 27254, 3930, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 11, 537, 264, 11924, 3930, 13, 576, 78325, 16790, 311, 678, 22426, 304, 279, 869, 10486, 448, 3040, 311, 36655, 8256, 11, 18975, 20527, 1948, 869, 323, 584, 22426, 11, 323, 7460, 264, 6961, 476, 10502, 52217, 429, 31202, 13388, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.5728, -1.3353, -0.0, -1.7922, -0.0004, -0.3762, -0.0004, -3.1676, -4.607, -0.0083, -0.0009, -0.0, -0.0029, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0531, -0.0818, -0.0099, -0.8278, -0.079, -0.