{"id": "300", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "gt": "To make a hot water heater circulate, one can install a recirculation system. The system consists of a pump that pulls hot water from the water heater and simultaneously sends cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused. This ensures that hot water is always available without having to wait for it to circulate naturally. Recirculation systems can be controlled by a button, timer, or motion sensor.", "pred": "To make a hot water heater circulate, a pump is used. This pump continuously circulates the water through the water heater, ensuring that hot water is always available.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To make a hot water heater circulate, a pump is used. This pump continuously circulates the water through the water heater, ensuring that hot water is always available.", "cot": "[\"To make a hot water heater circulate, a pump is used. This pump continuously circulates the water through the water heater, ensuring that hot water is always available.\", \"Answer: According to passage 2, a hot water circulation pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. This pump circulates the water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.\", \"To make a hot water heater circulate, a pump is used. The pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available. In some systems, a recirculating pump rapidly pulls hot water from the water heater, while simultaneously sending cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused.\", \"The passage states that a hot water circulation pump sends 