cter or intelligence before the merits of the argument can be properly discussed."}], "input_len": 320, "output_tokens": 1047, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 69.77, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "380", "question": "what is dmso used for", "gt": "Based on the given passages, DMSO is used for various purposes, including:\n\n1. Industrial uses: As an antifreeze and solvent for a wide range of chemicals.\n2. Medical uses: To relieve pain, reduce swelling and inflammation, promote healing, and treat a variety of medical ailments such as burns, scleroderma, and soft tissue damage.\n3. Pain relief: For muscles and joints, and as a general pain reliever applied to the skin.\n4. Skin care: To penetrate skin and tissue and enter the bloodstream.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"What is DMSO used for?\" can be summarized as: DMSO is used for various industrial, medical, and personal care purposes, including pain relief, wound healing, and skin care.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, DMSO (Dimethyl Sulfoxide) is used for a variety of medical purposes. It is utilized as an antifreeze and solvent for various chemicals in industrial applications. In the medical field, DMSO has a range of uses, including pain relief, reducing swelling and inflammation, and promoting healing. It is particularly effective in relieving pain associated with muscles and joints when applied topically. DMSO has also been documented to aid in the treatment of soft tissue damage, local tissue death, skin ulcers, and burns. In summary, DMSO is used for pain relief, reducing inflammation, promoting healing, and treating various medical ailments.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, DMSO (Dimethyl Sulfoxide) is used for a variety of medical purposes. It is utilized as an antifreeze and solvent for various chemicals in industrial applications. In the medical field, DMSO has a range of uses, including pain relief, reducing swelling and inflammation, and promoting healing. It is particularly effective in relieving pain associated with muscles and joints when applied topically. DMSO has also been documented to aid in the treatment of soft tissue damage, local tissue death, skin ulcers, and burns. In summary, DMSO is used for pain relief, reducing inflammation, promoting healing, and treating various medical ailments.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, DMSO (Dimethyl Sulfoxide) is used for a variety of medical purposes. It is utilized as an antifreeze and solvent for various chemicals in industrial applications. In the medical field, DMSO has a range of uses, including pain relief, reducing swelling and inflammation, and promoting healing. It is particularly effective in relieving pain associated with muscles and joints when applied topically. DMSO has also been documented to aid in the treatment of soft tissue damage, local tissue death, skin ulcers, and burns. In summary, DMSO is used for pain relief, reducing inflammation, promoting healing, and treating various medical ailments.\", \"Step 1: Identify the main information provided about DMSO in the passages.\\n- DMSO is a by-product in converting trees to paper.\\n- It is used as an antifreeze and a solvent.\\n- It has medical uses, including pain relief, reducing swelling, and inflammation.\\n- It has been used to promote healing, particularly for minor cuts, burns, and soft tissue damage.\\n\\nStep 2: Analyze the specific uses mentioned.\\n- DMSO is used for pain relief, especially in muscles and joints.\\n- It is used to reduce swelling, inflammation, and promote healing.\\n- It has been used for various medical ailments, including burns and skin ulcers.\\n\\nStep 3: Synthesize the information to answer the question.\\nBased on the information provided in the passages, DMSO is used for pain relief, reducing swelling, inflammation, promoting healing, and treating various medical ailments, including burns and skin ulcers.\\n\\nAnswer: DMSO is used for pain relief, reducing swelling, inflammation, promoting healing, and treating various medical ailments, including burns and skin ulcers.\", \"Based on the provided passages, DMSO (dimethyl sulfoxide) is used for a variety of purposes:\\n\\n1. **Medical Uses**: \\n   - It is used as a solvent for a wide range of chemicals.\\n   - It is applied topically to relieve pain, reduce swelling, and inflammation.\\n   - It is used to promote healing for minor cuts and burns, with reports of accelerated recovery.\\n   - It has been used in the treatment of soft tissue damage, local tissue death, skin ulcers, and burns.\\n\\n2. **Industrial Uses**:\\n   - It is a by-product in the conversion of trees to paper.\\n   - It is used as an antifreeze in industrial processes.\\n\\n3. **Specific Applications**:\\n   - It is used as an anti-inflammatory and pain reliever for muscles and joints.\\n   - It has been used with varying degrees of success in a great variety of medical ailments.\\n\\nOverall, DMSO is used for both medical and industrial purposes, with a specific focus on its pain-relieving and healing properties.\", \"DMSO (dimethyl sulfoxide) is used for a wide range of industrial and medical purposes. Industrially, it is used as an antifreeze and a solvent for various chemicals. Medically, it is used for its remarkable ability to penetrate skin and tissue, entering the bloodstream. DMSO is known for its pain-relieving properties, reducing swelling, inflammation, and acting as an excellent anti-inflammatory. It has been used to relieve pain in muscles and joints and has been applied topically. DMSO has also been used to promote healing, particularly for minor cuts, burns, and other soft tissue damages, skin ulcers, and burns.\"]", "time_sec": 29.335, "generation_time_seconds": 29.3309, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0002, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 422, 4826, 46, 320, 10344, 41872, 45862, 15011, 577, 8, 374, 1483, 369, 264, 8045, 315, 6457, 9895, 13, 1084, 374, 33616, 438, 458, 3196, 333, 27633, 323, 68896, 369, 5257, 25266, 304, 