{"id": "406", "question": "2006 chevy remove door panel", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is the answer to the question:\n\nTo remove the door panel on a 2006 Chevy, you will need to:\n\n1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup.\n2. Remove the screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\n3. Remove the pin that holds the panel in place on the outer edge of the door.\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the rear door.\n5. Remove any wiring connections.\n6. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\n\nAfter removing the screws and clips, you will be able to remove the door panel. It is recommended to watch an instructional video to see the process and locate the parts mentioned.", "pred": "[Remove the two screws inside the door pull cup, the screw in the middle of the inside door handle, and the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place. Then, use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.]", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "The passage provides instructions on how to remove the rear door panel in a Chevy HHR. Here are the steps mentioned in the passage:\n\n1. Remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup.\n2. Remove the screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\n3. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.\n\nThese steps apply to the Chevy Impala, model years 06, 07, 08, 09, 10, 11, and 12.\n\nAnswer:[Remove the two screws inside the door pull cup, the screw in the middle of the inside door handle, and the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place. Then, use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.]", "cot": "[\"The passage provides instructions on how to remove the rear door panel in a Chevy HHR. Here are the steps mentioned in the passage:\\n\\n1. Remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup.\\n2. Remove the screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\\n3. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.\\n\\nThese steps apply to the Chevy Impala, model years 06, 07, 08, 09, 10, 11, and 12.\\n\\nAnswer:[Remove the two screws inside the door pull cup, the screw in the middle of the inside door handle, and the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place. Then, use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.]\", \"To remove the rear door panel in your Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup, and there's also one in the middle of the inside door handle. On the outer edge of the door there's also a pin the holds the panel in place, you will need to remove that. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door. An instructional video has also been enclosed below that shows this entire process and where everything's located.\", \"To remove the rear door panel in a 2006 Chevrolet Impala, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup and one in the middle of the inside door handle.\\n2. On the outer edge of the door, there is a pin that holds the panel in place. You will need to remove this pin.\\n\\nAfter removing the screws and pin, proceed as follows:\\n\\n3. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.\\n4. Remove all screws and clips in the door panel using a screwdriver.\\n5. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\\n6. Remove any wiring connections.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can successfully remove the door panel from the 2006 Chevrolet Impala.\", \"Step 1: Identify the relevant information from the passages.\\n- Both passage 1 and passage 3 provide instructions for removing the rear door panel in a Chevy HHR.\\n- Passage 2 is about the Chevy Impala but does not specify the year.\\n\\nStep 2: Determine if there is specific information about removing a 2006 Chevy HHR door panel.\\n- Passage 1 and passage 3 both provide instructions for removing the door panel in a Chevy HHR, which includes the steps mentioned in the question.\\n- There is no specific mention of 2006 in either passage.\\n\\nStep 3: Consider if the instructions can be applied to a 2006 Chevy HHR.\\n- The instructions in passage 1 and passage 3 are general and do not specify a year, so they can be assumed to apply to any model year of the Chevy HHR.\\n\\nFinal answer: To remove the door panel in a 2006 Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup, and there's also one in the middle of the inside door handle. On the outer edge of the door there's also a pin that holds the panel in place, you will need to remove that. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.\"]", "time_sec": 26.589, "generation_time_seconds": 26.5813, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0004, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 21085, 5707, 11221, 389, 1246, 311, 4057, 279, 14639, 6006, 6945, 304, 264, 57298, 472, 17088, 13, 5692, 525, 279, 7354, 9733, 304, 279, 21085, 1447, 16, 13, 10783, 279, 1378, 44922, 7407, 4766, 315, 279, 6006, 6815, 10525, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 21966, 304, 279, 6149, 315, 279, 4766, 6006, 3705, 624, 18, 13, 10783, 279, 8983, 389, 279, 15955, 6821, 315, 279, 6006, 429, 9982, 279, 6945, 304, 1992, 624, 19, 13, 5443, 264, 6006, 6945, 16652, 5392, 311, 81279, 279, 6006, 6945, 1007, 315, 279, 472, 17088, 14639, 6006, 382, 9485, 7354, 3796, 311, 279, 57298, 14390, 6053, 11, 1614, 1635, 220, 15, 21, 11, 220, 15, 22, 11, 220, 15, 23, 11, 220, 15, 24, 11, 220, 16, 15, 11, 220, 16, 16, 11, 323, 220, 16, 17, 382, 16141, 7259, 13021, 279,