{"id": "609", "question": "how to do employee schedules", "gt": "To create employee schedules, start by making a list of all employees and the tasks they can perform. Then, create a chart with the work days and hours for each day. You can use scheduling software, a word processing program, or a sheet of paper to do this. Afterward, print out copies for employees or send schedules to their email accounts. It's also important to maintain a master schedule for making any necessary changes. Microsoft Excel can be used to create a work schedule for multiple employees, which can be modified as your business expands.", "pred": "1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform\n2. Make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes\n5. Use Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees so you can continue to use the schedule template as your business grows", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform\n2. Make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes\n5. Use Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees so you can continue to use the schedule template as your business grows", "cot": "[\"1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform\\n2. Make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day\\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts\\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes\\n5. Use Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees so you can continue to use the schedule template as your business grows\", \"To create employee schedules, you can use scheduling software, a simple word processing program, or a sheet of paper. Here's a step-by-step guide based on the information provided:\\n\\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can effectively manage and distribute work schedules to your employees.\", \"Step 1: Analyze the passage to understand the main point about employee schedules.\\n- The passage discusses the process of creating employee schedules, emphasizing the importance of using a methodical approach.\\n\\nStep 2: Identify specific steps mentioned in the passage.\\n- The passage provides a step-by-step guide for making an employee schedule.\\n\\nStep 3: Extract the specific steps from the passage.\\n- Step 1: Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\\n- Step 2: Make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\\n\\nStep 4: Formulate the answer using the information from the passage.\\n- To create an employee schedule, you should make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform, and then make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\\n\\nAnswer: To create an employee schedule, you should make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform, and then make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\", \"To create employee schedules, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\\n5. Use Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees so you can continue to use the schedule template as your business grows.\"]", "time_sec": 22.263, "generation_time_seconds": 22.2579, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0004, "record_pr