em is made up of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the endocrine system, it is done through chemicals known as hormones.\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are discrete and not physically connected.\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals."}], "input_len": 354, "output_tokens": 710, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 23.42, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "643", "question": "differences and similarities between red and white blood cells", "gt": "Based on the given passages, we can see that the primary difference between red and white blood cells is their respective functions within the body. Red blood cells are responsible for oxygen delivery to tissues, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help combat diseases and viruses. However, both types of cells share some common features, such as being formed elements of blood, being formed from pluripotent stem cells in red bone marrow, having a cell membrane and cytoplasm, and circulating in the fluids in blood vessels, which is pumped by the heart.", "pred": "[Similarities: Both RBCs and WBCs are formed elements of blood and are formed from pluripotent stem cells in red bone marrow. Differences: Red blood cells deliver oxygen, while white blood cells fight infections.]", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Similarities:\n- Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are formed elements of blood.\n- Both RBCs and WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in red bone marrow.\n\nDifferences:\n- Red blood cells are responsible for oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body.\n- White blood cells are a part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\n\nAnswer: [Similarities: Both RBCs and WBCs are formed elements of blood and are formed from pluripotent stem cells in red bone marrow. Differences: Red blood cells deliver oxygen, while white blood cells fight infections.]", "cot": "[\"Similarities:\\n- Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are formed elements of blood.\\n- Both RBCs and WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in red bone marrow.\\n\\nDifferences:\\n- Red blood cells are responsible for oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body.\\n- White blood cells are a part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\\n\\nAnswer: [Similarities: Both RBCs and WBCs are formed elements of blood and are formed from pluripotent stem cells in red bone marrow. Differences: Red blood cells deliver oxygen, while white blood cells fight infections.]\", \"Similarities:\\n- Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are formed elements of blood.\\n- Both RBCs and WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in red bone marrow.\\n\\nDifferences:\\n- Red blood cells are responsible for the oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease.\\n- Red blood cells are a part of the circulatory system and carry things such as oxygen throughout the body, while white blood cells are part of the immune system.\\n- Red blood cells have no nucleus and are called erythrocytes, while white blood cells have a nucleus and are called leukocytes.\", \"Similarities: - Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are formed elements of blood. - Both are formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow.\\n\\nDifferences: - Red blood cells are responsible for oxygen delivery to the tissue in the body, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\", \"Similarities: - RBCs, WBCs are formed elements of blood. - RBCs, WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in red bone marrow.\\n\\nDifferences: - Red blood cells are responsible for oxygen delivery to the body, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease. - RBCs are found in the circulatory system, while WBCs are part of the immune system.\"]", "time_sec": 16.823, "generation_time_seconds": 16.817, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0003, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [34402, 1361, 510, 12, 11733, 2518, 6543, 7761, 320, 49, 4897, 82, 8, 323, 4158, 65