{"id": "699", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how you can make ice cream:\n\n1. Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and turn on the machine, following the manufacturer's instructions (passage 1).\n2. Stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until sugar has dissolved, then heat just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge (passage 2).\n3. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract before chilling the mix thoroughly for at least 2 hours (passage 2).\n4. Once the ice cream base is ready, pour it into the ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's instructions (passage 1).\n5. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours (passage 1).\n\nNote that the passages do not provide a specific recipe for making ice cream, but rather provide general steps and tips for making ice cream using an ice cream maker.", "pred": "By following these steps, you can make delicious ice cream at home.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To make ice cream, follow these steps:\n\n1. Prepare the base: Start with a good vanilla ice cream base. This recipe makes one quart of ice cream, so you can double it for more.\n\n2. Chill the mix thoroughly: After preparing the base, chill the mix for at least 2 hours. This step helps the ice cream set properly.\n\n3. Heat the mix: Stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves. Heat the mix just until it's hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge.\n\n4. Chill and add flavor: Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container and chill it thoroughly. Once chilled, stir in vanilla extract.\n\n5. Churn the ice cream: Pour the chilled ice cream mix into an ice cream maker. Turn on the machine and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes.\n\n6. Serve or ripen: When the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately. Alternatively, place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours before serving.\n\nBy following these steps, you can make delicious ice cream at home.", "cot": "[\"To make ice cream, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Prepare the base: Start with a good vanilla ice cream base. This recipe makes one quart of ice cream, so you can double it for more.\\n\\n2. Chill the mix thoroughly: After preparing the base, chill the mix for at least 2 hours. This step helps the ice cream set properly.\\n\\n3. Heat the mix: Stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves. Heat the mix just until it's hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge.\\n\\n4. Chill and add flavor: Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container and chill it thoroughly. Once chilled, stir in vanilla extract.\\n\\n5. Churn the ice cream: Pour the chilled ice cream mix into an ice cream maker. Turn on the machine and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes.\\n\\n6. Serve or ripen: When the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately. Alternatively, place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours before serving.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can make delicious ice cream at home.\", \"To make ice cream, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Prepare the Base**: Start by mixing your base. A good vanilla ice cream base is recommended. You can make a wide variety of ice cream flavors by starting with this base.\\n\\n2. **Churn the Ice Cream**: Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker. Turn on the machine and churn according to the manufacturer's instructions. This process typically takes about 20 to 25 minutes.\\n\\n3. **Ripen the Ice Cream**: Once the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream. Then, place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours. This step helps the ice cream to set properly and become creamy.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you'll have homemade ice cream ready to enjoy!\", \"Step 1: Determine the type of ice cream to make.\\nThe passages mention that a good vanilla ice cream base is a popular starting point for making ice cream. Additionally, the passage mentions that cream-based ice cream is a bit icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream. Therefore, the type of ice cream being made is likely cream-based.\\n\\nStep 2: Prepare the ice cream base.\\nThe first step is to make the base. To do this, follow the instructions provided in passage 3. In this case, it is mentioned that the recipe makes one quart of ice cream, so if you want more, you need to double the recipe.\\n\\nStep 3: Churn the ice cream.\\nOnce the base is made, pour it into an ice cream maker. Turn on the machine and churn according to the manufacturer's directions, which takes 20 to 25 minutes (passage 1).\\n\\nStep 4: Serve or store the ice cream.\\nAfter the ice cream is churned, it is ready to serve. If you want to store it later, place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and put it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours (passage 1).\\n\\nAnswer: To make ice cream, follow these steps: \\n1. Make a cream-based ice cream base by double the recipe if you want more.\\n2. Pour the base into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes.\\n3. Serve the ice cream immediately or store it in the freezer for 2 to 3 hours with a piece of plastic wrap on top.\", \"To make ice cream, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker as directed by the manufacturer, typically for 20 to 25 minutes.\\n2. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or cover it with a piece of plastic wrap and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.\\n\\nThese steps provide a basic method for making ice cream, focusing on the process of churning and chilling the mixture.\"]", "time_sec": 37.009, "generation_time_seconds": 37.0022, "selection_time_seconds": 0.001, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 9853, 12644, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 31166, 279, 2331, 25, 5145, 448, 264, 1661, 32065, 9853, 12644, 2331, 13, 1096, 11116, 3643, 825, 40276, 315, 9853, 12644, 11, 773, 498, 646, 1990, 432, 369, 803, 382, 17, 13, 86489, 279, 6514, 26364, 25, 4636, 20045, 279, 2331, 11, 36301, 279, 6514, 369, 518, 3245, 220, 17, 4115, 13, 1096, 3019, 8609, 279, 9853, 12644, 738, 10277, 382, 18, 13, 26070, 279, 6514, 25, 64192, 13163, 11, 12644, 11, 323, 14074, 1119, 264, 19187, 848, 916, 3347, 8628, 3080, 279, 13163, 13772, 18186, 13, 26070, 279, 6514, 1101, 3080, 432, 594, 4017, 323, 264, 2613, 10058, 315, 31083, 7952, 2163, 279, 6821, 382, 19, 13, 86489, 323, 912, 17172, 25, 23200, 279, 12644, 20980, 311, 264, 4914, 480, 5476, 323, 36301, 432, 26364, 13, 9646, 83942, 11, 23065, 304, 32065, 8649, 382, 20, 13, 910, 399, 279, 9853, 12644, 25, 25968, 279, 83942, 9853, 12644, 6514, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 13, 11999, 389, 279, 5662, 323, 80869, 4092, 311, 279, 13963, 594, 17961, 369, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 382, 21, 13, 52932, 476, 23288, 268, 25, 3197, 279, 9853, 12644, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 498, 646, 8683, 432, 7069, 13, 38478, 11, 1992, 264, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 5961, 389, 279, 9853, 12644, 323, 1992, 432, 304, 279, 49585, 311, 23288, 268, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 4115, 1573, 13480, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 1281, 17923, 9853, 12644, 518, 2114, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.2295, -0.0002, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0172, -0.4008, -0.0129, -0.0023, -0.3392, -0.001, -0.0, -1.8152, -0.018, -0.2148, -0.2932, -0.6175, -0.8027, -0.0012, -0.07