s can be produced by the body and are not necessary to obtain through diet. Essential amino acids include valine, isoleucine, leucine, lysine, methionine, phenylalanine, threonine, and tryptophan. Nonessential amino acids include alanine, asparagine, aspartic acid, glutamic acid, arginine, cysteine, glutamine, glycine, ornithine, proline, serine, and tyrosine."}], "input_len": 573, "output_tokens": 1004, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 30.26, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "105", "question": "how the body systems work together", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's how the body systems work together:\n\n1. The skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, and nervous systems all work together to help keep the body functioning normally. (Passage 1)\n2. The urinary system works closely with all other systems of the body to clean blood from the body and remove waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. (Passage 2)\n3. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. (Passage 3)\n\nTherefore, the body systems work together in the following ways:\n\n* The skeletal system provides support and structure for the body, while the muscular system helps move the body and its parts.\n* The digestive system breaks down food into nutrients that can be absorbed and used by the body, while the respiratory system provides oxygen for energy production.\n* The circulatory system delivers oxygenated blood to the body's cells and removes carbon dioxide, while the urinary system removes waste products from the blood.\n* The endocrine system produces hormones that regulate various bodily functions, including growth and development, metabolism, and reproductive processes.\n* The lymphatic system helps defend the body against infection and disease, while the immune system fights off foreign invaders.\n* The nervous system controls and coordinates the body's functions, including movement, sensation, and thought processes.\n\nOverall, the body's systems work together in a complex interplay to maintain homeostasis and ensure the proper functioning of the body.", "pred": "The body systems work together by performing their specific functions while also collaborating with other systems to maintain overall body homeostasis.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Based on the provided passages, the body systems work together in the following ways:\n\n1. **Skeletal System**: Supports and protects the body, providing structure and movement.\n2. **Muscular System**: Enables movement and maintains body posture.\n3. **Digestive System**: Processes food and absorbs nutrients.\n4. **Respiratory System**: Supplies oxygen to body cells and removes carbon dioxide.\n5. **Circulatory System**: Transports blood, nutrients, and oxygen throughout the body.\n6. **Urinary System**: Eliminates waste products from the blood and maintains fluid balance.\n7. **Endocrine System**: Regulates various bodily functions through hormones.\n8. **Lymphatic System**: Participates in the immune response and fluid balance.\n9. **Immune System**: Defends against infections and diseases.\n10. **Reproductive System**: Produces and nurtures offspring.\n11. **Nervous System**: Coordinates body functions and processes information.\n\nEach system has specific functions but also collaborates with others to maintain overall body homeostasis. For example, the urinary system works closely with other systems to clean waste products, and the respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts, including the circulatory system.\n\nAnswer: The body systems work together by performing their specific functions while also collaborating with other systems to maintain overall body homeostasis.", "cot": "[\"Based on the provided passages, the body systems work together in the following ways:\\n\\n1. **Skeletal System**: Supports and protects the body, providing structure and movement.\\n2. **Muscular System**: Enables movement and maintains body posture.\\n3. **Digestive System**: Processes food and absorbs nutrients.\\n4. **Respiratory System**: Supplies oxygen to body cells and removes carbon dioxide.\\n5. **Circulatory System**: Transports blood, nutrients, and oxygen throughout the body.\\n6. **Urinary System**: Eliminates waste products from the blood and maintains fluid balance.\\n7. **Endocrine System**: Regulates various bodily functions through hormones.\\n8. **Lymphatic System**: Participates in the immune response and fluid balance.\\n9. **Immune System**: Defends against infections and diseases.\\n10. **Reproductive System**: Produces and nurtures offspring.\\n11. **Nervous System**: Coordinates body functions and processes information.\\n\\nEach system has specific functions but also collaborates with others to maintain overall body homeostasis. For example, the urinary system works closely with other systems to clean waste products, and the respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts, including the circulatory system.\\n\\nAnswer: The body systems work together by performing their specific functions while also collaborating with other systems to maintain overall body homeostasis.\", \"The body systems work together by each system performing specific functions that are essential for the overall functioning of the body. For example, the digestive system processes food, the respiratory system provides oxygen and removes carbon dioxide, and the urinary system cleans waste products from the body. These systems interact with each other; for instance, the urinary system works closely with the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, and nervous systems to clean waste products, while the respiratory system works closely with the muscular, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems to provide oxygen and remove carbon dioxide.\", \"The body systems work together by each system performing its specific functions and contributing to the overall function of the body. The urinary system cleans waste products from various systems, such as the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems.\", \"The body systems work together by performing specific tasks that contribute to the overall functioning of the body. For example, the respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide. The urinary system cleans waste products from several body systems, including the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The urinary system includes the kidneys and lower intestines. The respiratory system includes the nose, larynx, trachea, and lungs.\"]", "time_sec": 19.449, "generation_time_seconds": 19.4462, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0003, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 279, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 304, 279, 2701, 5510, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 50, 85155, 739, 95518, 66446, 323, 35136, 279, 2487, 11, 8241, 5944, 323, 7203, 624, 17, 13, 3070, 61598, 21366, 739, 95518, 76316, 7203, 323, 31995, 2487, 47278, 624, 18, 13, 3070, 45217, 533, 739, 95518, 62303, 3607, 323, 90011, 36393, 624, 19, 13, 3070, 1061, 5565, 5269, 739, 95518, 50252, 23552, 311, 2487, 7761, 323, 28160, 12499, 39489, 624, 20, 13, 3070, 34, 2437, 37120, 739, 95518, 4058, 3394, 6543, 11, 36393, 11, 323, 23552, 6814, 279, 2487, 624, 21, 13, 3070, 54515, 3287, 739, 95518, 42320, 258, 973, 12291, 3871, 504, 279, 6543, 323, 31995, 15590, 8172, 624, 22, 13, 3070, 3727, 77638, 739, 95518, 3184, 23156, 5257, 47031, 5746, 1526, 43215, 624, 23, 13, 3070, 43, 31700, 774, 739, 95518, 43481, 973, 304, 279, 22077, 2033, 323, 15590, 8172, 624, 24, 13, 3070, 50739, 2886, 739, 95518, 3892, 1412, 2348, 28920, 323, 18808, 624, 16, 15, 13, 3070, 693, 33270, 739, 95518, 12042, 1603, 323, 59096, 1413, 45371, 624, 16, 16, 13, 3070, 45, 648, 782, 739, 95518, 62501, 2487, 5746, 323, 11364, 1995, 382, 4854, 1849, 702, 3151, 5746, 714, 1083, 11182, 973, 448, 3800, 311, 10306, 8084, 2487, 2114, 535, 10718, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 2