{"id": "197", "question": "leasing meaning", "gt": "Leasing refers to a process in which a firm obtains the use of fixed assets by making contractual, periodic, and tax-deductible payments to the owner of those assets. The lessee is the party receiving the services or assets under the lease contract, while the lessor is the owner of the assets.", "pred": "Leasing is a process by which a firm can obtain the use of a certain fixed asset for which it must pay a series of contractual, periodic, tax deductible payments. The lessee is the receiver of the services or the assets under the lease contract and the lessor is the owner of the assets. The relationship between the tenant and the landlord is called a tenancy, and can be for a fixed or an indefinite period of time. The consideration for the lease is called rent.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Leasing is a process by which a firm can obtain the use of a certain fixed asset for which it must pay a series of contractual, periodic, tax deductible payments. The lessee is the receiver of the services or the assets under the lease contract and the lessor is the owner of the assets. The relationship between the tenant and the landlord is called a tenancy, and can be for a fixed or an indefinite period of time. The consideration for the lease is called rent.", "cot": "[\"Leasing is a process by which a firm can obtain the use of a certain fixed asset for which it must pay a series of contractual, periodic, tax deductible payments. The lessee is the receiver of the services or the assets under the lease contract and the lessor is the owner of the assets. The relationship between the tenant and the landlord is called a tenancy, and can be for a fixed or an indefinite period of time. The consideration for the lease is called rent.\", \"Leasing is a process by which a firm can obtain the use of certain fixed assets for which it must pay a series of contractual, periodic, tax deductible payments. The lessee is the receiver of the services or assets under the lease contract, and the lessor is the owner of the assets. A lease agreement is a contract between two parties: the lessor and the lessee. The lessor owns the asset, and the lessee obtains the right to use the asset in return for regular rental payments.\", \"Leasing is a process by which a firm can obtain the use of certain fixed assets for which it must pay a series of contractual, periodic, tax deductible payments. The lessee is the receiver of the services or the assets under the lease contract, and the lessor is the owner of the assets.\", \"Based on the provided passages and general knowledge, leasing means a process by which a firm or individual can obtain the use of certain fixed assets for a period of time, typically through a series of contractual, periodic, and tax-deductible payments. The lessee is the recipient of the services or assets under the lease contract, while the lessor owns the assets. The relationship between the lessor and the lessee is called a tenancy, which can be for a fixed or indefinite period of time. The consideration for the lease is called rent. \\n\\nThe provided passages also mention that a lease is a contractual arrangement that allows the lessee to pay the lessor for the use of an asset. Common assets that are leased include property, buildings, vehicles, and industrial or business equipment. The lessor is the legal owner of the asset, and the lessee obtains the right to use the asset in return for regular rental payments.\"]", "time_sec": 16.692, "generation_time_seconds": 16.6872, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0003, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [2304, 4422, 374, 264, 1882, 553, 892, 264, 7474, 646, 6851, 279, 990, 315, 264, 3654, 8356, 9329, 369, 892, 432, 1969, 2291, 264, 4013, 315, 75443, 11, 38345, 11, 3742, 77812, 14173, 13, 576, 3541, 4060, 374, 279, 13964, 315, 279, 3516,