{"id": "236", "question": "average weather sausalito", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the average weather in Sausalito can be summarized as follows:\n\n* Temperature: The average temperature in Sausalito ranges from 50°F (December) to 58°F (September).\n* Precipitation: Sausalito receives an average of 34 inches of rain per year, with the most precipitation occurring in January (0 inches).\n* Air Quality Index: The air quality index in Sausalito is 13% better than the national average, but the pollution index is 61% worse than the national average.\n* Sunshine: Sausalito experiences 256 sunny days per year, with an average of 56 days with measurable precipitation.\n* Comfort Index: According to Sperling's comfort index, Sausalito has a score of 84 out of 100, indicating a comfortable year-round climate.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages regarding the average weather in Sausalito during a specific month or time period.", "pred": "The average weather in Sausalito ranges from a low of 50 degrees in December to a high of 69 degrees in July. The annual precipitation is 34 inches, with 56 days of measurable precipitation. On average, there are 256 sunny days per year.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Step 1: Identify the relevant information from the passages.\n- The highest monthly average temperature in Sausalito for September is 58 degrees.\n- The lowest monthly average temperature in Sausalito for December is 50 degrees.\n- The most monthly precipitation in Sausalito occurs in January with 0 inches.\n- The July high is around 69 degrees.\n- The January low is 43.\n- Sausalito gets 34 inches of rain per year.\n- The average US city gets 26 inches of snow per year.\n- The number of days with any measurable precipitation is 56.\n- On average, there are 256 sunny days per year in Sausalito, California.\n\nStep 2: Analyze the information.\n- The temperature range varies from 50 degrees (lowest December temperature) to 69 degrees (highest July temperature).\n- The average precipitation is 34 inches per year.\n- There are 56 days with measurable precipitation.\n- The average number of sunny days per year is 256.\n\nStep 3: Formulate the answer based on the information.\nThe average weather in Sausalito ranges from a low of 50 degrees in December to a high of 69 degrees in July. The annual precipitation is 34 inches, with 56 days of measurable precipitation. On average, there are 256 sunny days per year.\n\nAnswer: The average weather in Sausalito ranges from a low of 50 degrees in December to a high of 69 degrees in July. The annual precipitation is 34 inches, with 56 days of measurable precipitation. On average, there are 256 sunny days per year.", "cot": "[\"Step 1: Identify the relevant information from the passages.\\n- The highest monthly average temperature in Sausalito for September is 58 degrees.\\n- The lowest monthly average temperature in Sausalito for December is 50 degrees.\\n- The most monthly precipitation in Sausalito occurs in January with 0 inches.\\n- The July high is around 69 degrees.\\n- The January low is 43.\\n- Sausalito gets 34 inches of rain per year.\\n- The average US city gets 26 inches of snow per year.\\n- The number of days with any measurable precipitation is 56.\\n- On average, there are 256 sunny days per year in Sausalito, California.\\n\\nStep 2: Analyze the information.\\n- The temperature range varies from 50 degrees (lowest December temperature) to 69 degrees (highest July temperature).\\n- The average precipitation is 34 inches per year.\\n- There are 56 days with measurable precipitation.\\n- The average number of sunny days per year is 256.\\n\\nStep 3: Formulate the answer based on the information.\\nThe average weather in Sausalito ranges from a low of 50 degrees in December to a high of 69 degrees in July. The annual precipitation is 34 inches, with 56 days of measurable precipitation. On average, there are 256 sunny days per year.\\n\\nAnswer: The average weather in Sausalito ranges from a low of 50 degrees in December to a high of 69 degrees in July. The annual precipitation is 34 inches, with 56 days of measurable precipitation. On average, there are 256 sunny days per year.\", \"Step 1: Analyze the information provided in the passages about the average weather in Sausalito.\\n\\nStep 2: Identify the key details about the average weather in Sausalito.\\n\\nFrom Passage 1:\\n- Highest monthly average temperature in September is 58 degrees.\\n- Lowest monthly average temperature in December is 50 degrees.\\n- Most monthly precipitation occurs in January with 0 inches.\\n\\nFrom Passage 2:\\n- Sausalito gets 34 inches of rain per year (US average is 39).\\n- Snowfall is 0 inches (average US city gets 26 inches of snow per year).\\n- Average number of days with measurable precipitation is 56.\\n- There are 256 sunny days per year in Sausalito.\\n- The July high is around 69 degrees.\\n- The January low is 43.\\n- Sperling's comfort index for Sausalito is 84 out of 100.\\n\\nStep 3: Determine the overall average weather characteristics based on the information provided.\\n\\nSausalito has a relatively mild climate with temperatures ranging from a low of 43 degrees in January to a high of 69 degrees in July. The average annual rainfall is 34 inches, which is significantly less than the US average. Snowfall is minimal, and the city experiences 256 sunny days per year, indicating a generally sunny climate. The comfort index is relatively high at 84 out of 100, suggesting an overall comfortable year-round climate.\\n\\nAnswer: The average weather in Sausalito is characterized by mild temperatures, minimal precipitation, and a high number of sunny days. The average high temperature is around 69 degrees Fahrenheit in July, and the average low temperature is around 43 degrees Fahrenheit in January. The average annual rainfall is 34 inches, which is significantly less than the US average, and snowfall is minimal. The city experiences 256 sunny days per year, indicating a generally sunny climate. The comfort index is relatively high at 84 out of 100, suggesting an overall comfortable year-round climate.\", \"To answer the question \\\"average weather sausalito\\\" based on the provided passages, let's break down the information given:\\n\\n1. **Temperature**:\\n   - Highest average monthly temperature in September is 58 degrees.\\n   - Lowest average monthly temperature in December is 50 degrees.\\n   - July high is around 69 degrees.\\n   - January low is 43 degrees.\\n\\n2. **Precipitation**:\\n   - Most monthly precipitation occurs in January with 0 inches.\\n   - Annual precipitation is 34 inches.\\n   - The US average is 39 inches.\\n   - Snowfall is 0 inches.\\n   - Average US city gets 26 inches of snow per year.\\n\\n3. **Air Quality and Pollution**:\\n   - Air quality index is 13% better than the national average.\\n   - Pollution index is 61% worse than the national average.\\n\\n4. **Comfort Index**:\\n   - Sperling's comfort index for Sausalito is 84 out of 100.\\n   - The US average for the comfort index is 54.\\n   - Comfort index is based on the total number of days annually within the comfort range of 70-80 degrees, and penalizes for days of excessive humidity.\\n\\n5. **General Climate Overview**:\\n   - Average US city gets 26 inches of snow per year.\\n   - Sausalito gets 34 inches of rain per year.\\n   - The number of days with any measurable precipitation is 56.\\n   - There are 256 sunny days per year in Sausalito, California.\\n\\nBased on the information provided, the average weather in Sausalito can be summarized as follows:\\n\\n- **Temperature**: Sausalito generally has mild temperatures, with the highest monthly average in September being 58 degrees, and the lowest in December being 50 degrees. The average July high is around 69 degrees, and the January low is 43 degrees.\\n- **Precipitation**: Sausalito receives 34 inches of rain per year, which is less than the US average of 39 inches. Snowfall is negligible, with 0 inches of snowfall on average.\\n- **Comfort Index**: Sausalito has a high comfort index of 84, indicating a more comfortable year-around climate compared to the US average of 54. This is due to the high number of days within the comfort range of 70\", \"To answer the question \\\"average weather sausalito\\\" based on the provided passages:\\n\\n1. **Temperature**:\\n   - The highest monthly average temperature in Sausalito for September is 58 degrees.\\n   - The lowest monthly average temperature in Sausalito for December is 50 degrees.\\n   - The July high is around 69 degrees.\\n   - The January low is 43 degrees.\\n\\n2. **Precipitation**:\\n   - The most monthly precipitation in Sausalito occurs in January with 0 inches.\\n   - Sausalito gets 34 inches of rain per year.\\n   - Snowfall is 0 inches.\\n   - The average US city gets 26 inches of snow per year.\\n\\n3. **Air Quality and Comfort Index**:\\n   - The air quality index in Sausalito is 13% better than the national average.\\n   - Sperling's comfort index for Sausalito is a 84 out of 100, indicating a more comfortable year-around climate.\\n   - The US average for the comfort index is 54.\\n\\n4. **General Climate**:\\n   - Sausalito has a total of 256 sunny days per year.\\n   - The number of days with any measurable precipitation is 56.\\n\\n5. **Comparison to National Average**:\\n   - The pollution index in Sausalito is 61% worse than the national average.\\n\\nGiven these details, the average weather in Sausalito can be summarized as follows:\\n\\n- **Temperature**: Average temperatures range from around 43 degrees in January to 69 degrees in July.\\n- **Precipitation**: Annual precipitation is 34 inches with no snowfall.\\n- **Air Quality**: Air quality is 13% better than the national average.\\n- **Comfort**: The comfort index is 84 out of 100, indicating a more comfortable climate.\\n- **Sunny Days**: There are 256 sunny days per year.\\n- **General Climate**: The city has a moderate climate with warm summer temperatures and mild winter temperatures, minimal precipitation, and no snowfall.\\n\\nAnswer: The average weather in Sausalito includes temperatures ranging from 43 to 69 degrees, 34 inches of annual precipitation, no snowfall, a comfort index of 84 out of 100, 256 sunny days per year, and a general climate with moderate temperatures and minimal precipitation.\"]", "time_sec": 60.173, "generation_time_seconds": 60.1668, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0006, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 9760, 1995, 504, 279, 46769, 624, 12, 576, 8426, 15088, 5461, 9315, 304, 328, 79074, 6357, 369, 6122, 374, 220, 20, 23, 12348, 624, 12, 576, 15457, 15088, 5461, 9315, 304, 328, 79074, 6357, 369, 6652, 374, 220, 20, 15, 12348, 624, 12, 576, 1429, 15088, 59950, 304, 328, 79074, 6357, 13666, 304, 6058, 448, 220, 15, 14924, 624, 12, 576, 5768, 1550, 374, 2163, 220, 21, 24, 12348, 624, 12, 576, 6058, 3347, 374, 220, 19, 18, 624, 12, 328, 79074, 6357, 5221, 220, 18, 19, 14924, 315, 11174, 817, 1042, 624, 12, 576, 5461, 2274, 3283, 5221, 220, 17, 21, 14924, 315, 11794, 817, 1042, 624, 12, 576, 1372, 315, 2849, 448, 894, 65203, 59950, 374, 220, 20, 21, 624, 12, 1913, 5461, 11, 1052, 525, 220, 17, 20, 21, 39698, 2849, 817, 1042, 304, 328, 79074, 6357, 11, 7043, 382, 8304, 220, 17, 25, 37427, 2986, 279, 1995, 624, 12, 576, 9315, 2088, 34227, 504, 220, 20, 15, 12348, 320, 89898, 6652, 9315, 8, 311, 220, 21, 24, 12348, 320, 74154, 5768, 9315, 4292, 12, 576, 5461, 59950, 374, 220, 18, 19, 14924, 817, 1042, 624, 12, 2619, 525, 220, 20, 21, 2849, 448, 65203, 59950, 624, 12, 576, 5461, 1372, 315, 39698, 2849, 817, 1042, 374, 220, 17, 20, 21, 382, 8304, 220, 18, 25, 3377, 6334, 279, 4226, 3118, 389, 279, 1995, 624, 785, 5461, 9104, 304, 328, 79074, 6357, 21283, 504, 264, 3347, 315, 220, 20, 15, 1