{"id": "291", "question": "how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit.\n2. Place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards.\n3. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound.\n4. Insert a meat thermometer and test the meat after cooking.\n5. When the internal temperature of the meat reaches 150 degrees Fahrenheit, cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.\n\nSo, the steps to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven are: preheat the oven, place the roast in a shallow baking pan, cook for 20-30 minutes per pound, check the internal temperature, cover and let it sit before serving.", "pred": "This method ensures that the pork loin roast is cooked thoroughly and evenly.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven:\n\n1. Start by preheating the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit.\n2. Place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack, with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards.\n3. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. \n4. Insert a meat thermometer and test the meat after cooking.\n5. When the internal temperature of the meat reaches 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven.\n6. Cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.\n\nThis method ensures that the pork loin roast is cooked thoroughly and evenly.", "cot": "[\"To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven:\\n\\n1. Start by preheating the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit.\\n2. Place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack, with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards.\\n3. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. \\n4. Insert a meat thermometer and test the meat after cooking.\\n5. When the internal temperature of the meat reaches 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven.\\n6. Cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.\\n\\nThis method ensures that the pork loin roast is cooked thoroughly and evenly.\", \"To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, start by preheating the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Put the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards. Next, cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer, and test the meat after cooking. When the internal temperature of the meat reaches 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving. Enjoy!\", \"To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Preheat the Oven**: Start by preheating your oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit (175 degrees Celsius).\\n\\n2. **Prepare the Pork Loin**: Place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan, ensuring that the fat side is facing upwards. This helps in rendering the fat and adding flavor to the meat.\\n\\n3. **Roast the Pork Loin**: Position the pork loin on a roasting rack within the baking pan to allow for even cooking. Place the pan in the preheated oven.\\n\\n4. **Cooking Time**: Cook the pork loin for approximately 20-30 minutes per pound. This ensures that the meat is fully cooked through. For example, if your pork loin weighs 2 pounds, it should take roughly 40-60 minutes to cook.\\n\\n5. **Check for Doneness**: Insert a meat thermometer into the center of the pork loin to check its internal temperature. The meat is considered done when it reaches an internal temperature of 150 degrees Fahrenheit (65 degrees Celsius). This temperature ensures that the pork is cooked thoroughly but still retains its juiciness.\\n\\n6. **Rest the Pork Loin**: Once the pork loin reaches the desired temperature, remove it from the oven. Cover it with aluminum foil to keep it warm. Let the pork loin rest for about 30 minutes. This allows the juices to redistribute, making the meat more tender and flavorful when it's served.\\n\\n7. **Serve**: After resting, the pork loin is ready to be served. Slice and enjoy, either as a main dish or as part of a larger meal.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can achieve a tender, flavorful, and well-cooked pork loin roast, regardless of whether it starts as a frozen product.\", \"To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit.\\n2. Place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards.\\n3. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound.\\n4. Insert a meat thermometer and test the meat after cooking.\\n5. When the internal temperature of the meat reaches 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven.\\n6. Cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can ensure that your pork loin roast is cooked to perfection.\"]", "time_sec": 36.479, "generation_time_seconds": 36.4693, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0006, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 264, 19690, 35067, 76960, 57685, 304, 279, 23387, 1447, 16, 13, 5145, 553, 855, 383, 1095, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 624, 17, 13, 10771, 279, 19690, 35067, 76960, 304, 264, 25600, 27815, 7215, 389, 1909, 315, 264, 926, 14725, 29659, 11, 448, 279, 8664, 315, 279, 35067, 76960, 12880, 43954, 624, 18, 13, 12514, 279, 35067, 76960, 369, 911, 220, 17, 15, 12, 18, 15, 4420, 817, 30023, 13, 715, 19, 13, 17101, 264, 13041, 92197, 323, 1273, 279, 13041, 1283, 17233, 624, 20, 13, 3197, 27