 quantifies the amount of greenhouse gases, primarily carbon dioxide (CO2), produced as a result of daily activities. The carbon footprint can be reduced by altering lifestyle choices, such as using more energy-efficient appliances, reducing travel, and consuming less meat. For example, car emissions can contribute significantly to a person's carbon footprint, potentially reaching over 6 tons of CO2 per year, which is enough for two people."}, {"rollout": 2, "token_ids": [785, 12499, 42872, 10953, 279, 12158, 5421, 315, 264, 1697, 594, 18899, 13, 1084, 14807, 279, 3311, 315, 12499, 39489, 323, 1008, 36547, 44512, 8947, 438, 264, 1102, 315, 7298, 7488, 13, 362, 12499, 42872, 646, 387, 11046, 553, 3259, 4344, 304, 18899, 11, 1496, 2613, 4344, 646, 1281, 264, 5089, 6672, 13, 576, 5461, 12499, 42872, 817, 1697, 374, 220, 21, 19608, 817, 1042, 11, 323, 304, 279, 547, 808, 2572, 432, 374, 220, 17, 15, 19608, 817, 1042, 11, 448, 264, 5089, 13348, 315, 429, 1660, 4152, 311, 34428, 20143, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1682, -1.1258, -0.0, -0.0194, -0.0, -0.024, -0.0001, -0.0, -1.2254, -0.0102, -0.006, -0.0288, -0.1836, -0.0795, -0.2693, -0.0002, -0.0351, 0.0, -0.0055, 0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0287, -0.0657, -0.0, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0054, -0.0, -0.0664, -1.5052, -0.2722, -0.0, -1.0029, -0.0169, -0.0028, -0.0001, -2.7781, -0.012, -0.923, -0.8947, -0.1934, -0.9464, -0.2726, -0.2551, -0.0007, -0.0708, -0.0002, -0.0029, -0.0006, -0.012, -0.7508, -0.028, -0.6962, -0.0, -0.7916, -0.5955, -0.0468, -0.0105, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.004, 0.0, -0.0747, -0.8759, -0.0231, -0.0, -0.0173, -0.0, -0.2107, -0.0981, -0.0796, -0.0077, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0531, -0.0264, -0.1502, -1.3929, -0.0066, -0.1304, -0.4823, -0.2954, -0.8534, 0.0, -0.0011, 0.0, -0.0402, -0.6346], "cumulative_logprob": -20.8877, "norm_logp": -0.2222, "input_len": 443, "output_tokens": 94, "pred": "The carbon footprint measures the environmental impact of a person's lifestyle. It indicates the amount of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases produced as a result of daily activities. A carbon footprint can be reduced by making changes in lifestyle, even small changes can make a significant difference. The average carbon footprint per person is 6 tons per year, and in the U.S., it is 20 tons per year, with a significant portion of that being due to automobile emissions."}, {"rollout": 3, "token_ids": [785, 2456, 315, 264, 12499, 42872, 374, 311, 6629, 279, 12158, 5421, 315, 264, 1697, 594, 18899, 13, 1084, 14807, 279, 3311, 315, 12499, 39489, 323, 1008, 36547, 44512, 8947, 438, 264, 1102, 315, 7298, 7488, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1682, -0.5008, -0.0, -0.9351, -0.0, 0.0, -0.1329, -0.184, -0.0025, -0.0001, -0.016, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.8329, -0.0055, -0.006, -0.0651, -0.0673, -0.26, -0.5363, -0.0007, -0.0286, 0.0, -0.0102, 0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0646, -0.0556, -0.0, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0096, -0.0, -0.0675, -5.6122], "cumulative_logprob": -9.562, "norm_logp": -0.2516, "input_len": 443, "output_tokens": 38, "pred": "The effect of a carbon footprint is to measure the environmental impact of a person's lifestyle. It indicates the amount of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases produced as a result of daily activities."}], "input_len": 443, "output_tokens": 342, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 43.2, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "337", "question": "how to get rid of ticks from dogs", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to get rid of ticks from dogs:\n\n1. Check your dog's body thoroughly, especially in areas like inside and behind the ears, around the eyes, and other favorite tick hiding places.\n2. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, and wear gloves if needed.\n3. Pull on the tick gently and steadily, making sure not to yank it away from your dog too quickly.\n4. Regularly use tick control products on your dog, as recommended by your veterinarian, to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog in the first place.\n\nIf you have any further questions or concerns, consult your veterinarian for advice.", "pred": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, you can use tick control products recommended by your veterinarian. These products are specifically designed to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog. It's important to regularly use these products, as ticks can attach to and feed on both dogs and humans. By preventing tick attachment, you can reduce the risk of diseases being transmitted to both dogs and humans.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, you can use tick control products recommended by your veterinarian. These products are specifically designed to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog. It's important to regularly use these products, as ticks can attach to and feed on both dogs and humans. By preventing tick attachment, you can reduce the risk of diseases being transmitted to both dogs and humans.", "cot": "[\"To get rid of ticks from dogs, you can use tick control products recommended by your veterinarian. These products are specifically designed to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog. It's important to regularly use these products, as ticks can attach to and feed on both dogs and humans. By preventing tick attachment, you can reduce the risk of diseases being transmitted to both dogs and humans.\", \"To get rid of ticks from dogs, it is best to use tick control products recommended by a veterinarian. These products are designed to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog. Additionally, it is important to check your dog regularly for ticks, especially in areas where ticks are common, such as ears and around the eyes. If a tick is found, it should be removed using a pair of tweezers, grasping the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, and pulling gently and steadily. It is also advisable to wear gloves when removing a tick to avoid potential infections.\", \"To get rid of ticks from dogs, it's important to check inside and behind the dog's ears and around its eyes, as these are common tick hiding places. To remove a tick, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. It's recommended to wear gloves when removing the tick to prevent direct contact. Additionally, using tick control products regularly, as advised by a veterinarian, is the best way to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog.\", \"To get rid of ticks from dogs, you can use tick control products recommended by your veterinarian. It's important to regularly use these products to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog. Additionally, you can check your dog for ticks inside and behind his ears, around his eyes, and other common tick hiding places. If you find a tick, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, and gently pull it off. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick.\"]", "time_sec": 20.787, "generation_time_seconds": 20.7815, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0004, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 11, 498, 646, 990, 9341, 2524, 3871, 11102, 553, 697, 81240, 13, 4220, 3871, 525, 11689, 6188, 311, 5358, 29957, 504, 71808, 311, 697, 5562, 13, 1084, 594, 2989, 311, 15502, 990, 1493, 3871, 11, 438, 29957, 646, 15498, 311, 323, 5395, 389, 2176, 12590, 323, 12677, 13, 3216, 26160, 9341, 19984, 11, 498, 646, 7949, 279, 5214, 315, 18808, 1660, 33599, 311, 2176, 12590, 323, 12677, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0962, -0.0201, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0, -0.0007, -0.0003, -0.0049, -0.7279, -0.3626, -0.6287, -0.0405, -0.0004, 0.0, -0.12, -0.0, -0.3617, -0.0001, -0.0047, -0.4159, -0.0002, -0.5854, -1.7412, -0.0335, -0.0965, -0.0403, -0.0021, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.0029, -0.0486, -0.0019, -0.2286, -2.4882, -0.144, -0.1186, -0.0, -1.5814, -0.0539, -0.0341, -0.0014, -2.3908, -0.0286, -0.136, -0.0239, -0.6008, -0.0194, -0.0773, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.6223, -0.0228, 0.0, -0.001, -0.3622, -3.9053, -1.4382, -1.5201, -0.107, -0.0438, -0.0011, -0.2353, -0.4888, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.9899, -0.8041, -0.0002, -0.2103, -0.0989, -1.9377, 0.0, -1.1963, -0.0106, -0.1473], "cumulative_logprob": -27.4081, "norm_logp": -0.3606, "input_len": 555, "output_tokens": 76, "pred": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, you can use tick control products recommended by your veterinarian. These products are specifically designed to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog. It's important to regularly use these products, as ticks can attach to and feed on both dogs and humans. By preventing tick attachment, you can reduce the risk of diseases being transmitted to both dogs and humans."}, {"rollout": 1, "token_ids": [1249, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 11, 432, 374, 1850, 311, 990, 9341, 2524, 3871, 11102, 553, 264, 81240, 13, 4220, 3871, 525, 6188, 311, 5358, 29957, 504, 71808, 311, 697, 5562, 13, 22406, 11, 432, 374, 2989, 311, 1779, 697, 5562, 15502, 369, 29957, 11, 5310, 304, 5671, 1380, 29957, 525, 4185, 11, 1741, 438, 24230, 323, 2163, 279, 6414, 13, 1416, 264, 9341, 374, 1730, 11, 432, 1265, 387, 6963, 1667, 264, 6716, 315, 14545, 10125, 388, 11, 48987, 9989, 279, 1968, 315, 279, 9341, 1380, 432, 84503, 311, 2