tatus": "success"}}
{"id": "381", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "gt": "To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, first click on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. Then, switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group. Click on the Sort option. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data. Alternatively, you can use Kutools for Excel's Sort Sheets tool to sort all worksheets.", "pred": "After following these steps, the data in the specified column of the Excel sheet should be sorted alphabetically.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically:\n\n1. Open the Excel sheet you want to sort.\n2. Click on the Data tab from the toolbar at the top of the screen.\n3. Locate the Sort & Filter group.\n4. Click on the Sort option.\n5. In the Sort window, select the column you wish to sort by. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B).\n6. Choose the sorting order (A to Z for alphabetical order).\n7. Click on the OK button.\n\nAfter following these steps, the data in the specified column of the Excel sheet should be sorted alphabetically.", "cot": "[\"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically:\\n\\n1. Open the Excel sheet you want to sort.\\n2. Click on the Data tab from the toolbar at the top of the screen.\\n3. Locate the Sort & Filter group.\\n4. Click on the Sort option.\\n5. In the Sort window, select the column you wish to sort by. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B).\\n6. Choose the sorting order (A to Z for alphabetical order).\\n7. Click on the OK button.\\n\\nAfter following these steps, the data in the specified column of the Excel sheet should be sorted alphabetically.\", \"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Click on the Data tab located at the top of the screen.\\n2. Locate the Sort & Filter group within the Data tab.\\n3. Click on the Sort option to open the Sort window.\\n4. In the Sort window, select the column you want to sort by. For example, if you want to sort by the Product column (column B), click on the drop-down menu and select the column name.\\n5. Choose the sorting order, such as alphabetical (A to Z) or reverse alphabetical order (Z to A).\\n6. Click on the OK button to apply the sorting.\\n\\nAfter following these steps, the data in the selected column will be arranged alphabetically.\", \"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Click on the Data tab from the toolbar at the top of the screen.\\n2. Select the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\\n3. Click on the Sort option.\\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name.\\n\\nIn this example, to sort the data by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z), you would select the column B as the sort column.\\n\\nAfter selecting the sort column, click on the OK button to apply the sorting. The data in the spreadsheet should now be sorted alphabetically by the selected column.\\n\\nAnswer:[Select the Data tab, click on the Sort option, select the column by name, and click on the OK button to apply the sorting.]\", \"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can use the following steps:\\n\\n1. Select the data that you wish to sort by. In the given example, the data to be sorted is the Product column (column B).\\n\\n2. Click on the Data tab from the toolbar at the top of the screen.\\n\\n3. Click on the Sort button and select Custom Sort from the popup menu.\\n\\n4. When the Sort window appears, select the data that you wish to sort by. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z).\\n\\n5. Click on the OK button.\\n\\n