{"id": "408", "question": "how to make panko crumbs", "gt": "To make panko crumbs, preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C). Push torn pieces or chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake at 300 degrees F for 6 to 8 minutes, shaking the sheet twice during baking. Remove from the oven and cool completely.", "pred": "Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F, push the bread chunks through a food processor, spread the crumbs on a baking sheet, bake until dry but not toasted, shake the sheet twice during baking, and let the crumbs cool completely.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. Alternatively, push torn pieces of bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet.\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes. Shake the sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\n5. Remove the baking sheet from the oven and let the crumbs cool completely.\n\nAnswer: Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F, push the bread chunks through a food processor, spread the crumbs on a baking sheet, bake until dry but not toasted, shake the sheet twice during baking, and let the crumbs cool completely.", "cot": "[\"To make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. Alternatively, push torn pieces of bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet.\\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes. Shake the sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\\n5. Remove the baking sheet from the oven and let the crumbs cool completely.\\n\\nAnswer: Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F, push the bread chunks through a food processor, spread the crumbs on a baking sheet, bake until dry but not toasted, shake the sheet twice during baking, and let the crumbs cool completely.\", \"1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F. 2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. 3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake at 300 F degrees until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes. 4. Shake the sheet twice during baking. 5. Be careful not to let the crumbs brown!\", \"To make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees Fahrenheit (150 degrees Celsius).\\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet.\\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for about 6 to 8 minutes.\\n5. Shake the baking sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\\n6. Remove the baking sheet from the oven and allow the crumbs to cool completely.\\n\\nNote: Be careful not to let the crumbs brown!\", \"To make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\\n2. Push torn pieces of bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet.\\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for about 6 to 8 minutes.\\n5. Shake the sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\\n6. Remove from the oven and cool completely.\\n\\nThese steps are based on the information provided in the passages.\"]", "time_sec": 24.68, "generation_time_seconds": 24.6734, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0003, "record_process": true, "trajecto