: "Your Snapchat account was temporarily locked because you were using a third-party app to access Snapchat. Snapchat sends a warning message before locking an account, and your account was locked after receiving this warning."}], "input_len": 572, "output_tokens": 753, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 38.6, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "495", "question": "salary exchange pension contributions", "gt": "Salary exchange pension contributions, also known as salary sacrifice, is a method where an employee agrees to give up part of their salary or bonus in exchange for a pension payment paid by their employer. This can allow both employers and employees to save money. The salary that is waived under the salary exchange is equal to the value of the regular pension contribution made. For example, it could be 7.5% or 9% of the pay, depending on the pension scheme. The employer then pays a corresponding amount into the relevant pension scheme.", "pred": "Salary exchange pension contributions refer to a method where an employee agrees to give up part of their salary or bonus in exchange for a pension payment paid by their employer. This allows both employers and employees to make savings. Employers benefit by paying lower National Insurance Contributions (NICs) due to paying their employees a reduced salary. The employee, in turn, receives a pension contribution from the employer instead of a cash salary.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Salary exchange pension contributions refer to a method where an employee agrees to give up part of their salary or bonus in exchange for a pension payment paid by their employer. This allows both employers and employees to make savings. Employers benefit by paying lower National Insurance Contributions (NICs) due to paying their employees a reduced salary. The employee, in turn, receives a pension contribution from the employer instead of a cash salary.", "cot": "[\"Salary exchange pension contributions refer to a method where an employee agrees to give up part of their salary or bonus in exchange for a pension payment paid by their employer. This allows both employers and employees to make savings. Employers benefit by paying lower National Insurance Contributions (NICs) due to paying their employees a reduced salary. The employee, in turn, receives a pension contribution from the employer instead of a cash salary.\", \"Salary exchange pension contributions involve an arrangement where an employee agrees to give up part of their salary or bonus in exchange for a pension payment paid by their employer. This arrangement allows both employers and employees to save money. Employers benefit by paying lower National Insurance Contributions (NICs) due to the reduced salary paid to their employees. The employee benefits by receiving a pension contribution from their employer, which can be a significant part of their retirement savings. The value of the pension contribution that the employee waives under the salary exchange is equal to the value of their regular pension contribution to specific pension schemes such as USS, USPAS, or SGSS, excluding any additional contributions (AVCs). For instance, for members of USS, the regular contribution was 7.5% of the pay from 1 October 2011, and for members of USPAS, it was 9% from 1 August 2011. In exchange, the employer would pay a corresponding amount into the relevant pension scheme.\", \"Salary exchange pension contributions are a way for both employers and employees to save money. In a salary exchange, an employee agrees to give up part of their salary or bonus in exchange for a pension payment paid by their employer. This arrangement allows employers to pay lower National Insurance Contributions (NICs) because they are paying their employees a reduced salary. Employees benefit by receiving a pension contribution that can be invested in a pension scheme, potentially leading to a larger retirement benefit. The specific amounts of the salary waiver and the corresponding pension contributions vary depending on the pension scheme (USS, USPAS, or SGSS) and the employee's regular contribution rate. For example, a member of USS with a regular contribution rate of 7.5% of their pay would give up part of their salary to receive a corresponding pension contribution.\", \"Step 1: Identify the key elements of salary exchange pension contributions from the passages.\\n- Salary exchange is a way for employers and employees to save money.\\n- Employers pay lower NICs when they pay their employees a reduced salary.\\n- Salary exchange involves giving up part of one's salary in exchange for a pension payment.\\n- The University pays a corresponding amount into the relevant pension scheme in exchange for the salary waived.\\n\\nStep 2: Determine the specific details about salary exchange pension contributions.\\n- The employee gives up part of their salary or bonus in exchange for a pension payment.\\n- Employers pay lower NICs as a result of paying their employees a reduced salary.\\n- The University pays a corresponding amount into the relevant pension scheme.\\n\\nStep 3: Formulate the answer based on the identified details.\\nAnswer: Salary exchange pension contributions involve an employee giving up part of their salary or bonus in exchange for a pension payment. Employers pay lower NICs as a result of paying their employees a reduced salary. The University pays a corresponding amount into the relevant pension scheme.\"]", "time_sec": 30.087, "generation_time_seconds": 30.0789, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0004, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [41673, 9289, 27681, 19026, 8300, 311, 264, 1714, 1380, 458, 9364, 32908, 311, 2968, 705, 949, 315, 862, 16107, 476, 12037, 304, 9289, 369, 264, 27681, 8160, 7171, 553, 862, 19136, 13, 1096, 6147, 2176, 22426, 323, 8256, 311, 1281, 18986, 13, 20782, 388, 8760, 553, 12515, 4722, 5055, 21674, 96004, 320, 44947, 82, 8, 4152, 311, 12515, 862, 8256, 264, 11046, 16107, 13, 576, 9364, 11, 304, 2484, 11, 21189, 264, 27681, 18527, 504, 279, 19136, 4518, 315, 264, 8350, 16107, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.2836, -0.0156, -0.4381, -0.0, -1.2897, 0.0, -0.0178, -0.3338, -0.0049, -0.0988, -0.0646, -0.034, -0.0, -0.0104, -