{"id": "509", "question": "what is the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that porterhouse steak is a larger version of T-Bone steak and it contains more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steak.", "pred": "The difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak lies in the location of the cut and the inclusion of more tenderloin in porterhouse steaks compared to T-Bone steaks. Both sirloin steak and porterhouse steak are cut from the short loin area of the beef, but porterhouse steaks are larger due to being carved from a larger portion of the tenderloin.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Step 1: Identify the key differences between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak based on the provided passages.\n\n- Passage 1: Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contain more of the tenderloin compared to T-Bone steaks.\n- Passage 2: Both T-Bone and Porterhouse steaks are cut from the short loin area, with Porterhouse being a larger version of T-Bone due to being carved from a larger portion of the tenderloin.\n\nStep 2: Compare the information from both passages to determine if there is any contradiction or additional information that needs to be considered.\n\n- Passage 1 provides specific information about the cut's location and the inclusion of more tenderloin in Porterhouse steaks compared to T-Bone steaks.\n- Passage 2 confirms that T-Bone and Porterhouse steaks are essentially the same in terms of the cut area and the size difference.\n\nStep 3: Formulate the answer based on the combined information from both passages.\n\nThe difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak lies in the location of the cut and the inclusion of more tenderloin in porterhouse steaks compared to T-Bone steaks. Both sirloin steak and porterhouse steak are cut from the short loin area of the beef, but porterhouse steaks are larger due to being carved from a larger portion of the tenderloin.", "cot": "[\"Step 1: Identify the key differences between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak based on the provided passages.\\n\\n- Passage 1: Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contain more of the tenderloin compared to T-Bone steaks.\\n- Passage 2: Both T-Bone and Porterhouse steaks are cut from the short loin area, with Porterhouse being a larger version of T-Bone due to being carved from a larger portion of the tenderloin.\\n\\nStep 2: Compare the information from both passages to determine if there is any contradiction or additional information that needs to be considered.\\n\\n- Passage 1 provides specific information about the cut's location and the inclusion of more tenderloin in Porterhouse steaks compared to T-Bone steaks.\\n- Passage 2 confirms that T-Bone and Porterhouse steaks are essentially the same in terms of the cut area and the size difference.\\n\\nStep 3: Formulate the answer based on the combined information from both passages.\\n\\nThe difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak lies in the location of the cut and the inclusion of more tenderloin in porterhouse steaks compared to T-Bone steaks. Both sirloin steak and porterhouse steak are cut from the short loin area of the beef, but porterhouse steaks are larger due to being carved from a larger portion of the tenderloin.\", \"Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contain a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steaks.\", \"Step 1: Identify the key information from the provided passages.\\n- The passage states that Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin.\\n- It mentions that Porterhouse steaks contain more tenderloin or fillet.\\n- Porterhouse steaks are described as a larger version of T-Bone steaks, carved from the larger portion of the tenderloin.\\n\\nStep 2: Compare the sirloin steak and the Porterhouse steak.\\n- The sirloin steak is a cut from the back of the animal.\\n- The Porterhouse steak is a cut from the short loin, further back on the sirloin.\\n\\nStep 3: Determine the difference between the two steaks.\\n- The difference lies in their location on the animal and the amount of tenderloin or fillet they contain.\\n- Porterhouse steaks contain more tenderloin or fillet due to being cut from further back on the sirloin.\\n\\nAnswer: Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin, contain more tenderloin or fillet, and are generally more expensive than T-Bone steaks.\", \"The passage does not provide a specific difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak.\"]", "time_sec": 28.453, "generation_time_seconds": 28.4467, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0006, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 1376, 11799, 1948, 27048, 385, 258, 48959, 323, 87186, 7675, 48959, 3118, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 382, 12, 98475, 220, 16, 25, 37937, 7675, 4087, 9810, 525, 3931, 504, 4623, 1182, 389, 279, 27048, 385, 258, 323, 8916, 6644, 803, 315, 279, 27582, 385, 258, 7707, 311, 350, 7671, 603, 4087, 9810, 624, 12, 98475, 220, 17, 25, 11733, 350, 7671, 603, 323, 37937, 7675, 4087, 9810, 525, 3931, 504, 279, 2805, 76960, 3082, 11, 448, 37937, 7675, 1660, 264, 8131, 2319, 315, 350, 7671, 603, 4152, 311, 1660, 48167, 504, 264, 8131, 13348, 315, 279, 27582, 385, 258, 382, 8304, 220, 17, 25, 23768, 279, 1995, 504, 2176, 46769, 311, 8253, 421, 1052, 374, 894, 49759, 476, 5107, 1995, 429, 3880, 311, 387, 6509, 382, 12, 98475, 220, 16, 5707, 3151, 1995, 911, 279, 3931, 594, 3728, 323, 279, 27187, 315, 803, 27582, 385, 258, 304, 37937, 7675, 4087, 9810, 7707, 311, 350, 7671, 603, 4087, 9810, 624, 12, 98475, 220, 17, 42396, 429, 350, 7671, 603, 323, 37937, 7675, 4087, 9810, 525, 15791, 279, 1852, 304, 3793, 315, 279, 3931, 3082, 323, 279,