{"id": "610", "question": "how to do employee schedules", "gt": "To create an employee schedule, start by making a list of all employees and their duties (Passage 2). Then, create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day (Passage 2). Print out copies of the schedule for employees or send them via email (Passage 3). If you need to make any changes, keep a master schedule and update it as needed (Passage 3). Microsoft Excel is a useful tool for creating schedules for multiple employees and can be used as your business grows (Passage 3). It's important to note that there may be other work laws that you need to follow, such as paying overtime if you schedule an employee more than 40 hours per week (Passage 1).", "pred": "1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\n4. Keep a master schedule to make any changes.\n5. Use a scheduling software, a simple word processing program, or a sheet of paper to make the schedule.\n6. Use Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, so you can continue to use the schedule template as your business grows.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To create an employee schedule, you can follow these steps:\n\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\n4. Keep a master schedule to make any changes.\n5. Use a scheduling software, a simple word processing program, or a sheet of paper to make the schedule.\n6. Use Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, so you can continue to use the schedule template as your business grows.", "cot": "[\"To create an employee schedule, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\\n4. Keep a master schedule to make any changes.\\n5. Use a scheduling software, a simple word processing program, or a sheet of paper to make the schedule.\\n6. Use Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, so you can continue to use the schedule template as your business grows.\", \"To create employee schedules, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\\n\\nOptional steps for advanced use:\\n\\n- Use scheduling software or a simple word processing program.\\n- Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\\n- Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\\n- Use software like Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees and maintain the schedule template as your business grows.\", \"1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\\n2. Make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\\n4. Keep a master schedule for to make any changes.\\n5. Use scheduling software, a simple word processing program, or a sheet of paper.\\n6. Use Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees.\\n7. Update the schedule as needed to accommodate changes in employee duties or availability.\", \"To create employee schedules, follow these steps: First, make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform. Then, create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day. Finally, print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\"]", "time_sec": 