: 226, "pred": "[Similarities: Both systems maintain homeostasis, are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms, and use chemical messengers. Differences: The nervous system is made of neuron cells, uses electrochemical pulses for transmission, is continuous and interconnected, and utilizes neurons for signal transmission. The Endocrine System is made of glands, uses hormones for transmission, is discrete and not physically connected, and uses the circulatory system for signal transmission.]"}], "input_len": 354, "output_tokens": 899, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 50.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "644", "question": "how to plant a potato that has sprouted", "gt": "To plant a potato that has sprouted, first cut large potatoes into chunks with two or three eyes each, being careful not to break the long sprouts. Place these chunks on a tray and let them dry out in a cool, dark place overnight. Small, sprouted potatoes can be planted whole. Next, prepare your planting area by turning the soil over with a hoe or tiller to a depth of 12 inches, removing any large rocks or debris. Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep. Cut your potatoes into cubes of about 1 to 2 inches, making sure to leave a sprout on each cube. Place these cubes in the trench, sprouted side facing up, spaced about 6 to 8 inches apart. Cover the potatoes with compost and then replace the dirt on top of the plantings. Water the potatoes thoroughly and regularly when the soil is dry to the touch. Finally, add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants, keeping it at least 4 inches away from the sprouting potato vines. This mulch will help keep the soil cool and maintain a consistent moisture level.", "pred": "By following these steps, you can successfully plant a sprouted potato and ensure its growth.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To plant a sprouted potato, follow these steps:\n\n1. Prepare the planting area: Turn the soil over in your planned planting area with a hoe or tiller to a depth of 12 inches and break the dirt up finely. Remove any large rocks and other debris while hoeing. Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep.\n\n2. Cut the sprouted potato: Cut the sprouted potato into cubes, about 1 to 2 inches on each side, leaving a sprout on each cube. Nonsprouted sections should have two or three eyes on each.\n\n3. Plant the potato cubes: Place the cubes into the bottom of the trench, separating each cube from the other by about 6 to 8 inches. Place the sprouted or eye side of the cubes facing up.\n\n4. Cover the potatoes: Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and then replace the dirt on top of the plantings.\n\n5. Mulch: After planting, add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants, pulling it back at least 4 inches from the sprouting potato vines. This will keep the soil cool while maintaining a consistent moisture level.\n\nBy following these steps, you can successfully plant a sprouted potato and ensure its growth.", "cot": "[\"To plant a sprouted potato, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Prepare the planting area: Turn the soil over in your planned planting area with a hoe or tiller to a depth of 12 inches and break the dirt up finely. Remove any large rocks and other debris while hoeing. Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep.\\n\\n2. Cut the sprouted potato: Cut the sprouted potato into cubes, about 1 to 2 inches on each side, leaving a sprout on each cube. Nonsprouted sections should have two or three eyes on each.\\n\\n3. Plant the potato cubes: Place the cubes into the bottom of the trench, separating each cube from the other by about 6 to 8 inches. Place the sprouted or eye side of the cubes facing up.\\n\\n4. Cover the potatoes: Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and then replace the dirt on top of the plantings.\\n\\n5. Mulch: After planting, add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants, pulling it back at least 4 inches from the sprouting potato vines. This will keep the soil cool while maintaining a consistent moisture level.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can successfully plant a sprouted potato and ensure its growth.\", \"To plant a sprouted potato, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Prepare the Soil**: Turn the soil over in your planned planting area with a hoe or tiller to a depth of 12 inches and break the dirt up finely. Remove any large rocks and other debris while hoeing.\\n\\n2. **Dig the Trench**: Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep.\\n\\n3. **Prepare the Potato**: Cut the sprouted potato into chunks with 2 to 3 eyes each. Place the chunks on a tray or cookie sheet and set them in a cool, dark location overnight to allow the cut ends to dry out.\\n\\n4. **Planting**: If you're planting more than one row, space them apart by about 24 to 36 inches. Place the potato chunks into the bottom of the trench, separating each chunk from the other by about 6 to 8 inches. Make sure the sprouted or eye side of the chunks is facing up.\\n\\n5. **Cover and Mulch**: Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and then replace the dirt on top of the plantings. Continue watering regularly when the soil is dry to the touch, and add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants, pulling it back at least 4 inches from the sprouting potato vines. This helps keep the soil cool while maintaining a consistent moisture level.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can successfully plant and grow sprouted potatoes.\", \"To plant a sprouted potato, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Prepare the Soil**: Turn the soil over in your planned planting area with a hoe or tiller to a depth of 12 inches. Break the dirt up finely, removing any large rocks and other debris. \\n\\n2. **Create a Trench**: Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep. If planting multiple rows, space them apart by about 24 to 36 inches.\\n\\n3. **Cut the Potato**: Cut your sprouted potato into cubes, about 1 to 2 inches on each side, leaving a sprout on each cube. Nonsprouted sections should have two or three eyes on each.\\n\\n4. **Plant the Potato Cubes**: Place the cubes into the bottom of the trench, separating each cube from the other by about 6 to 8 inches. Ensure the sprouted or eye side of the cubes is facing up.\\n\\n5. **Cover with Compost and Soil**: Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and then replace the dirt on top of the plantings.\\n\\nThese steps will help you successfully plant and grow your sprouted potato.\", \"Answer: To plant a sprouted potato, start by cutting the sprouted potato into chunks with two or three eyes each. Place the potato chunks on a tray or cookie sheet, and set them in a cool, dark location overnight so the cut ends can dry out. Small potatoes can be planted whole. Water the potatoes thoroughly. Continue watering regularly when the soil is dry to the touch. Add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants, pulling it back at least 4 inches from the sprouting potato vines. Mulch keeps the soil cool while maintaining a consistent moisture level.\"]", "time_sec": 40.546, "generation_time_seconds": 40.5394, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0004, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 6008, 264, 8151, 18533, 38734, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 31166, 279, 47014, 3082, 25, 11999, 279, 17171, 916, 304, 697, 12909, 47014, 3082, 448, 264, 45876, 476, 11956, 261, 311, 264, 7990, 315, 220, 16, 17, 14924, 323, 1438, 279, 25284, 705, 60702, 13, 10783, 894, 3460, 23035, 323, 1008, 33998, 1393, 45876, 287, 13, 37969, 264, 53252, 911, 220, 19, 14924, 6884, 323, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 14924, 5538, 382, 17, 13, 19649, 279, 8151, 18533, 38734, 25, 19649, 279, 8151, 18533, 38734, 1119, 54104, 11, 911, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 14924, 389, 1817, 3108, 11, 9380, 264, 8151, 411, 389, 1817, 23739, 13, 451, 2382, 649, 18533, 14158, 1265, 614, 1378, 476, 2326, 6414, 389, 1817, 382, 18, 13, 17838, 279, 38734, 54104, 25, 10771, 279, 54104, 1119, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 53252, 11, 49445, 1817, 23739, 504, 279, 1008, 553, 911, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 14924, 13, 10771, 279, 8151, 18533, 476, 7912, 3108, 315, 279, 54104, 12880, 705, 382, 19, 13, 17757, 279, 34167, 25, 17757, 279, 34167, 448, 264, 6193, 315, 56723, 323, 1221, 8290, 279, 25284, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 6008, 819, 382, 20, 13, 29351, 331, 25, 4636, 47014, 11, 912, 264, 220, 19, 24241, 6193, 315, 15602, 331, 2163, 279, 10779, 11, 22266, 432, 1182, 518, 3245, 220, 19, 14924, 504, 279, 8151, 10909, 38734, 85429, 13, 1096, 686, 2506, 279, 17171, 70