igned to the item sold, representing a value somewhere between the oldest and newest units purchased into stock. This method is commonly used in situations where inventory items are so intermingled that it is impossible to assign a specific cost to an individual unit, or when the accounting system is not sufficiently sophisticated to track FIFO or LIFO inventory layers."}], "input_len": 558, "output_tokens": 693, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 65.28, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
