ters, and partly cloudy conditions year-round. The temperature in Indianapolis typically varies from 22°F to 85°F, with temperatures rarely below 3°F or above 92°F. The wettest year recorded in Indianapolis was 1876 with 57.65 inches of measured rain, while the driest year was 1934 with 24.97 inches of measured rain. The most snowfall recorded was in 1979 in Rockford with 74.5 inches in one season."}], "input_len": 404, "output_tokens": 991, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 36.07, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "106", "question": "how the body systems work together", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the body systems work together as follows:\n\nThe skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, and reproductive systems all work together to help keep the body functioning normally. The urinary system helps to clean waste products from the other systems, while the respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the other systems. The nervous system plays a crucial role in coordinating the functions of all the other systems.", "pred": "The body systems work together by each system having a specific function that benefits the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. These systems work together to maintain the proper functioning of the body.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "The body systems work together by each system having a specific function that benefits the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. These systems work together to maintain the proper functioning of the body.", "cot": "[\"The body systems work together by each system having a specific function that benefits the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. These systems work together to maintain the proper functioning of the body.\", \"According to the passages, several systems in the human body work together to help keep it functioning normally. These systems include the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, reproductive, and the nervous systems.\\n\\nThe urinary system works closely with all other systems of the body, cleaning waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems, including the kidneys and lower intestines.\\n\\nThe respiratory system works closely with all other systems of the body, providing oxygen for all body parts and removing carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems, including the nose, larynx, trachea, and the lungs.\", \"The body systems work together to help keep the body functioning normally. The urinary system works closely with all other systems of the body. The respiratory system also works closely with all other systems of the body.\", \"The body systems work together by performing specific tasks that contribute to the overall functioning of the body. For example, the respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide. The urinary system cleans waste products from several body systems, including the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The urinary system includes the kidneys and lower intestines. The respiratory system includes the nose, larynx, trachea, and lungs.\"]", "time_sec": 14.089, "generation_time_seconds": 14.0845, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0002, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 5