{"id": "136", "question": "how to roast individual garlic cloves", "gt": "Sure! Here's how to roast individual garlic cloves based on the provided passages:\n\nTo roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of each clove, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up.\n5. Drizzle a couple of teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\n6. Season the garlic cloves to taste with herbs and spices, if desired.\n7. Roast the garlic in the preheated oven for up to 45 minutes or until the cloves are softened to your liking.\n8. Store roasted garlic cloves in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.\n\nNote that the roasting time may vary depending on the size of your garlic cloves, so check on them periodically to avoid overcooking.", "pred": "This method allows the garlic cloves to roast evenly and become soft and flavorful.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving the skins intact.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of each clove, exposing the individual cloves.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up.\n5. Drizzle a couple of teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed garlic clove.\n6. Rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves using your fingers.\n\nThis method allows the garlic cloves to roast evenly and become soft and flavorful.", "cot": "[\"To roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving the skins intact.\\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of each clove, exposing the individual cloves.\\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up.\\n5. Drizzle a couple of teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed garlic clove.\\n6. Rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves using your fingers.\\n\\nThis method allows the garlic cloves to roast evenly and become soft and flavorful.\", \"To roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 400°F (205°C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of the cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. A muffin pan works great for this as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.\\n5. Drizzle a couple of teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can roast individual garlic cloves effectively.\", \"Roasting individual garlic cloves involves several steps. First, preheat the oven to 400°F (205° C). Next, peel and discard the outer layers of the garlic bulb, leaving the skins of the individual cloves intact. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of the cloves to expose them. Place the garlic heads, cut side up, in a baking pan, such as a muffin pan, to keep them from rolling around. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed garlic head and use your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cloves.\\n\\nAnswer: To roast individual garlic cloves, preheat the oven to 400°F (205° C), peel and discard the outer layers, expose the cloves by cutting 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top, place them cut side up in a baking pan, drizzle with olive oil, and rub the oil over the cloves.\", \"I will analyze the passages step by step to answer the question.\\n\\nStep 1: Understand the question\\nThe question asks about the method to roast individual garlic cloves.\\n\\nStep 2: Identify relevant information\\nPassage 3 provides a method for roasting whole heads of garlic, which includes individual cloves.\\n\\nStep 3: Extract specific details\\nFrom Passage 3, I can extract the following details:\\na) Preheat the oven to 400°F (205°C).\\nb) Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the cloves.\\nc) Cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of the cloves to expose them.\\nd) Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up.\\ne) Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head and rub the oil over the cloves.\\n\\nStep 4: Formulate the answer\\nBased on the information provided in the passages, here's how to roast individual garlic cloves:\\n1. Preheat the oven to 400°F (205°C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the cloves.\\n3. Cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of the cloves to expose them.\\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up.\\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head and rub the oil over the cloves.\\n\\nAnswer: Roast individual garlic cloves by preheating the oven to 400°F (205°C), peeling and cutting the cloves, placing them in a baking pan, and drizzling olive oil over them before roasting.\"]", "time_sec": 28.742, "generation_time_seconds": 28.7387, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0004, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 57685, 3842, 30635, 84288, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 697, 23387, 311, 220, 19, 15, 15, 58472, 320, 17, 15, 20, 30937, 4292, 17, 13, 88594, 323, 37867, 279, 25298, 722, 15955, 13617, 315, 279, 43