{"id": "338", "question": "how to make ribs", "gt": "To make ribs, start by removing the membrane from the bottom of the ribs with a knife. Place the ribs in a resealable bag and add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover them. Afterwards, line a baking pan with heavy duty foil. Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer for heat circulation on all sides. Mix mustard and liquid smoke, if using, and brush the ribs on both sides. Sprinkle the ribs with a dry rub and pat gently to make sure it adheres to the meat. To grill the ribs, heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium and remove the ribs from the foil. Place them meaty-side up on the grill and brush them with some of the sauce. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook for another 5 minutes. Continue this process until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through with grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.", "pred": "To make ribs, you can either grill them or oven-cook them. For grilling, heat the grill to medium, place the ribs meaty-side up, brush with sauce, and cook for 20 minutes, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes. For oven-cooking, remove the membrane, season the ribs, and cook in a resealable bag with BBQ sauce in an oven-lined pan with a foil tent.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, here's how to make ribs:\n\n1. **Preparation:**\n   - If grilling: Remove the ribs from the foil.\n   - If oven-cooked: Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs.\n\n2. **Grilling (Option 1):**\n   - Heat the grill to medium (350°F to 450°F).\n   - Place the ribs meaty-side up on the grill and brush them with some sauce.\n   - Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes.\n   - Flip and brush the ribs and cook another 5 minutes.\n   - Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes.\n   - Cook for a total of 20 minutes until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks.\n\n3. **Preparation:**\n   - Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer.\n   - Season the ribs: Mix mustard and liquid smoke (if using), brush on both sides of the ribs.\n   - Sprinkle the ribs with a dry rub and pat gently to ensure it adheres to the rib meat.\n\n4. **Oven-cooked (Option 2):**\n   - Put the ribs in a resealable bag and add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover.\n   - Line the baking pan with heavy-duty foil, overlapping the foil to make a tent.\n\nAnswer: To make ribs, you can either grill them or oven-cook them. For grilling, heat the grill to medium, place the ribs meaty-side up, brush with sauce, and cook for 20 minutes, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes. For oven-cooking, remove the membrane, season the ribs, and cook in a resealable bag with BBQ sauce in an oven-lined pan with a foil tent.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, here's how to make ribs:\\n\\n1. **Preparation:**\\n   - If grilling: Remove the ribs from the foil.\\n   - If oven-cooked: Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs.\\n\\n2. **Grilling (Option 1):**\\n   - Heat the grill to medium (350°F to 450°F).\\n   - Place the ribs meaty-side up on the grill and brush them with some sauce.\\n   - Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes.\\n   - Flip and brush the ribs and cook another 5 minutes.\\n   - Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes.\\n   - Cook for a total of 20 minutes until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks.\\n\\n3. **Preparation:**\\n   - Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer.\\n   - Season the ribs: Mix mustard and liquid smoke (if using), brush on both sides of the ribs.\\n   - Sprinkle the ribs with a dry rub and pat gently to ensure it adheres to the rib meat.\\n\\n4. **Oven-cooked (Option 2):**\\n   - Put the ribs in a resealable bag and add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover.\\n   - Line the baking pan with heavy-duty foil, overlapping the foil to make a tent.\\n\\nAnswer: To make ribs, you can either grill them or oven-cook them. For grilling, heat the grill to medium, place the ribs meaty-side up, brush with sauce, and cook for 20 minutes, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes. For oven-cooking, remove the membrane, season the ribs, and cook in a resealable bag with BBQ sauce in an oven-lined pan with a foil tent.\", \"To make ribs, first, remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs. Use a knife to start it near the narrow end, and pull off in one piece. Next, put the ribs in a resealable bag and add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover. After that, line the baking pan with heavy duty foil, using plenty of overlapping foil to make a tent.\", \"To make ribs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Preparation:**\\n   - For grill method: Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F). Place the ribs, meaty-side up, on the grill. Brush them with some sauce. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook another 5 minutes. Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks. This takes a total grilling time of 20 minutes.\\n\\n2. **Seasoning and Cooking (Oven):**\\n   - Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs. Use a knife to start it near the narrow end, and pull off in one piece.\\n   - Put the ribs in a resealable bag. Add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover.\\n   - Line the baking pan with heavy-duty foil. Use plenty of overlapping foil to make a tent.\\n\\n3. **Preparation (Grill or Oven):**\\n   - Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer to allow heat circulation on all sides.\\n\\n4. **Cooking:**\\n   - Season the ribs: Mix the mustard and the liquid smoke (if using), and brush the ribs on both sides. Sprinkle the ribs with the dry rub and pat gently to make sure the rub adheres to the rib meat.\\n\\nThe exact method depends on whether you are grilling or oven-cooking the ribs.\", \"To make ribs, you can follow the steps outlined in the passages:\\n\\n1. **Grilling ribs**:\\n   - Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F).\\n   - Remove the ribs from the foil and place them meaty-side up on the grill.\\n   - Brush them with some sauce.\\n   - Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes.\\n   - Flip and brush the ribs and cook another 5 minutes.\\n   - Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes.\\n   - The ribs should be heated through and have grill marks after a total grilling time of 20 minutes.\\n\\n2. **Oven-cooked ribs**:\\n   - Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs.\\n   - Put the ribs in a resealable bag and add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover.\\n   - Line the baking pan with heavy-duty foil and make sure it overlaps to create a tent.\\n\\nAdditionally, for the oven-cooked ribs:\\n- Season the ribs by mixing mustard and liquid smoke (if using) and brushing them on both sides.\\n- Sprinkle the ribs with a dry rub and pat gently to ensure the rub adheres to the rib meat.\\n\\nThese methods provide a basic guide on how to prepare ribs, either by grilling or oven-cooking them.\"]", "time_sec": 46.154, "generation_time_seconds": 46.15, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0004, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 594, 1246, 311, 1281, 55149, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 4703, 35135, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 1416, 1081, 9400, 25, 10783, 279, 55149, 504, 279, 46399, 624, 256, 481, 1416, 23387, 22471, 10823, 25, 10783, 279, 38554, 504, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 55149, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 6464, 9400, 320, 5341, 220, 16, 1648, 1019, 256, 481, 26070, 279, 39058, 311, 11051, 320, 18, 20, 15, 58472, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 4292, 256, 481, 10771, 279, 55149, 13041, 88, 24067, 705, 389, 279, 39058, 323, 15625, 1105, 448, 1045, 19187, 624, 256, 481, 17757, 279, 39058, 323, 4296, 369, 220, 20, 4420, 624, 256, 481, 40284, 323, 15625, 279, 55149, 323, 4296, 2441, 220, 20, 4420