{"id": "382", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "gt": "Passage 3 provides the necessary information to answer the question. To arrange an excel sheet alphabetically, click on the Select All button, switch to the Data tab, locate the Sort & Filter group, click on the Sort option, and then select the desired column to sort by.", "pred": "In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z). After selecting the column, click on the OK button. Now when you return to the spreadsheet, the data should be sorted alphabetically.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\n\n1. Select the data you wish to sort by clicking on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. The cells in your worksheet will highlight to confirm they're selected.\n2. Go to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\n3. Click on the Sort option.\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\n\nIn this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z). After selecting the column, click on the OK button. Now when you return to the spreadsheet, the data should be sorted alphabetically.", "cot": "[\"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select the data you wish to sort by clicking on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. The cells in your worksheet will highlight to confirm they're selected.\\n2. Go to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\\n3. Click on the Sort option.\\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\\n\\nIn this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z). After selecting the column, click on the OK button. Now when you return to the spreadsheet, the data should be sorted alphabetically.\", \"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can use the Sort function in Excel. Here's how:\\n\\n1. Select the data you want to sort.\\n2. Go to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon.\\n3. Click on the Sort option.\\n4. In the Sort By drop-down menu, select a column by name that corresponds to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\\n5. Excel will then sort the data in alphabetical order (A to Z).\\n\\nAlternatively, you can use Kutools for Excel, which has a Sort Sheets tool that can sort all worksheets easily.\", \"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select all the cells you want to sort by clicking on the \\\"Select All\\\" button at the intersection of your row and column headings. The cells in your worksheet will highlight to confirm they're selected.\\n\\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the \\\"Sort & Filter\\\" group. Click on the \\\"Sort\\\" option.\\n\\n3. Click on the \\\"Sort By\\\" drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\\n\\n4. In the Sort window, you can choose to sort the data in alphabetical order (A to Z) or reverse alphabetical order (Z to A). For example, if you want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order, select that column and choose \\\"A to Z\\\" as the sort order.\\n\\n5. Click on the \\\"OK\\\" button to apply the sort. The data in your Excel sheet should now be arranged alphabetically according to the selected column.\\n\\nAlternative method using Kutools for Excel:\\n1. Open Kutools for Excel and navigate to the \\\"Sort Sheets\\\" tool.\\n2. Select the \\\"Custom Sort\\\" option from the popup menu.\\n3. In the Sort window, select the data you wish to sort by. For example, you can sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z).\\n4. Click on the \\\"OK\\\" button to apply the sort.\\n\\nBoth methods will help you arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically based on the selected column.\", \"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can use the \\\"Custom Sort\\\" function:\\n\\n1. Click on the \\\"Data\\\" tab from the toolbar at the top of the screen.\\n2. Click on the \\\"Sort\\\" button and select \\\"Custom Sort\\\" from the popup menu.\\n3. In the \\\"Sort\\\" window, select the data that you wish to sort by.\\n4. For this example, we want to sort by the \\\"Product\\\" column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z).\\n5. Click on the \\\"OK\\\" button. Now, when you return to the spreadsheet, the data should be sorted alphabetically.\\n\\nThis method ensures that the data is arranged in alphabetical order based on the selected column.\"]", "time_sec": 33.574, "generation_time_seconds": 33.5674, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0007, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 279, 821, 498, 6426, 311, 3378, 553, 18458, 389, 279, 8427, 2009, 3137, 518, 279, 19246, 315, 697, 2802, 323, 3250, 69452, 13, 576, 7761, 304, 697, 36636, 686, 11167, 311, 7683, 807, 2299, 4091, 624, 17, 13, 5994, 311, 279, 2885, 5651, 304, 279, 5100, 21029, 44567, 323, 24523, 279, 15967, 609, 12339, 1874, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 2999, 624, 19, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 3216, 5943, 14875, 5022, 311, 3293, 264, 3250, 553, 829, 13, 576, 5036, 7866, 311, 279, 69452, 31969, 304, 279, 1156, 2802, 315, 697, 821, 382, 641, 419, 3110, 11, 582, 1366, 311, 3378, 553, 279, 5643, 3250, 320, 6229, 425, 8, 304, 83298, 1973, 320, 32, 311, 1863, 568, 4636, 26301, 279, 3250, 11, 4205, 389, 279, 10402, 3137, 13, 4695, 979, 498, 470, 311, 279, 45886, 11, 279, 8