{"id": "409", "question": "how to make panko crumbs", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to make panko crumbs:\n\nPassage 1 states to push torn pieces of bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. Then, spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake in a preheated oven until they are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes.\n\nPassage 2 provides similar instructions, stating to push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. Then, spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake at 300°F until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes.\n\nPassage 3 provides additional information, suggesting to preheat the oven to 300°F before making the crumbs. The passage also recommends using a blender carafe to pulse the bread until coarse crumbs form, and then spreading the crumbs evenly on two half-sheet pans and baking until they just begin to brown and are crisp, about 5 minutes. After cooling the crumbs on the pans for 15 to 20 minutes, transfer them to an airtight container and store them at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.\n\nTherefore, to make panko crumbs based on the provided passages, you can use a food processor or blender to shred or pulse bread into coarse crumbs, and then bake them in a preheated oven until they are dry but not toasted.", "pred": "These steps will give you panko crumbs that are ready for use in various recipes.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\n2. Push torn pieces of bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet.\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for about 6 to 8 minutes. Shake the sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\n5. Remove the baking sheet from the oven and allow the crumbs to cool completely.\n\nThese steps will give you panko crumbs that are ready for use in various recipes.", "cot": "[\"To make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\\n2. Push torn pieces of bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet.\\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for about 6 to 8 minutes. Shake the sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\\n5. Remove the baking sheet from the oven and allow the crumbs to cool completely.\\n\\nThese steps will give you panko crumbs that are ready for use in various recipes.\", \"To make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\\n2. Push torn pieces of bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet.\\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, 6 to 8 minutes. Shake the sheet twice during baking in order to evenly dry crumbs.\\n5. Remove from the oven and cool completely.\\n\\nAnswer: Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F. Push torn pieces of bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake at 300 F degrees until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes. Shake the sheet twice during baking. Remove from the oven and cool completely.\", \"To make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat an oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\\n2. Push torn pieces of bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet.\\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes. Shake the sheet twice during baking to evenly dry the crumbs.\\n5. Remove from the oven and cool completely.\\n\\nThese steps are outlined in all three passages provided.\", \"To make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\\n2. Push torn pieces of bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet.\\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for about 6 to 8 minutes. Shake the sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\\n5. Remove the baking sheet from the oven and cool the crumbs completely.\\n6. After cooling, carefully transfer the crumbs to an airtight container and store them at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.\\n\\nRemember to be careful not to let the crumbs brown too much during the baking process.\\n\\nAnswer: Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F, push torn pieces of bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs, spread the crumbs on a baking sheet, bake until dry but not toasted, shake the sheet twice during baking, and remove to cool completely.\"]", "time_sec": 24.799, "generation_time_seconds": 24.7921, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0003, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 281, 92852, 96577, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 20, 15, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 22950, 21145, 9666, 315, 16002, 1526, 279, 52362, 287, 13364, 315, 264, 3607, 17654, 311, 1281, 49247, 96577, 624, 18, 13, 47716, 279, 96577, 389, 264, 27815, 10834, 624, 19, 13, 52074, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 279, 96577, 525, 9058, 714, 537, 92872, 11, 369, 911, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 4420, 13, 72323, 279, 10834, 10917, 2337, 27815, 311, 5978, 1496, 45379, 624, 20, 13, 10783, 279, 27815, 10834, 504, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 96577, 311, 7010, 6587, 382, 9485, 7354, 686, 2968, 498, 281, 92852, 96577, 429, 525, 5527, 369, 990, 304, 5257, 18627, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.3559, -0.0005, -0.0001, 0.0, -0.0002, -0