_len": 618, "output_tokens": 995, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 43.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "653", "question": "how to properly clean your hair", "gt": "To properly clean your hair, first select the appropriate shampoo and conditioner for your hair type. Ensure your water is warm but not too hot, and thoroughly wet your hair. Apply a bit of shampoo into the palm of your hand and work it through the hair. If your hair is long, comb through it with your fingers to reduce tangles rather than piling it on your head. Rinse the hair completely and use a wide-tooth comb to remove any tangles. Apply conditioner in the same manner as the shampoo and let it stay on for a few minutes. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again. Pat dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoid rubbing it with the towel as it can cause damage. For complete drying, a hair dryer can be used.", "pred": "1) Make sure to select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type. 2) While in the shower, make sure your water is warm, but not too hot. Turn the flow down just a bit so you're not splashing all over the place. 3) Thoroughly wet the hair. 4) Apply a bit of shampoo into the palm of your hand (a nickel sized amount is usually just about right) and work it through the hair. If your hair is longer, don't pile it up on your head, instead comb through it with your fingers to reduce tangles. 5) Rinse the hair completely and, if the hair is longer, use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair. 6) Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo. Allow the conditioner to remain on for a few mintues. 7) Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again. 8) Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion. Never rub the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel as this will cause damage to the hair. 9) Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "1) Make sure to select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type. 2) While in the shower, make sure your water is warm, but not too hot. Turn the flow down just a bit so you're not splashing all over the place. 3) Thoroughly wet the hair. 4) Apply a bit of shampoo into the palm of your hand (a nickel sized amount is usually just about right) and work it through the hair. If your hair is longer, don't pile it up on your head, instead comb through it with your fingers to reduce tangles. 5) Rinse the hair completely and, if the hair is longer, use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair. 6) Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo. Allow the conditioner to remain on for a few mintues. 7) Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again. 8) Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion. Never rub the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel as this will cause damage to the hair. 9) Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair.", "cot": "[\"1) Make sure to select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type. 2) While in the shower, make sure your water is warm, but not too hot. Turn the flow down just a bit so you're not splashing all over the place. 3) Thoroughly wet the hair. 4) Apply a bit of shampoo into the palm of your hand (a nickel sized amount is usually just about right) and work it through the hair. If your hair is longer, don't pile it up on your head, instead comb through it with your fingers to reduce tangles. 5) Rinse the hair completely and, if the hair is longer, use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair. 6) Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo. Allow the conditioner to remain on for a few mintues. 7) Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again. 8) Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion. Never rub the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel as this will cause damage to the hair. 9) Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair.\", \"To properly clean your hair, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Select the Proper Shampoo and Conditioner:** Choose a shampoo and conditioner that are suitable for your hair type to ensure effective cleansing.\\n\\n2. **Warm Water:** Make sure the water is warm but not too hot. Adjust the water flow to avoid splashing.\\n\\n3. **Thoroughly Wet the Hair:** Wet your hair thoroughly before applying the shampoo.\\n\\n4. **Apply Shampoo:** Take a small amount of shampoo (about a nickel-sized amount) and work it through your hair. If you have longer hair, comb through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\\n\\n5. **Rinse:** Rinse the shampoo out of your hair completely.\\n\\n6. **Apply Conditioner:** Apply conditioner in the same manner as the shampoo. Allow it to remain on for a few minutes.\\n\\n7. **Rinse Again:** Rinse the conditioner out thoroughly.\\n\\n8. **Dry with a Towel:** Wrap a towel around your hair to soak up excess water. Avoid rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with the towel. Instead, use a patting or stroking motion to dry your hair gently.\\n\\n9. **Use a Hair Dryer:** If necessary, use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can ensure that your hair is thoroughly cleaned and cared for, maintaining its health and appearance.\", \"To properly clean your hair, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\\n2. Make sure the water is warm but not too hot, and turn the flow down to avoid splashing.\\n3. Thoroughly wet your hair.\\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about a nickel-sized amount) and work it through your hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\\n5. Rinse the shampoo thoroughly.\\n6. Apply conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\\n7. Rinse the conditioner thoroughly.\\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion. Avoid rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel to prevent damage.\\n10. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair.\\n\\nAnswer:[Rinse the hair completely, use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair, apply a conditioner, allow it to remain on for a few minutes, rinse with cool water, comb through it again, dry with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoid rubbing with a towel, use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair.]\", \"To properly clean your hair, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\\n2. Ensure the water temperature is warm, but not too hot, and turn the flow down slightly to avoid splashing.\\n3. Thoroughly wet your hair.\\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (a nickel-sized amount is usually sufficient) to your palm and work it through your hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles if your hair is longer.\\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if your hair is longer.\\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing with a towel to prevent damage.\\n10. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair.\\n\\nAnswer: To properly clean your hair, follow the steps outlined above, ensuring you use the right shampoo and conditioner for your hair type, adjust the water temperature, and handle your hair gently during the drying process to avoid damage.\"]", "time_sec": 45.4, "generation_time_seconds": 45.3932, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0006, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [16, 8, 7405, 2704, 311, 3293, 279, 6169, 61932, 323, 64324, 369, 697, 6869, 943, 13, 220, 17, 8, 5976, 304, 279, 17196, 11, 1281, 2704, 697, 