{"id": "717", "question": "how to poach an egg using a poachpod", "gt": "To poach an egg using a PoachPod, first, bring a large pot of water to a boil. Lightly oil the silicone PoachPod, then crack an egg and gently slide it into the PoachPod, taking care not to break the yolk. Float the PoachPod in the boiling water, ensuring it remains upright and no water gets inside. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for about six minutes. After cooking, use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the PoachPod out of the hot water. Finally, flip the PoachPod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate. The PoachPod can be cleaned in a dishwasher.", "pred": "By following these steps, you can successfully poach an egg using a PoachPod, achieving a perfectly cooked egg with a delicate texture and a flavorful runny yolk.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Prepare the Pod**: Lightly oil the silicone PoachPod to prevent the egg from sticking to the pod.\n\n2. **Crack the Egg**: Crack an egg into the oiled PoachPod, ensuring the yolk remains intact.\n\n3. **Float in Boiling Water**: Gently slide the PoachPod, containing the egg, into a pot of boiling water. Make sure the pod stays upright and does not let any water into the pod.\n\n4. **Cook the Egg**: Cover the pot with a tight-fitting lid and let the egg cook for 4-6 minutes. This ensures that the egg cooks evenly and the whites set properly while the yolk remains runny.\n\n5. **Remove and Serve**: After the cooking time, use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the PoachPod out of the hot water. Flip the PoachPod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.\n\nBy following these steps, you can successfully poach an egg using a PoachPod, achieving a perfectly cooked egg with a delicate texture and a flavorful runny yolk.", "cot": "[\"To poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Prepare the Pod**: Lightly oil the silicone PoachPod to prevent the egg from sticking to the pod.\\n\\n2. **Crack the Egg**: Crack an egg into the oiled PoachPod, ensuring the yolk remains intact.\\n\\n3. **Float in Boiling Water**: Gently slide the PoachPod, containing the egg, into a pot of boiling water. Make sure the pod stays upright and does not let any water into the pod.\\n\\n4. **Cook the Egg**: Cover the pot with a tight-fitting lid and let the egg cook for 4-6 minutes. This ensures that the egg cooks evenly and the whites set properly while the yolk remains runny.\\n\\n5. **Remove and Serve**: After the cooking time, use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the PoachPod out of the hot water. Flip the PoachPod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can successfully poach an egg using a PoachPod, achieving a perfectly cooked egg with a delicate texture and a flavorful runny yolk.\", \"To poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\\n2. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the egg's yolk.\\n3. Float the poaching pod in the boiling water, making sure the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod.\\n4. Cover the pot with the lid and let the egg cook for six minutes.\\n5. Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\\n6. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release your poached egg onto the plate.\\n\\nThis process ensures that the egg is poached to perfection, with the yolk remaining intact and the white set properly. The PoachPod's flexibility and nonstick surface make it easy to handle and clean after use.\", \"To poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\\n2. Crack an egg and gently slide the egg into your silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the egg's yolk.\\n3. Carefully float the poaching pod in the boiling water, making sure the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod.\\n4. Cover the pot with the lid and let the egg cook for six minutes.\\n5. Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\\n6. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release your poached egg onto the plate.\\n\\nThese steps ensure that the egg is poached evenly and the yolk remains intact.\", \"To poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps: Bring a large pot of water to a boil. Crack an egg and gently slide it into your silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the egg's yolk. Carefully float the poaching pod in the boiling water, making sure the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod. Cover the pot with the lid and let the egg cook for six minutes. Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the hot water. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release your poached egg onto the plate.\"]", "time_sec": 41.33, "generation_time_seconds": 41.323, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0012, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 3193, 610, 458, 18636, 1667, 264, 13808, 610, 23527, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 50590, 279, 16821, 95518, 8658, 398, 5590, 279, 52925, 13808, 610, 23527, 311, 5358, 279, 18636, 504, 36972, 311, 279, 7509, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 16001, 473, 279, 41213, 95518, 54945, 458, 18636, 1119, 279, 297, 2181, 13808, 610, 23527, 11, 22573, 279, 379, 22604, 8458, 34439, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 5442, 304, 2516, 7979, 9959, 95518, 479, 4402, 14983, 279, 13808, 610, 23527, 11, 8482, 279, 18636, 11, 1119, 264,