{"id": "63", "question": "set default browser to windows", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the given passages, here are the steps to set the default browser to Windows:\n\nMethod 1:\n\n1. Open the Settings app by clicking the Start menu and then clicking the Settings icon, or by using the Windows + I keyboard shortcut.\n2. In the Settings app, click the first option titled System (display, notifications, apps, power).\n3. In the left-pane, click Default apps.\n4. On the right-side, scroll down the page to see Web browser section.\n5. Click on the Edge browser entry (or any browser other than Chrome) to reveal Choose an app, and then click Google Chrome to set it as default browser.\n\nAlternatively, you can also set Mozilla Firefox as your default Windows browser by following these steps:\n\n1. Open your Firefox browser.\n2. Click on the Firefox menu button, represented by three horizontal lines and located in the upper right-hand corner of the browser window.\n3. When the pop-out menu appears, select Options.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "Set the default browser to Windows by opening the Settings app, navigating to the \"System\" section, selecting the \"Web browser\" option, and choosing the desired browser from the list.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To set the default browser to Windows, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open the Settings app by clicking on the Settings icon in the Start menu or using the Windows + I keyboard shortcut.\n2. In the left-pane, click on the \"System\" option.\n3. In the right-side section, scroll down to the \"Web browser\" section.\n4. Click on the current default browser (e.g., Edge) and then click \"Choose an app.\"\n5. Select the desired browser (e.g., Google Chrome) from the list and click \"Choose default app.\"\n\nFor Firefox, follow these steps:\n1. Open your Firefox browser.\n2. Click on the Firefox menu button, represented by three horizontal lines, located in the upper right-hand corner of the browser window.\n3. In the pop-out menu, select \"Options.\"\n\nAnswer: Set the default browser to Windows by opening the Settings app, navigating to the \"System\" section, selecting the \"Web browser\" option, and choosing the desired browser from the list.", "cot": "[\"To set the default browser to Windows, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Open the Settings app by clicking on the Settings icon in the Start menu or using the Windows + I keyboard shortcut.\\n2. In the left-pane, click on the \\\"System\\\" option.\\n3. In the right-side section, scroll down to the \\\"Web browser\\\" section.\\n4. Click on the current default browser (e.g., Edge) and then click \\\"Choose an app.\\\"\\n5. Select the desired browser (e.g., Google Chrome) from the list and click \\\"Choose default app.\\\"\\n\\nFor Firefox, follow these steps:\\n1. Open your Firefox browser.\\n2. Click on the Firefox menu button, represented by three horizontal lines, located in the upper right-hand corner of the browser window.\\n3. In the pop-out menu, select \\\"Options.\\\"\\n\\nAnswer: Set the default browser to Windows by opening the Settings app, navigating to the \\\"System\\\" section, selecting the \\\"Web browser\\\" option, and choosing the desired browser from the list.\", \"Step 1: Open Settings app. To do so, open Start menu and then click Settings icon. Alternatively, you can use Windows + I keyboard shortcut to quickly open Settings app.\\nStep 2: Click the first option titled System (display, notifications, apps, power).\\nStep 3: In the left-pane, click Default apps.\\nStep 4: Now, on the right-side, scroll down the page to see Web browser section.\\nStep 5: Click on the Edge browser entry (or any browser other than Chrome) to reveal Choose an app, and then click Google Chrome to set it as default browser.\\n\\nAnswer:[Set default browser to windows]\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Set the default browser to Windows by following these steps:\\n\\n1. Open the Settings app on your Windows device. You can do this by opening the Start menu and clicking the Settings icon, or using the Windows + I keyboard shortcut.\\n2. Click the first option titled System (display, notifications, apps, power).\\n3. In the left-pane, click Default apps.\\n4. Scroll down the page to see the Web browser section.\\n5. Click on the Edge browser entry to reveal Choose an app, and then click Google Chrome to set it as the default browser.\\n\\nAnswer:[Step 1: Open Settings app. To do so, open Start menu and then click Settings icon. Alternatively, you can use Windows + I keyboard shortcut to quickly open Settings app. Step 2: Click the first option titled System (display, notifications, apps, power). Step 3: In the left-pane, click Default apps. Step 4: Now, on the right-side, scroll down the page to see Web browser section. Step 5: Click on the Edge browser entry (or any browser other than Chrome) to reveal Choose an app, and then click Google Chrome to set it as default browser.]\"]", "time_sec": 20.994, "generation_time_seconds": 20.9879, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0001, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 738, 279, 1638, 6929, 311, 5515, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 5264, 279, 11296, 906, 553, 18458, 389, 279, 11296, 4603, 304, 279, 5145, 5022, 476, 1667, 279, 5515, 488, 358, 13625, 37115, 624, 17, 13, 758, 279, 2115, 38452, 11, 4205, 389, 279, 330, 2320, 1, 2999, 624, 18, 13, 758, 279, 1290, 24067, 3772, 11, 9059, 1495, 311, 279, 330, 5981, 6929, 1, 3772, 624, 19, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 1482, 1638, 6929, 320, 68, 1302, 2572, 10349, 8, 323, 1221, 4205, 330, 24051, 458, 906, 10040, 20, 13, 8427, 279, 12685, 6929, 320, 68, 1302, 2572, 5085, 17225, 8, 504, 279, 1140, 323, 4205, 330, 24051, 1638, 906, 2217, 2461, 25929, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 5264, 697, 25929, 6929, 624, 17, 13, 9189, 38