ations, apps, power). Step 3: In the left-pane, click Default apps. Step 4: Now, on the right-side, scroll down the page to see Web browser section. Step 5: Click on the Edge browser entry (or any browser other than Chrome) to reveal Choose an app, and then click Google Chrome to set it as default browser.]"}], "input_len": 459, "output_tokens": 595, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 16.55, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "77", "question": "how to cook brats", "gt": "To cook brats, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\n3. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\n4. Place the bratwurst in a large pot with onions, butter, and beer.\n5. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n6. Remove the bratwurst from the beer mixture and continue cooking on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally.\n7. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "pred": "To cook brats, pricking them with a fork to prevent them from exploding, place them in a stock pot with onions, butter, and beer, simmer for 15 to 20 minutes, preheat the grill for medium-high heat, lightly oil the grate, and cook the bratwurst on the grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To cook brats, follow these steps:\n\n1. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent it from exploding while cooking.\n2. Place the bratwurst in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer.\n3. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n4. Preheat the grill for medium-high heat, then lightly oil the grate.\n5. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to ensure even browning.\n\nAnswer: To cook brats, pricking them with a fork to prevent them from exploding, place them in a stock pot with onions, butter, and beer, simmer for 15 to 20 minutes, preheat the grill for medium-high heat, lightly oil the grate, and cook the bratwurst on the grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally.", "cot": "[\"To cook brats, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent it from exploding while cooking.\\n2. Place the bratwurst in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer.\\n3. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n4. Preheat the grill for medium-high heat, then lightly oil the grate.\\n5. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to ensure even browning.\\n\\nAnswer: To cook brats, pricking them with a fork to prevent them from exploding, place them in a stock pot with onions, butter, and beer, simmer for 15 to 20 minutes, preheat the grill for medium-high heat, lightly oil the grate, and cook the bratwurst on the grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally.\", \"Answer: To cook bratwurst, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Prick bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\\n2. Place the bratwurst in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer.\\n3. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n4. While the bratwurst is cooking in the beer mixture, reduce the heat to low and continue cooking onions separately.\\n5. Cook the bratwurst on a preheated grill, turning once, for 5 to 10 minutes.\\n6. Serve the bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side.\\n\\nThese steps ensure that the bratwurst is cooked evenly and the onions are browned to perfection.\", \"To cook brats, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent it from exploding while cooking.\\n\\n2. Place the bratwurst in a large stock pot along with onions, butter, and beer.\\n\\n3. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n\\n4. Preheat the grill to medium-high heat.\\n\\n5. Lightly oil the grill grate.\\n\\n6. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to ensure even browning.\\n\\n7. Serve the cooked bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side.\\n\\n8. Alternatively, cook the onions separately by brown them in butter for 1 to 2 minutes, stirring frequently to ensure even browning on all sides.\", \"To cook brats, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\\n2. Place the bratwurst in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer.\\n3. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n4. Preheat a grill for medium-high heat.\\n5. Lightly oil the grill grate.\\n6. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to ensure even browning.\\n\\nThese steps will ensure that the bratwurst is cooked thoroughly and evenly.\"]", "time_sec": 25.381, "generation_time_seconds": 25.3773, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0003, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 1411, 1862, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 2340, 865, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 448, 264, 22435, 311, 5358, 432, 504, 72645, 1393, 17233, 624, 17, 13, 10771, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 264, 3460, 5591, 3338, 448, 44597, 11, 14100, 11, 323, 12883, 624, 18, 13, 10771, 279, 3338, 916, 11051, 8628, 323, 61815, 369, 220, 16, 20, 311, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 624, 19, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 39058, 369, 11051, 27561, 8628, 11, 1221, 33404, 5590, 279, 85354, 624, 20, 13, 12514, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 389, 279, 855, 383, 657, 39058, 369, 220, 16, 15, 311, 220, 16, 19, 4420, 11, 13054, 22930, 311, 5978, 1496, 293, 50420, 382, 16141, 25, 2014, 4296, 1411, 1862, 11, 548, 16272, 1105, 448, 264, 22435, 311, 5358, 1105, 504, 72645, 11, 1992, 1105, 304, 264, 5591, 3338, 448, 44597, 11, 14100, 11, 323, 12883, 11, 61815, 369, 220, 16, 20, 311, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 11, 855, 19963, 279, 39058, 369, 11051, 27561, 8628, 11, 33404, 5590, 279, 85354, 11, 323, 4296, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 389, 279, 39058, 369, 220, 16, 15, 311, 220, 16, 19, 4420, 11, 13054, 22930, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.3156, -0.0032, -0.0003, -0.0351, -0.0286, -0.0352, -0.0056, -0.0193, -0.1115, -0.0008, -0.0, -1.6439, -0.0, -0.143, -0.0, -0.1427, -0.0, 0.0, -0.043, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0006, -0.0007, -3.18, 0.0, -0.0134, -1.1552, -0.0007, -0.0299, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0234, -0.0001, -0.0102, -0.0004,