{"id": "116", "question": "how are water shares transferred", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's how water shares are transferred:\n\n1. Passage 1 states that a fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer. The passage also mentions that a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\n2. Passage 2 outlines the steps required to transfer a Water Stock Certificate: (a) The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate and sign the back of the certificate, (b) the new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership, (c) a fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer, and (d) a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner.\n3. Passage 3 provides general information about buying a home with water shares or rights, including the need to understand the steps involved in transferring water rights into the buyer's name. However, this passage does not provide specific instructions for transferring water shares.\n\nTherefore, based on the provided passages, the answer to the question is:\n\nTransferring water shares involves paying a fee of $75.00 to process the transfer, returning the Water Stock Certificate to the company, providing proof of ownership, and obtaining a new Water Stock Certificate in the new owner's name.", "pred": "The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate, the new owner must provide proof of ownership, and a $75.00 fee must be paid to process the transfer.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To transfer water shares, the following steps are required:\n\n1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate.\n2. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership.\n3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer.\n4. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\n\nAnswer: The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate, the new owner must provide proof of ownership, and a $75.00 fee must be paid to process the transfer.", "cot": "[\"To transfer water shares, the following steps are required:\\n\\n1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate.\\n2. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership.\\n3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer.\\n4. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\\n\\nAnswer: The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate, the new owner must provide proof of ownership, and a $75.00 fee must be paid to process the transfer.\", \"To transfer water shares, the following steps must be taken:\\n\\n1. **Return the Water Stock Certificate**: The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate.\\n2. **Provide Proof of Ownership**: The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership.\\n3. **Pay a Transfer Fee**: A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer of the Water Stock Certificate.\\n4. **Issue a New Water Stock Certificate**: A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\\n\\nThese steps ensure a clear and official transfer of water shares or rights from one owner to another.\", \"To transfer water shares, the following steps are required:\\n\\n1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate. This is necessary to indicate that the seller is relinquishing their rights to the water shares.\\n\\n2. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership. This proof is essential to verify that the new owner is legally entitled to the water shares.\\n\\n3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer. This fee is charged to cover the administrative costs associated with transferring the water shares.\\n\\n4. A new Water Stock Certificate is issued to the new owner of record. This certificate serves as the official documentation of the new owner's ownership of the water shares.\\n\\n5. An additional fee of $75.00 must be paid when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form. This fee is charged to cover the administrative costs associated with replacing a lost certificate.\\n\\nIn summary, the transfer of water shares requires the seller to return and sign the back of the Water Stock Certificate, the new owner to provide proof of ownership, and the payment of a $75.00 fee to process the transfer. A new Water Stock Certificate is issued to the new owner, and an additional $75.00 fee is required for a Lost Certificate Affidavit form.\", \"To transfer water shares, the following steps are required:\\n\\n1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate.\\n2. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership.\\n3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer.\\n4. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\\n5. An additional fee of $75.00 must be paid when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form.\\n\\nThese steps are outlined in the provided passages.\"]", "time_sec": 22.927, "generation_time_seconds": 22.9246, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0002, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 8317, 3015, 13248, 11, 279, 2701, 7354, 525, 2567, 1447, 16, 13, 576, 22856, 1969, 470, 279, 9959, 12648, 31402, 429, 572, 12607, 311, 1105, 323, 1841, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 15748, 624, 17, 13, 576, 501, 6372, 315, 279, 3343, 1969, 3410, 11064, 315, 15278, 624, 18, 13, 362, 11060, 315, 400, 22, 20, 13, 15, 15, 1969, 387, 7171, 311, 1882, 264, 9959, 12648, 31402, 8317, 624, 19, 13, 362, 501, 9959, 12648, 31402, 686, 387, 10897, 311, 279, 501, 6372, 315, 3255, 382, 16141, 25, 