{"id": "185", "question": "how long does it take to make chicken tender in crock pot", "gt": "To make chicken tender in a crock pot, you can cook it on low for 6 - 8 hours or until done. Alternatively, you can cook it on high for 1 hour, then on low for about 5 hours or until done. Another option is cooking it for 4 hours on high.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Step 1: Analyze the passage for information about cooking chicken in a crock pot.\nThe passage mentions cooking chicken in a crock pot, but it does not specify the time it takes to make chicken tender.\n\nStep 2: Look for relevant details in the passage.\nThe passage talks about cooking chicken on low for 6-8 hours or on high for 1 hour, then on low for 5 hours.\n\nStep 3: Evaluate if the information is sufficient to answer the question.\nThe passage provides cooking times but does not specifically mention making chicken tender. It only mentions cooking times for different methods.\n\nStep 4: Consider if there is any additional information provided in other passages.\nAnother passage mentions that chicken breast will always come out tender as long as there is enough moisture, but it does not specify a time.\n\nStep 5: Conclude based on the available information.\nSince the passage does not provide specific information about making chicken tender in a crock pot, and only gives cooking times, we cannot determine the time it takes to make chicken tender based on the given passages.\n\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "[\"Step 1: Analyze the passage for information about cooking chicken in a crock pot.\\nThe passage mentions cooking chicken in a crock pot, but it does not specify the time it takes to make chicken tender.\\n\\nStep 2: Look for relevant details in the passage.\\nThe passage talks about cooking chicken on low for 6-8 hours or on high for 1 hour, then on low for 5 hours.\\n\\nStep 3: Evaluate if the information is sufficient to answer the question.\\nThe passage provides cooking times but does not specifically mention making chicken tender. It only mentions cooking times for different methods.\\n\\nStep 4: Consider if there is any additional information provided in other passages.\\nAnother passage mentions that chicken breast will always come out tender as long as there is enough moisture, but it does not specify a time.\\n\\nStep 5: Conclude based on the available information.\\nSince the passage does not provide specific information about making chicken tender in a crock pot, and only gives cooking times, we cannot determine the time it takes to make chicken tender based on the given passages.\\n\\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Based on the information provided in the passages, it takes 6-8 hours to cook chicken in a crock pot when set on low.\", \"To determine how long it takes to make chicken tender in a crock pot, I'll analyze the information provided in the passages:\\n\\n1. Passage 1 mentions cooking chicken on low for 6-8 hours.\\n2. Passage 2 reinforces this by stating \\\"Cook on low for 6 - 8 hours or until done.\\\"\\n3. Passage 3 provides additional information:\\n   - It mentions cooking chicken breasts on low for 8 hours.\\n   - It also states that chicken breast will come out tender as long as there's enough moisture.\\n\\nBased on this information, we can conclude that the recommended cooking time for chicken in a crock pot is between 6 and 8 hours on low heat. This ensures that the chicken will be tender and cooked through.\\n\\nAnswer: 6-8 hours on low heat in a crock pot.\", \"Based on the information provided in the passage, a chicken breast can be cooked in a crock pot for 8 hours on low heat to make it tender. Additionally, it can be cooked for 4 hours on high heat if time is limited, but it will still turn out tender.\"]", "time_sec": 18.804, "generatio