.6255, -0.5064, -0.0013, -0.0, -0.0, -0.156, -0.3925, -0.016, -0.6301, -0.2318, 0.0, -0.0548, -0.0, -0.0056, -0.2298, -1.1951, -0.0001, -0.0154, -0.4355, -0.0076, -0.0094, -0.415, -0.0028], "cumulative_logprob": -12.455, "norm_logp": -0.0916, "input_len": 597, "output_tokens": 136, "pred": "These steps will result in panko crumbs that can be used in various recipes."}], "input_len": 597, "output_tokens": 707, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 7.84, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "423", "question": "what is a upc description", "gt": "A UPC description refers to the Universal Product Code, which is a barcode symbology used for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item and is mainly used for scanning items at the point of sale.", "pred": "A UPC is a barcode symbology that is widely used in several countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits, which are uniquely assigned to each trade item.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Step 1: Identify the key information about UPC from the passage.\n- The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology.\n- It is widely used in several countries for tracking trade items in stores.\n- UPC consists of 12 numeric digits, which are uniquely assigned to each trade item.\n\nStep 2: Analyze the provided answer.\n- The answer should include the description of UPC as a barcode symbology used for tracking trade items in stores.\n- It should mention that UPC consists of 12 numeric digits, which are uniquely assigned to each trade item.\n\nStep 3: Verify if the answer includes all the details from the passage.\n- The answer includes the correct description of UPC as a barcode symbology used for tracking trade items in stores.\n- It also mentions that UPC consists of 12 numeric digits, which are uniquely assigned to each trade item.\n\nStep 4: Check for any additional information or examples.\n- The answer does not include any specific examples, numbers, or comparisons from the passage.\n- The answer does not mention the related EAN barcode or the use of UPC for scanning trade items at the point of sale as described in the passage.\n\nFinal Answer: A UPC is a barcode symbology that is widely used in several countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits, which are uniquely assigned to each trade item.", "cot": "[\"Step 1: Identify the key information about UPC from the passage.\\n- The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology.\\n- It is widely used in several countries for tracking trade items in stores.\\n- UPC consists of 12 numeric digits, which are uniquely assigned to each trade item.\\n\\nStep 2: Analyze the provided answer.\\n- The answer should include the description of UPC as a barcode symbology used for tracking trade items in stores.\\n- It should mention that UPC consists of 12 numeric digits, which are uniquely assigned to each trade item.\\n\\nStep 3: Verify if the answer includes all the details from the passage.\\n- The answer includes the correct description of UPC as a barcode symbology used for tracking trade items in stores.\\n- It also mentions that UPC consists of 12 numeric digits, which are uniquely assigned to each trade item.\\n\\nStep 4: Check for any additional information or examples.\\n- The answer does not include any specific examples, numbers, or comparisons from the passage.\\n- The answer does not mention the related EAN barcode or the use of UPC for scanning trade items at the point of sale as described in the passage.\\n\\nFinal Answer: A UPC is a barcode symbology that is widely used in several countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits, which are uniquely assigned to each trade item.\", \"Step 1: Identify key information from the passage.\\nThe passage states that the Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology used for tracking trade items in various countries. It consists of 12 numeric digits and is used for scanning at the point of sale.\\n\\nStep 2: Check if there are any additional details about the UPC.\\nThere are no additional details provided about the UPC itself; the passage only describes what it is and its usage.\\n\\nStep 3: Consider if there is any relevant information from the other passages.\\nThe other passages do not provide any information about the UPC.\\n\\nStep 4: Formulate the answer based on the identified information.\\nSince the passage only provides a general description of the UPC, and there is no additional information from the other passages, I cannot provide a more detailed answer.\\n\\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology widely used in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, in Europe and other countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits, and along with the related EAN barcode, it is the barcode mainly used for scanning of trade items at the point of sale, per GS1 specifications.\\n\\nAnswer: A UPC is a barcode symbology used for tracking trade items in stores, consisting of 12 numeric digits, and it is widely used in various countries for scanning items at the point of sale.\", \"The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology widely used in various countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is primarily used for scanning items at the point of sale according to GS1 specifications. The provided passages do not contain specific details about the description of a UPC, but based on the information given, it can be inferred that a UPC is a barcode system for tracking trade items.\"]", "time_sec": 30.857, "generation_time_seconds": 30.8514, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0003, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 1376, 1995, 911, 95129, 504, 279, 21085, 624, 12, 576, 25500, 5643, 6119, 320, 3124, 34, 8, 374, 264, 49407, 66654, 2449, 624, 12, 1084, 374, 13570, 1483, 304, 3807, 5837, 369, 14849, 6559, 3589, 304, 10533, 624, 12, 95129, 17167, 315, 220, 16, 17, 24064, 18509, 11, 892, 525, 41229, 12607, 311, 1817, 6559, 1509, 382, 8304, 220, 17, 25, 37427, 2986, 279, 3897, 4226, 624, 12, 576, 4226, 1265, 2924, 27