{"id": "433", "question": "how to clean tarnished jewelry at home", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to clean tarnished jewelry at home:\n\n1. Mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip a soft cloth to shine silver jewelry that is merely dull or starting to discolor. Rub the jewelry, then rinse in cool water and buff with a cloth until dry.\n2. Use warm soapy water and a soft-bristle brush or old toothbrush to clean diamonds. Pat the jewelry dry with a soft cloth.\n3. Soak tarnished silver jewelry in a saltwater solution of two cups of hot water. This method is gentle and can remove tarnish without abrading the silver. Make sure the gemstones will not be affected by the solution before submerging them.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide information on how to clean other types of jewelry, such as gold or platinum, or what to do if the tarnish is heavy or if the jewelry has intricate designs that may be damaged during cleaning.", "pred": "By following these methods, you can effectively clean your tarnished jewelry at home.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To clean tarnished jewelry at home, you can use various methods depending on the level of tarnish and the type of jewelry. Here are some steps you can follow:\n\n1. **For Lightly Tarnished Jewelry**: Mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip the jewelry in a soft cloth. Rub the jewelry gently, then rinse in cool water and buff with a cloth until dry.\n\n2. **For Heavily Tarnished Jewelry**: Mix a paste of three parts baking soda to one part water. Wet the silver and apply the cleaner with a soft, lint-free cloth.\n\n3. **For Diamonds**: Use warm soapy water and a soft-bristle brush or an old toothbrush. Pat it dry with a soft cloth.\n\n4. **For Jewelry with Gemstones**: Use a saltwater solution. Pour two cups of hot water into a bowl and soak the jewelry for a sufficient amount of time. Ensure the gemstones won't be affected by being submerged in the solution.\n\nBy following these methods, you can effectively clean your tarnished jewelry at home.", "cot": "[\"To clean tarnished jewelry at home, you can use various methods depending on the level of tarnish and the type of jewelry. Here are some steps you can follow:\\n\\n1. **For Lightly Tarnished Jewelry**: Mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip the jewelry in a soft cloth. Rub the jewelry gently, then rinse in cool water and buff with a cloth until dry.\\n\\n2. **For Heavily Tarnished Jewelry**: Mix a paste of three parts baking soda to one part water. Wet the silver and apply the cleaner with a soft, lint-free cloth.\\n\\n3. **For Diamonds**: Use warm soapy water and a soft-bristle brush or an old toothbrush. Pat it dry with a soft cloth.\\n\\n4. **For Jewelry with Gemstones**: Use a saltwater solution. Pour two cups of hot water into a bowl and soak the jewelry for a sufficient amount of time. Ensure the gemstones won't be affected by being submerged in the solution.\\n\\nBy following these methods, you can effectively clean your tarnished jewelry at home.\", \"To clean tarnished jewelry at home, you can use specific cleaning methods depending on the type of metal and the level of tarnish:\\n\\n1. **For Dull or Starting to Discolor Jewelry**:\\n   - Mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water.\\n   - Dip the jewelry in the soapy water and rub it with a soft cloth.\\n   - Rinse the jewelry in cool water.\\n   - Buff the jewelry dry with a cloth.\\n\\n2. **For Heavier Tarnish**:\\n   - Mix a paste of three parts baking soda to one part water.\\n   - Apply the paste to the jewelry using a soft, lint-free cloth.\\n   - Pat dry the jewelry with a soft cloth.\\n\\n3. **For Diamond Jewelry**:\\n   - Use warm soapy water.\\n   - Use a soft-bristle brush or an old toothbrush to clean the diamond.\\n   - Pat the diamond dry with a soft cloth.\\n\\n4. **For Silver Jewelry**:\\n   - Pour two cups of hot water into a bowl.\\n   - Submerge the jewelry in the water to remove tarnish.\\n   - If the jewelry has gemstones, ensure they won't be affected by being submerged in the solution.\\n\\nThese methods help remove tarnish without damaging the jewelry.\", \"To clean tarnished jewelry at home, you can use the following methods:\\n\\n1. For items that are merely dull, filmy, or starting to discolor, mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip in a soft cloth. Rub the jewelry, then rinse in cool water and buff with a cloth until dry.\\n2. For heavier tarnish, mix a paste of three parts baking soda to one part water. Wet the silver and apply the cleaner with a soft, lint-free cloth (not paper towels, which can scratch).\\n3. Pour two cups of hot water into a bowl. You just need enough to cover the jewelry you're cleaning. This method works as a gentle cleanser that removes tarnish without abrading the silver.\\n4. For just one piece of jewelry, use less water. If your jewelry has gemstones, make sure they won't be affected by being submerged in a saltwater solution.\\n\\nBy using these methods, you can effectively clean and restore the shine of your tarnished jewelry at home.\", \"To clean tarnished jewelry at home, you can follow these steps using the methods described in the passages:\\n\\n1. **For Lightly Tarnished Jewelry**: Use a mixture of mild dish soap and warm water. Dampen a soft cloth with the solution and gently rub the jewelry. Rinse it in cool water, and then buff it dry with a soft cloth.\\n\\n2. **For Heavily Tarnished Jewelry**: Prepare a paste by mixing three parts baking soda with one part water. Apply this paste to the tarnished areas with a soft, lint-free cloth. After applying the paste, rinse the jewelry in cool water and dry it with a soft cloth.\\n\\n3. **Alternative Method for Silver Jewelry**: Submerge the jewelry in a bowl of hot water with two cups of salt. This method is gentle and effective for removing tarnish without damaging the silver. For a large amount of jewelry, you can use more water; for a single piece, use less. Ensure that any gemstones on the jewelry will not be affected by the saltwater solution.\\n\\nThese methods should help you clean your tarnished jewelry effectively at home.\"]", "time_sec": 36.395, "generation_time_seconds": 36.3897, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0005, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 4240, 86480, 3304, 30717, 518, 2114, 11, 498, 646, 990, 5257, 5413, 11649, 389, 279, 2188, 315, 86480, 812, 323, 279, 943, 315, 30717, 13, 5692, 525, 1045, 7354, 498, 646, 1795, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 2461, 8658, 398, 350, 1885, 3304, 61868, 95518, 19219, 264, 2421, 21025, 315, 23034, 12000, 26785, 448, 8205, 3015, 323, 23604, 279, 30717, 304, 264, 8413, 27292, 13, 12839, 279, 30717, 29273, 11, 1221, 73241, 304, 7010, 3015, 323, 11522, 448, 264, 27292, 3080, 9058, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 2461, 1260, 402, 1541, 350, 1885, 3304, 61868, 95518, 19219, 264, 24937, 315, 2326, 5479, 27815, 38862, 311, 825, 949, 3015, 13, 44856, 279, 14961, 323, 3796, 279, 31881, 448, 264, 8413, 11, 57920, 12577, 27292, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 2461, 90110, 95518, 5443, 8205, 773, 9667, 3015, 323, 264, 8413, 30117, 28300, 15625, 476, 458, 2310, 25507, 36061, 13, 7135, 432, 9058, 448, 264, 8413, 27292, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 2461, 61868, 448, 31145, 32510, 95518, 5443, 264, 12021, 12987, 6291, 13, 25968, 1378, 25374, 315, 4017, 3015, 1119, 264, 19212, 323, 60692, 279, 30717, 369, 264, 14016, 3311, 315, 882, 13, 29279, 279, 18747, 32510, 2765, 944, 387, 11495, 553, 1660, 84077, 304, 279, 6291, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 5413, 11, 498, 646, 13444, 4240, 697, 86480, 3304, 30717, 518, 2114, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1456, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0002, 0.0, -0.0014, -0.2326, -0.0008, -0.3641, -1.7999, -0.0004, -0.1087, 0.0, -0.0, -1.0311, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.3956, -0.0019, -0.0177, 0.0, -0.0357, -0.6588, 