{"id": "478", "question": "change of address u.s. postal service", "gt": "Passage 3 provides information on how to change your address with the U.S. Postal Service. You can visit their website, call the USPS Call Center, or fill out and submit a form at a U.S. Post Office.", "pred": "The U.S. Postal Service allows you to change your address quickly and securely. You can do this in as little as one minute by visiting https://moversguide.usps.com/, calling the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or filling out and submitting PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office. The service is versatile, allowing you to notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service. It's also secure, with the latest encryption technologies ensuring your data is safe.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "The U.S. Postal Service allows you to change your address quickly and securely. You can do this in as little as one minute by visiting https://moversguide.usps.com/, calling the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or filling out and submitting PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office. The service is versatile, allowing you to notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service. It's also secure, with the latest encryption technologies ensuring your data is safe.", "cot": "[\"The U.S. Postal Service allows you to change your address quickly and securely. You can do this in as little as one minute by visiting https://moversguide.usps.com/, calling the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or filling out and submitting PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office. The service is versatile, allowing you to notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service. It's also secure, with the latest encryption technologies ensuring your data is safe.\", \"Step 1: Understand the question - The question asks about changing an address with the U.S. Postal Service.\\nStep 2: Analyze the passages for relevant information - All three passages provide information about changing addresses with the U.S. Postal Service.\\nStep 3: Identify key details - \\n- The process can be done quickly (as little as 1 minute).\\n- It can notify up to 100 organizations.\\n- It is secure with encryption technologies.\\n- The form can be completed online.\\n- There are three ways to change the address: visiting the website, calling the call center, or filling out and submitting PS Form 3575.\\n- The form can be submitted at any U.S. Post Office.\\nStep 4: Formulate the answer - Based on the information provided in the passages, here is the answer:\\n\\nThe U.S. Postal Service offers a Change of Address service that can be completed quickly, securely, and with multiple methods. You can change your address online, visit the website, call the call center, or fill out and submit PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office. The process can notify up to 100 organizations and is secure with encryption technologies.\\n\\nAnswer: The U.S. Postal Service offers a Change of Address service that can be completed quickly, securely, and with multiple methods. You can change your address online, visit the website, call the call center, or fill out and submit PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office. The process can notify up to 100 organizations and is secure with encryption technologies.\", \"Step 1: Identify the main points from the passages about changing the address with the U.S. Postal Service.\\n\\n- Fast and versatile: The service allows changing the address in as little as 1 minute and notifying up to 100 organizations.\\n- Secure: The latest encryption technologies ensure data security.\\n- Categorized forms: Forms are categorized for easy access.\\n- Online form: You can complete the U.S. Postal Service Official Change of Address form online.\\n- Business mail forwarding: The feature is important for businesses moving due to disasters.\\n- Three ways to change the address: Visit the website, call the USPS Call Center, or fill out and submit PS Form 3575.\\n\\nStep 2: Formulate the answer based on the information provided.\\n\\nAnswer: Changing the address with the U.S. Postal Service is fast, versatile, and secure. You can complete the change of address form online and use the service for business mail forwarding. There are three ways to change your address: visiting the website, calling the USPS Call Center, or filling out and submitting PS Form 3575.\", \"To change your address with the U.S. Postal Service, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Online**: You can complete the U.S. Postal Service Official Change of Address form online. This option is quick and easy, allowing you to complete the form from your computer or mobile device.\\n\\n2. **Phone**: Call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777). This option is convenient if you prefer to speak to a representative.\\n\\n3. **Form**: Fill out and submit PS Form 3575, which you can pick up at any U.S. Post Office or request by mail. This form allows you to provide the necessary details to change your address.\\n\\nEach of these methods ensures that your mail is forwarded to the new address, and the process is secure with encryption technologies to protect your data.\"]", "time_sec": 38.662, "generation_time_seconds": 38.6554, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0005, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 547, 808, 13, 54217, 5362, 6147, 498, 311, 2297, 697, 2621, 6157, 323, 51023, 13, 1446, 646, 653, 419, 304, 438, 2632, 438, 825, 9383, 553, 16721, 3703, 1110, 76, 8969, 48370, 21916, 1690, 905, 34545, 8098, 279, 84876, 7143, 5832, 518, 220, 16, 12, 23, 15, 15, 12, 7384, 32340, 5012, 320, 16, 12, 23, 15, 15, 12, 17, 22, 20, 12, 23, 22, 22, 22, 701, 476, 21274, 700, 323, 33094, 11405, 3377, 220, 18, 20, 22, 20, 518, 894, 547, 808, 13, 3877, 8246, 13, 576, 2473, 374, 31945, 11, 10693, 498, 311, 15456, 705, 311, 220, 16, 15, 15, 1