{"id": "719", "question": "how to poach an egg using a poachpod", "gt": "To poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\n\n1. Begin by bringing a large pot of water to a boil.\n2. Gently slide an egg into your silicone poaching pod, taking care not to break the egg's yolk.\n3. Float the poaching pod in the boiling water, ensuring that the pod stays upright and no water gets inside.\n4. Cover the pot with a tight-fitting lid and allow the egg to cook for 6 minutes.\n5. After 6 minutes, remove the lid from the pot and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to carefully lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\n6. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.", "pred": "To poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\n1. Lightly oil the PoachPod.\n2. Crack the egg into the PoachPod.\n3. Float the PoachPod in a saucepan of simmering water.\n4. Cover the pan with a tight-fitting lid.\n5. Cook for about 4-6 minutes.\n6. Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the PoachPod out of the hot water.\n7. Flip the PoachPod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\n1. Lightly oil the PoachPod.\n2. Crack the egg into the PoachPod.\n3. Float the PoachPod in a saucepan of simmering water.\n4. Cover the pan with a tight-fitting lid.\n5. Cook for about 4-6 minutes.\n6. Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the PoachPod out of the hot water.\n7. Flip the PoachPod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.", "cot": "[\"To poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\\n1. Lightly oil the PoachPod.\\n2. Crack the egg into the PoachPod.\\n3. Float the PoachPod in a saucepan of simmering water.\\n4. Cover the pan with a tight-fitting lid.\\n5. Cook for about 4-6 minutes.\\n6. Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the PoachPod out of the hot water.\\n7. Flip the PoachPod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.\", \"To poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Prepare the Pod**: Lightly oil the PoachPod before cracking the egg into it. Make sure the pod is ready and clean.\\n\\n2. **Boil Water**: Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\\n\\n3. **Insert the Egg**: Crack an egg and gently slide it into the PoachPod, taking care not to break the yolk.\\n\\n4. **Float the Pod**: Float the PoachPod in the boiling water, ensuring it stays upright and no water gets into the pod.\\n\\n5. **Cook the Egg**: Cover the pot with a tight-fitting lid and let the egg cook for approximately 4-6 minutes.\\n\\n6. **Remove the Pod**: Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the PoachPod out of the hot water.\\n\\n7. **Release the Egg**: Flip the PoachPod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.\\n\\nThis method ensures that the egg is poached to perfection, with the yolk remaining intact and the whites fully cooked.\", \"To poach an egg using a PoachPod, start by bringing a large pot of water to a boil. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, ensuring the yolk is not broken. Carefully float the poaching pod in the boiling water, making sure it stays upright and no water gets into the pod. Cover the pot with a tight-fitting lid and let the egg cook for six minutes. Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the hot water. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release your poached egg onto the plate.\", \"Step 1: Identify the key steps for poaching an egg using a PoachPod from the provided passages.\\n\\nStep 2: The instructions in the passages are quite similar, so I'll use the general information provided.\\n\\nStep 3: Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\\n\\nStep 4: Crack an egg and gently slide the egg into your silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the egg's yolk.\\n\\nStep 5: Float the poaching pod in the boiling water, making sure the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod.\\n\\nStep 6: Cover the pot with the lid and let the egg cook for six minutes.\\n\\nStep 7: Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\\n\\nStep 8: Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release your poached egg onto the plate.\\n\\nAnswer: To poach an egg using a PoachPod, bring a large pot of water to a boil. Crack an egg and gently slide the egg into your silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the egg's yolk. Float the poaching pod in the boiling water, making sure the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod. Cover the pot with the lid and let the egg cook for six minutes. Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the hot water. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release your poached egg onto the plate.\"]", "time_sec": 44.967, "generation_time_seconds": 44.9589, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0006, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 3193, 610, 458, 18636, 1667, 264, 13808, 610, 23527, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 8658, 398, 5590, 279, 13808, 610, 23527, 624, 17, 13, 54945, 279, 18636, 1119, 279, 13808, 610, 23527, 624, 18, 13, 13001, 279, 13808, 610, 23527, 304, 264, 19187, 848, 315, 61815, 287, 3015, 624, 19, 13, 17757, 279, 7215, 448, 264, 10296, 2220, 14810, 26334, 624, 20, 13, 12514, 369, 911, 220, 19, 12, 21, 4420, 624, 21, 13, 10783, 279, 26334, 323, 990, 264, 3460, 1739, 15521, 45