gen into and carbon dioxide out of the lungs, and circulation, which is the transport of oxygen taken into the body during ventilation to where it is needed in the body. The ventilation component takes center stage in enhancing therapeutic back exercise programs or successful participation in a proactive holistic therapy."}], "input_len": 440, "output_tokens": 842, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 53.66, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "27", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "gt": "To fix a door that won't lock, first try to align the door latch with the hole in the strike plate. If the latch is misaligned, you can perform a lipstick test to see where the latch contacts the strike plate. If it contacts too high or too low, tighten all the door's hinge screws. You may also need to enlarge the latch hole in the jamb or move the strike plate. If this doesn't work, shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb, pry it up until it comes loose and remove it. Replace the door stop back on the jamb, set back 1/4 inch from its original location. Nail the side and top piece of the door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "pred": "If the door still won't lock after these steps, you may need to enlarge the latch hole in the jamb or move the strike plate to ensure proper alignment. Tighten the hinges first, and then enlarge the strike plate hole if necessary.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To fix a door that won't lock, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Shut the door and try to lock it**: If the door won't lock, open it and proceed to the next steps.\n\n2. **Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb**: Use a chisel to gently tap and pry under the door stop until it becomes loose.\n\n3. **Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it**: Continue prying until the door stop is completely removed.\n\n4. **Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well**: Remove the door stop from the top as well.\n\n5. **Set the door stop back on the jamb**: Place the door stop back on the jamb.\n\n6. **Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location**: Adjust the door stop to be set back 1/4 inch from its original position.\n\n7. **Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on**: Secure the side and top pieces of the door stop back onto the jamb with nails.\n\n8. **Adjust the door stop alignment**: Ensure the door stop is properly aligned by checking for a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off. Align the door stop accordingly.\n\n9. **Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on again**: Double-check and nail the side and top pieces of the door stop back on.\n\n10. **Close the door and test the lock**: After securing the door stop, close the door and test if it locks properly.\n\nIf the door still won't lock after these steps, you may need to enlarge the latch hole in the jamb or move the strike plate to ensure proper alignment. Tighten the hinges first, and then enlarge the strike plate hole if necessary.", "cot": "[\"To fix a door that won't lock, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Shut the door and try to lock it**: If the door won't lock, open it and proceed to the next steps.\\n\\n2. **Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb**: Use a chisel to gently tap and pry under the door stop until it becomes loose.\\n\\n3. **Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it**: Continue prying until the door stop is completely removed.\\n\\n4. **Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well**: Remove the door stop from the top as well.\\n\\n5. **Set the door stop back on the jamb**: Place the door stop back on the jamb.\\n\\n6. **Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location**: Adjust the door stop to be set back 1/4 inch from its original position.\\n\\n7. **Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on**: Secure the side and top pieces of the door stop back onto the jamb with nails.\\n\\n8. **Adjust the door stop alignment**: Ensure the door stop is properly aligned by checking for a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off. Align the door stop accordingly.\\n\\n9. **Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on again**: Double-check and nail the side and top pieces of the door stop back on.\\n\\n10. **Close the door and test the lock**: After securing the door stop, close the door and test if it locks properly.\\n\\nIf the door still won't lock after these steps, you may need to enlarge the latch hole in the jamb or move the strike plate to ensure proper alignment. Tighten the hinges first, and then enlarge the strike plate hole if necessary.\", \"To fix a door that won't lock, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\\n2. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\\n3. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\\n4. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\\n5. Align the door stop back on the jamb, setting it back 1/4 inch from its original location.\\n6. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\\n7. Check if the door now shuts and locks normally.\\n\\nIf the door still won't lock, you may need to:\\n1. Tighten the hinges first.\\n2. Enlarge the strike plate hole.\\n3. Move the strike plate.\\n4. If the latch still doesn't align with the hole in the strike plate, use the \\\"lipstick test\\\" to find the misalignment.\\n5. If the latch contacts the strike plate too high or too low, make sure all the door's hinge screws are tight.\\n\\nAnswer: Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Align the door stop back on the jamb, setting it back 1/4 inch from its original location. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. Check if the door now shuts and locks normally. If the door still won't lock, tighten the hinges first, enlarge the strike plate hole, move the strike plate, and use the \\\"lipstick test\\\" to find the misalignment. Make sure all the door's hinge screws are tight.\", \"To fix a door that won't lock, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Shut the door and try to lock it.** If it won't lock, open the door.\\n2. **Use a chisel** to tap the end under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\\n3. **Pry up on it** until it comes loose and remove it.\\n4. **Remove the door stop on top as well.**\\n5. **Reattach the door stop** back on the jamb.\\n6. **Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.**\\n7. **Align the door stop** using the distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off.\\n8. **Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.**\\n9. **Test the door** to ensure it shuts and locks normally.\\n\\nIf the door latch doesn't align with the hole in the strike plate, you may need to:\\n1. **Tighten the hinges first.**\\n2. **Enlarge the strike plate hole.**\\n3. **Move the strike plate.**\\n4. **Perform the \\\"lipstick test\\\"** to check if the latch contacts the strike plate too high or too low.\\n5. **Ensure all the door's hinge screws are tight.**\\n\\nIf these steps do not resolve the issue, consider consulting a professional locksmith for further assistance.\", \"Answer: To fix a door that won't lock, first shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door. Use a chisel to remove the door stop on the striker side of the jamb and tap it under the door stop until it comes loose. Remove the door stop on top as well. Lace the door stop back on the jamb, setting it back 1/4 inch from its original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off. Use this line to align the door stop and nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.\"]", "time_sec": 45.213, "generation_time_seconds": 45.168, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0021, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 2016, 332, 279, 6006, 323, 1430, 311