{"id": "78", "question": "how to cook brats", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how to cook brats:\n\nStep 1: Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n\nStep 2: Lightly oil the grate.\n\nStep 3: Combine beer and onions in a large pot, bring to a boil, and submerge the bratwurst. Add red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper.\n\nStep 4: Simmer the bratwurst in the beer mixture for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly.\n\nStep 5: Remove the bratwurst from the beer mixture and grill it on the preheated grill for an additional 5 to 10 minutes, turning occasionally, until browned and cooked through.\n\nStep 6: Serve the bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side dish.\n\nNote: It's important to prick the bratwurst with a fork before cooking to prevent them from exploding while cooking. Also, cooked bratwurst can be stored in the fridge for up to 5 days or frozen for up to 3 months.", "pred": "Cook brats by preheating the grill, adding beer and onions to a pot, cooking the bratwurst in the beer, and grilling the bratwurst.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To cook brats, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. When hot, lightly oil the grill grate.\n3. Combine the beer and onions in a large pot; bring to a boil.\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer; add the red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper.\n5. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding during cooking.\n6. Place the bratwurst in the pot with the onions, butter, and beer.\n7. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n8. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning once, for 5 to 10 minutes.\n9. Serve the bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side.\n\nAnswer: Cook brats by preheating the grill, adding beer and onions to a pot, cooking the bratwurst in the beer, and grilling the bratwurst.", "cot": "[\"To cook brats, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\\n2. When hot, lightly oil the grill grate.\\n3. Combine the beer and onions in a large pot; bring to a boil.\\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer; add the red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper.\\n5. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding during cooking.\\n6. Place the bratwurst in the pot with the onions, butter, and beer.\\n7. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n8. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning once, for 5 to 10 minutes.\\n9. Serve the bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side.\\n\\nAnswer: Cook brats by preheating the grill, adding beer and onions to a pot, cooking the bratwurst in the beer, and grilling the bratwurst.\", \"Step 1: Identify the main steps for cooking brats from the passages.\\n\\nFrom passage 1, we have:\\n1. Prepare the bratwurst by pricking it with a fork.\\n2. Place the bratwurst in a large pot with onions, butter, and beer.\\n3. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n4. Preheat the grill to medium-high heat.\\n5. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 5 to 10 minutes, turning once.\\n\\nFrom passage 2, we have:\\n1. Preheat the grill to medium-high heat.\\n2. Place the bratwurst on the preheated grill and cook for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly.\\n\\nStep 2: Combine the steps to create a comprehensive cooking method for brats.\\n\\n1. Prepare the bratwurst by pricking it with a fork to prevent it from exploding during cooking.\\n2. Place the bratwurst in a large pot with onions, butter, and beer.\\n3. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n4. Preheat the grill to medium-high heat.\\n5. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 5 to 10 minutes, turning once.\\n\\nStep 3: Provide the final answer.\\n\\nAnswer: To cook brats, prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent it from exploding during cooking. Place the bratwurst in a large pot with onions, butter, and beer. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes. Preheat the grill to medium-high heat and cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 5 to 10 minutes, turning once.\", \"To cook brats, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Prick bratwurst with a fork**: This step is crucial to prevent the brats from exploding as they cook. This is mentioned in passage 2.\\n\\n2. **Combine bratwurst, onions, butter, and beer**: Place the pricked bratwurst in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer. This step is described in both passages 2 and 3.\\n\\n3. **Simmer over medium heat for 15 to 20 minutes**: Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes. This step is mentioned in passage 2.\\n\\n4. **Preheat grill for medium-high heat**: Prepare the grill for cooking. This step is mentioned in passage 2 and passage 3.\\n\\n5. **Cook bratwurst on preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly**: Cook the bratwurst on the grill, turning them to ensure even browning. This step is detailed in passage 3.\\n\\n6. **Serve with beer mixture**: Serve the cooked bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side. This step is mentioned in passage 1.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can cook brats effectively.\", \"To cook brats, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\\n2. Lightly oil the grill grate.\\n3. Combine the beer and onions in a large pot; bring to a boil.\\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture, along with onions, butter, and beer.\\n5. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding during cooking.\\n6. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n7. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning once, for 5 to 10 minutes.\\n8. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.\\n\\nAnswer: To cook brats, preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat, lightly oil the grill grate, combine beer and onions in a large pot, submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture, prick the bratwurst, place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes, cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 5 to 10 minutes, and serve with the beer mixture.\"]", "time_sec": 39.04, "generation_time_seconds": 39.0343, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0005, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 1411, 1862, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 27561, 8628, 624, 17, 13, 3197, 4017, 11, 33404, 5590, 279, 39058, 85354, 624, 18, 13, 46812, 279, 12883, 323, 44597, 304, 264, 3460, 3338, 26, 4446, 311, 264, 43690, 624, 19, 13, 3719, 19052, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 279, 12883, 26, 912, 279, 2518, 24353, 81623, 11, 30635, 16723, 11, 12021, 11, 323, 24353, 624, 20, 13, 2340, 865, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 448, 264, 22435, 311, 5358, 1105, 504, 72645, 2337, 17233, 624, 21, 13, 10771, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 279, 3338, 448, 279, 44597, 11, 14100, 11, 323, 12883, 624, 22, 13, 10771, 279, 3338, 916, 11051, 8628, 323, 61815, 369, 220, 16, 20, 311, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 624, 23, 13, 12514, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 389, 279, 855, 383, 657, 39058, 11, 13054, 3055, 11, 369, 220, 20, 311, 220, 16, 15, 4420, 624, 24, 13, 52932, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 448, 279, 12883, 20980, 438, 264, 60276, 476, 3108, 382, 16141, 25, 12514, 1411, 1862, 553, 855, 383, 1095, 279, 39058, 11, 7842, 12883, 323, 44597, 311, 264, 3338, 11, 17233, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 279, 12883, 11, 323, 1081, 9400, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.3156, -0.0032, -0.0003, -0.0351, -0.0286, -0.0352, -0.0056, -0.0193, -0.1115, -0.0008, -0.0, -1.0189, -0.0, -0.1008, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0528, -0.0, -0.0, 0.0, -0.4922, -0.0013, -0.0, -1.1225, -0.3024, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0055, -1.5023, -0.0011, -0.0008, -0.0, 0.0, -0.3009, -0.1429, -0.010