ive_logprob": -23.2527, "norm_logp": -0.0938, "input_len": 600, "output_tokens": 248, "pred": "To cook brats, preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat, lightly oil the grill grate, combine beer and onions in a large pot, submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture, prick the bratwurst, place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes, cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 5 to 10 minutes, and serve with the beer mixture."}], "input_len": 600, "output_tokens": 1131, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 16.81, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "89", "question": "how to prepare blood slide", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the given passages, here are the steps to prepare a blood slide:\n\n1. Sterilize the needle with a flame before using it to prick your finger or obtain blood from another source.\n2. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n3. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n4. Hold another clean slide at an angle of about 45 degrees and gently touch the blood with one end of the slide, allowing the blood to run along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\n5. Carefully push the slide along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n6. Repeat step 4 and 5 to make two smears.\n7. Allow the slides to air dry.\n8. Label the slides clearly once they are dry.\n9. Place the slides in provided slide transport containers.\n\nNote: It is important to avoid coming into contact with another person's blood, and to wear rubber gloves if it is unavoidable.", "pred": "These steps ensure that the blood is evenly spread out on the slide, which is necessary for observation and analysis.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\n\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide, allowing the blood to run along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\n5. Push the second slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n6. Make 2 smears and allow them to air dry.\n7. Label the smears clearly.\n8. Once dried, place the smears in the provided slide transport containers.\n\nThese steps ensure that the blood is evenly spread out on the slide, which is necessary for observation and analysis.", "cot": "[\"To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide, allowing the blood to run along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n5. Push the second slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n6. Make 2 smears and allow them to air dry.\\n7. Label the smears clearly.\\n8. Once dried, place the smears in the provided slide transport containers.\\n\\nThese steps ensure that the blood is evenly spread out on the slide, which is necessary for observation and analysis.\", \"To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.** This ensures that the slide is clean and ready for the blood sample.\\n2. **Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.** This drop of blood will serve as the starting point for the smear.\\n3. **Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.** This倾斜滑动滑动滑动\\n4. **Touch the blood with one end of the second slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.** This process allows the blood to spread out in a thin line.\\n5. **Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.** This ensures that the blood is spread evenly across the slide.\\n6. **Make 2 smears, allow to air dry, and label clearly.** This step ensures that the slide is ready for examination and that any necessary identification is made.\\n7. **Once dried, place in the provided slide transport containers.** This is to keep the slide in a controlled environment and prevent contamination.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can prepare a blood slide for examination.\", \"To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n5. Push the slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n6. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\\n7. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.\\n\\nThese steps ensure that the blood is spread out evenly on the slide for examination.\", \"To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the second slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n5. Push the second slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n6. Make two smears, allowing them to air dry.\\n7. Label the slides clearly once they are dried.\\n8. Place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.\\n\\nThese steps ensure that the blood smear is properly prepared for examination.\"]", "time_sec": 24.639, "generation_time_seconds": 24.6335, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0004, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 10549, 264, 6543, 14983, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 10771, 264, 4240, 8991, 14983, 389, 264, 10063, 7329, 624, 17, 13, 2691, 825, 2613, 5943, 315, 6543, 311, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 624, 18, 13, 11778, 2441, 4240, 14983, 323, 3331, 432, 518, 458, 9210, 315, 911, 220, 19, 20, 12348, 624, 19, 13, 19338, 279, 6543, 448, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 11, 10693, 279, 6543, 311, 1598, 3156, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 14983, 553, 2062, 34505, 1917, 624, 20, 13, 22950, 279, 2086, 14983, 15516, 3156, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 1156, 14983, 311, 8193, 264, 15430, 80503, 315, 6