, -0.0032, -2.0187, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0046, -0.1908, -0.4166], "cumulative_logprob": -49.3617, "norm_logp": -0.3164, "input_len": 447, "output_tokens": 156, "pred": "Building a lean-to shed involves a series of steps. First, the foundation is prepared by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Next, two 4 x 4 skids are cut to a length of 70 2/4 inches and set at the site. Two 2 x 6 rim joists are then cut to a length of 7 3/4 inches, and six joists are cut to a length of 44 3/4 inches. These materials are assembled to form the floor, which is then set on the skids. The floor is checked for square, and then anchored to the skids using four joist clip angles. The walls of the shed are constructed separately and raised onto the frame."}], "input_len": 447, "output_tokens": 895, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 25.6, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "138", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the Income Tax Act, when an asset is discarded but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded as per section 43(6). This is done under the block concept, where all assets of the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are considered as a single asset. Any changes to the block's value must abide by the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961. Additionally, the assessee can claim depreciation on the residual value of such discarded asset, even if it's not used for the purposes of business or profession in that year and subsequent years.", "pred": "In summary, the Income Tax Act allows for the adjustment of the block value of an asset if it is discarded, using the scrap value as a reduction. This ensures that the depreciation is calculated accurately based on the remaining value of the asset.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "The treatment of an asset discarded by a business according to the Income Tax Act is as follows:\n\n1. **Block Concept Application**: Assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are clubbed together and considered as a single asset. This is known as the block concept.\n\n2. **Discard Value Adjustment**: If an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act permits the scrap value of the asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded.\n\n3. **Depreciation Calculation**: Depreciation is calculated based on the residual value of the discarded asset, which is the opening worth-depreciable value (WDV) of the asset minus its scrap value. The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on this residual value even if the discarded asset is not used for the purposes of business or profession in the current year and subsequent years.\n\nIn summary, the Income Tax Act allows for the adjustment of the block value of an asset if it is discarded, using the scrap value as a reduction. This ensures that the depreciation is calculated accurately based on the remaining value of the asset.", "cot": "[\"The treatment of an asset discarded by a business according to the Income Tax Act is as follows:\\n\\n1. **Block Concept Application**: Assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are clubbed together and considered as a single asset. This is known as the block concept.\\n\\n2. **Discard Value Adjustment**: If an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act permits the scrap value of the asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded.\\n\\n3. **Depreciation Calculation**: Depreciation is calculated based on the residual value of the discarded asset, which is the opening worth-depreciable value (WDV) of the asset minus its scrap value. The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on this residual value even if the discarded asset is not used for the purposes of business or profession in the current year and subsequent years.\\n\\nIn summary, the Income Tax Act allows for the adjustment of the block value of an asset if it is discarded, using the scrap value as a reduction. This ensures that the depreciation is calculated accurately based on the remaining value of the asset.\", \"First, let's break down the passage and the question step by step:\\n\\n1. **Understanding the passage**: The passage discusses the treatment of assets when they are discarded in the context of the Income Tax Act. It mentions two key points:\\n   - **Section 43(6)**: This section allows the scrap value of an asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year when the asset is discarded.\\n   - **Block concept**: All assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are considered as a single asset.\\n\\n2. **Analyzing the question**: The question asks about the treatment of an asset when it is discarded, focusing on how it is treated under the Income Tax Act.\\n\\n3. **Connecting the passage to the question**: The passage directly addresses what happens when an asset is discarded by mentioning the reduction of the scrap value from the block in the previous year.\\n\\n4. **Formulating the answer**: Based on the information provided in the passage, when an asset is discarded, the scrap value of the asset is reduced from the block in the previous year.\\n\\nAnswer: When an asset is discarded, the scrap value of the asset is reduced from the block in the previous year according to the Income Tax Act.\", \"According to the passage, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset is reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This is in accordance with section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961. The block concept is mentioned, where all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are considered as a single asset. Any alterations to the value of the block have to be strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961. The passage also mentions that the assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of such discarded asset, even though such discarded asset is not used for the purposes of business or profession in such year and subsequent years.\", \"Step 1: Identify the relevant information from the passages.\\n- Passage 1 discusses the block concept in the Income Tax Act.\\n- Passage 3 explains the treatment of depreciation when an asset is discarded.\\n- Passage 2 provides an illustration for understanding the income before depreciation and tax.\\n\\nStep 2: Analyze the key points related to the treatment of an asset discarded.\\n- According to Passage 1, if an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year.\\n- Passage 3 states that the assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, even if the asset is not used for the purposes of business or profession in subsequent years.\\n\\nStep 3: Formulate the answer based on the analysis.\\n- The treatment of an asset discarded as per the Income Tax Act involves reducing the asset's value in the block from the previous year if it is not sold. Additionally, the assessee can claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset.\\n\\nAnswer: The treatment of an asset discarded as per the Income Tax Act involves reducing the asset's value in the block from the previous year if it is not sold. Additionally, the assessee can claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset.\"]", "time_sec": 30.354, "generation_time_seconds": 30.3499, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0002, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 6380, 315, 458, 9329, 43210, 553, 264, 2562, 4092, 311, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 374, 438, 11017, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 4713, 34355, 7323, 95518, 40638, 15679, 2878, 279, 1852, 536, 323, 3832, 311, 279, 1852, 4379, 315, 93089, 525, 6335, 2721, 3786, 323, 6509, 438, 264, 3175, 9329, 13, 1096, 374, 3881, 438, 279, 2504, 7286, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 23477, 567, 5162, 91949, 95518, 1416, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 28690, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 311, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 279, 9329, 374, 43210, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 7839, 2758, 7101, 74216, 95518, 4148, 2758, 7101, 374, 16588, 3118, 389, 279, 32147, 897, 315, 279, 43210, 9329, 11, 892, 374, 279, 8568, 5802, 6810, 10645, 2156, 897, 320, 17563, 53, 8, 315, 279, 9329, 2