{"id": "158", "question": "how to factory reset a htc one vx", "gt": "To factory reset an HTC One VX, you can follow the steps mentioned in passage 3. Slide the Notifications panel open, tap on Storage, then Factory data reset, and finally tap on Reset phone and Erase everything.", "pred": "", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To factory reset an HTC One VX, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Switch off the device:** Use the Power button to turn off the device. \n2. **Access the Bootloader Mode:** Press and hold the Volume Down and Power buttons together for a couple of seconds until the Bootloader Mode menu appears. \n3. **Navigate to Factory Reset:** Use the Volume buttons to scroll through the menu and select the Factory Reset option. \n4. **Confirm Factory Reset:** Press and hold the Volume Down and Power buttons again for a couple of seconds to confirm the Factory Reset. \n5. **Wait for Completion:** The device will restart and the factory reset process will begin. This may take some time. \n\nAfter the process is complete, your HTC One VX will be reset to its factory settings. \n\nAnswer: [Please think step by step, and then provide your final answer.]", "cot": "[\"To factory reset an HTC One VX, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Switch off the device:** Use the Power button to turn off the device. \\n2. **Access the Bootloader Mode:** Press and hold the Volume Down and Power buttons together for a couple of seconds until the Bootloader Mode menu appears. \\n3. **Navigate to Factory Reset:** Use the Volume buttons to scroll through the menu and select the Factory Reset option. \\n4. **Confirm Factory Reset:** Press and hold the Volume Down and Power buttons again for a couple of seconds to confirm the Factory Reset. \\n5. **Wait for Completion:** The device will restart and the factory reset process will begin. This may take some time. \\n\\nAfter the process is complete, your HTC One VX will be reset to its factory settings. \\n\\nAnswer: [Please think step by step, and then provide your final answer.]\", \"To factory reset an HTC One VX, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Switch off the device**: Hold down the Power button for a while to turn the device off.\\n2. **Access Bootloader Mode**: Press and hold the Volume Down + Power key for a couple of seconds. This will bring up the Bootloader Mode menu.\\n3. **Select Factory Reset**: From the Bootloader Mode menu, use the Volume buttons to scroll and the Power key to select the option for \\\"Factory Reset\\\".\\n4. **Confirm Factory Reset**: Press and hold the Volume Down + Power key for a couple of seconds again to confirm the factory reset.\\n\\nAfter following these steps, your HTC One VX will be reset to its factory settings.\", \"1. First, switch off the phone by using the Power rocker.\\n2. After that, press and hold Volum Down and Power buttons together for a couple of seconds.\\n3. You can release all keys when the Bootloader Mode appears on the screen.\\n4. Choose the Factory Reset by pressing the Volum Down button to scroll and Power key to select.\\n5. Then press and hold the Volume Down + Power key for a couple of seconds.\\n6. When you see Bootloader Mode menu release held buttons.\\n7. From the menu choose option RECOVERY MODE by using Volume buttons to scroll and Power key to select options.\\n8. Congratulations! You should be right now in the expected mode.\", \"To factory reset an HTC One VX, follow these steps:\\n1. Slide the Notifications panel open, and then tap.\\n2. Tap Storage Factory data reset.\\n3. Tap Reset phone, and then tap Erase everything.\\n\\nAnswer: To factory reset an HTC One VX, slide the Notifications panel open, tap Storage Factory data reset, tap Reset phone, and then tap Erase everything.\"]", "time_sec": 18.863, "generation_time_seconds": 18.8595, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0003, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 8633, 7585, 