0.5464, -0.0002, -0.0293, -0.0, -1.0782, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0001, -2.46, -0.0172, -0.0, -0.3215, -0.0002, -0.1653, -0.0001, -0.0103, -0.3282, -0.0, -0.0025, -0.0047, -0.0, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0001, -0.0374, -0.0419, 0.0, -0.0003, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0083, -0.0, -1.6771, -3.6993, -0.0113, -0.2101, -0.0002, -0.0649, -0.0004, -0.0003, -0.0719, -0.0054, -0.0, -0.1057, 0.0, -0.0, 0.0, -0.2111, -0.3146, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0058, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0939, -0.0001, -0.0202, -1.7308, 0.0, -0.0, -0.5117, -0.0, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0, -0.2522, -0.0826, -0.0005, -0.007, -7.7091, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0963, -0.3046, -0.0004], "cumulative_logprob": -96.3485, "norm_logp": -0.3039, "input_len": 491, "output_tokens": 317, "pred": "In summary:\n- Elements are pure substances composed of one type of atom and cannot be broken down into simpler substances by chemical means.\n- Compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements, bonded together to form a new substance with unique properties.\n- Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and can be separated easily by physical methods."}], "input_len": 491, "output_tokens": 748, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 59.52, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "226", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to fix a lift valve in a toilet:\n\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve and any remaining pieces of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n3. Install the new flapper valve and connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, making sure it is securely fastened.\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank and flush the toilet to test for correct operation.\n5. Adjust the chain as needed to ensure a proper flush. Cut off any excess chain to prevent tangling.\n\nNote: If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "pred": "By following these steps, you can effectively fix a lift valve in a toilet.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To fix a lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Shut off the water supply valve**: Before starting any repairs, ensure that the water supply to the toilet is turned off to avoid any accidents or water damage.\n\n2. **Remove the old flapper valve**: Carefully remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Make sure to also remove any remaining pieces of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n\n3. **Install the new flapper valve**: Push the small solid end of the new toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included, screw it in tightly until there is no more give and it is secure.\n\n4. **Connect the chain**: Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened.\n\n5. **Turn on the water supply**: After securing the components, turn the water valve back on.\n\n6. **Test the flush**: Test the flush to ensure everything is working correctly. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\n\n7. **Check for correct operation**: Open the water valve to fill the tank. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation. If necessary, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n\nBy following these steps, you can effectively fix a lift valve in a toilet.", "cot": "[\"To fix a lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Shut off the water supply valve**: Before starting any repairs, ensure that the water supply to the toilet is turned off to avoid any accidents or water damage.\\n\\n2. **Remove the old flapper valve**: Carefully remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Make sure to also remove any remaining pieces of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n\\n3. **Install the new flapper valve**: Push the small solid end of the new toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included, screw it in tightly until there is no more give and it is secure.\\n\\n4. **Connect the chain**: Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened.\\n\\n5. **Turn on the water supply**: After securing the components, turn the water valve back on.\\n\\n6. **Test the flush**: Test the flush to ensure everything is working correctly. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\\n\\n7. **Check for correct operation**: Open the water valve to fill the tank. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation. If necessary, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can effectively fix a lift valve in a toilet.\", \"To fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Shutoff the Water Supply Valve**: Turn off the water supply valve to the toilet to ensure that no water flows into the tank during the repair process.\\n\\n2. **Remove the Old Flapper Valve**: Carefully slip the old flapper valve off the mounting arms. Ensure you remove any remnants of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n\\n3. **Open the Water Valve and Flush**: Open the water valve to fill the tank. This step is crucial to ensure the tank is full before you proceed with the repair. Once the tank is full, flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\\n\\n4. **Adjust the Lift Chain**: If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links. This adjustment helps ensure the chain is properly positioned and operates correctly.\\n\\n5. **Cut Off Excess Chain**: After making the necessary adjustments, cut off any excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\\n\\n6. **Install the New Lift Arm and Chain**: Push the small solid end of the new toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure. The other end of the lift arm will hang freely in the air.\\n\\n7. **Connect the Chain**: Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. This hole is the one closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\\n\\n8. **Test the Flush**: Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can effectively fix the lift valve in a toilet, ensuring it functions correctly and efficiently.\", \"To fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Shut off the water supply valve** to the toilet to ensure safety and prevent water from flowing while you work.\\n2. **Remove the old flapper valve** by slipping it off the mounting arms. Also, remove the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n3. **Open the water valve** to fill the tank and flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\\n4. If necessary, **readjust the lift chain** by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links to ensure proper alignment.\\n5. **Cut off the excess lift chain** to prevent it from getting tangled.\\n6. **Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle**. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly until there is no more give and it is secure.\\n7. **Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm**, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\\n8. **Turn the water valve back on** and test out the flush of the toilet.\\n9. If the toilet flushes slowly, **adjust the chain** to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can effectively fix the lift valve in your toilet.\", \"To fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n3. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\\n4. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\\n5. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\\n6. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\\n7. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\\n8. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure. The other end will hang freely in the air.\\n9. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\\n10. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\\n11. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\\n12. For further adjustments, readjust the lift chain as needed.\"]", "time_sec": 40.639, "generation_time_seconds": 40.6356,