{"id": "252", "question": "how to grill pork chops, allrecipes.com", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to grill pork chops according to Allrecipes.com:\n\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate. (Passage 1)\n2. In a bowl, mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. (Passage 1)\n3. For Oven-Fried Pork Chops, use stuffing mix for the breading. The pork chops come out tender and juicy. This recipe takes 30 minutes to prepare and 10 minutes to prep. (Passage 2)\n4. To grill pork chops over indirect heat, rinse the chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. Massage the spice rub into the meat for 10 minutes before grilling. Grill the chops until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side. (Passage 3)\n\nTherefore, to grill pork chops according to Allrecipes.com, you should preheat the grill, season the pork chops with a spice mixture, and grill them over indirect heat until they are cooked through.", "pred": "Preheat the outdoor grill for medium heat, lightly oil the grate, mix together seasoning ingredients in a bowl, rinse pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture, grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side. After grilling, allow the pork chops to rest for 10 minutes.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Step 1: Identify the steps for grilling pork chops from the passage.\n- Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate.\n- Mix together seasoning ingredients in a bowl.\n- Rinse pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture.\n- Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\n\nStep 2: Check for additional information or recipes.\n- The second passage mentions an oven-fried pork chop recipe but does not provide grilling instructions.\n- The third passage provides additional grilling instructions for pork chops, including the use of a spice rub and grilling time.\n\nStep 3: Synthesize the information to form a comprehensive answer.\n- Preheat the outdoor grill for medium heat.\n- Lightly oil the grate.\n- Mix together seasoning ingredients in a bowl.\n- Rinse pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture.\n- Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\n- After grilling, allow the pork chops to rest for 10 minutes.\n\nAnswer: Preheat the outdoor grill for medium heat, lightly oil the grate, mix together seasoning ingredients in a bowl, rinse pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture, grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side. After grilling, allow the pork chops to rest for 10 minutes.", "cot": "[\"Step 1: Identify the steps for grilling pork chops from the passage.\\n- Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate.\\n- Mix together seasoning ingredients in a bowl.\\n- Rinse pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture.\\n- Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\\n\\nStep 2: Check for additional information or recipes.\\n- The second passage mentions an oven-fried pork chop recipe but does not provide grilling instructions.\\n- The third passage provides additional grilling instructions for pork chops, including the use of a spice rub and grilling time.\\n\\nStep 3: Synthesize the information to form a comprehensive answer.\\n- Preheat the outdoor grill for medium heat.\\n- Lightly oil the grate.\\n- Mix together seasoning ingredients in a bowl.\\n- Rinse pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture.\\n- Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\\n- After grilling, allow the pork chops to rest for 10 minutes.\\n\\nAnswer: Preheat the outdoor grill for medium heat, lightly oil the grate, mix together seasoning ingredients in a bowl, rinse pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture, grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side. After grilling, allow the pork chops to rest for 10 minutes.\", \"To grill pork chops, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate.\\n2. In a bowl, mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined.\\n3. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture.\\n4. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes.\\n5. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\", \"First, preheat the outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate. Rinse the pork chops, and sprinkle both sides with the spice mixture. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat. Allow the pork chops to stand for 10 minutes. Finally, grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, which should take about 12 minutes per side.\\n\\nAnswer:[Preheat the outdoor grill for medium heat, lightly oil the grate, rinse the pork chops, sprinkle both sides with the spice mixture, massage the spice rub into the meat, allow the pork chops to stand for 10 minutes, then grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.]\", \"To grill pork chops, first preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate. Mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring in a bowl until thoroughly combined. Rinse the pork chops and sprinkle the wet mixture on both sides. Massage the spice rub into the meat and let it stand for 10 minutes. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\"]", "time_sec": 23.46, "generation_time_seconds": 23.4563, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0002, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 7354, 369, 1081, 9400, 35067, 90078, 504, 279, 21085, 624, 12, 4968, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 8628, 11, 323, 33404, 5590, 279, 85354, 624, 12, 19219, 3786, 86219, 13966, 304, 264, 19212, 624, 12, 57368, 325, 35067, 90078, 323, 84847, 279, 14401, 90078, 389, 2176, 11067, 448, 279, 41686, 20980, 624, 12, 49848, 279, 90078, 916, 24614, 8628, 3080, 902, 5021, 18217, 4766, 11, 911, 220, 16, 17, 4420, 817, 3108, 382, 8304, 220, 17, 25, 4248, 369, 5107, 1995, 476, 18627, 624, 12, 576, 2086, 21085, 33845, 458, 23387, 2220, 4487, 35067, 46994, 11116, 714, 1558, 537, 3410, 1081, 9400, 11221, 624, 12, 576, 4843, 21085, 5707, 5107, 1081, 9400, 11221, 369, 35067, 90078, 11, 2670, 279, 990, 315, 264, 41686, 10273, 323, 1081, 9400, 882, 382, 8304, 220, 18, 25, 23153, 26887, 279, 1995, 311, 1352, 264, 15817, 4226, 624, 12, 4968, 19963, 279, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 8628, 624, 12, 8658, 398, 5590, 279, 85354, 624, 12, 19219, 3786, 86219, 13966, 304, 264, 19212, 624, 12, 57368, 325, 35067, 90078, 323, 84847, 279, 14401, 90078, 389, 2176, 11067, 448, 279, 41686, 20980, 624, 12, 49848, 279, 90078, 916, 24614, 8628, 3080, 902, 5021, 18217, 4766, 11, 911, 220, 16, 17, 4420, 817, 3108, 624, 12, 4636, 1081, 9400, 11, 2138, 279, 35067, 90078, 311, 2732, 369, 220, 16, 15, 4420, 382, 16141, 25, 4968, 19963, 279, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 8628, 11, 33404, 5590, 279, 85354, 11, 6514, 3786, 86219, 13966, 304, 264, 19212, 11, 73241, 35067, 90078, 323, 84847, 279, 14401, 