43, -0.0006, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0183, -0.0008, -0.0, -3.7076, -0.0552, -0.0045, -0.0, -0.0, 0.0, -0.9595, -0.4074], "cumulative_logprob": -35.6381, "norm_logp": -0.1371, "input_len": 436, "output_tokens": 260, "pred": "1. Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer.\n2. Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs.\n3. Season the ribs by mixing mustard and liquid smoke (if using), brushing the ribs on both sides, and sprinkling with a dry rub.\n4. Put the ribs in a resealable bag and add BBQ sauce to cover.\n5. Line the baking pan with heavy-duty foil, overlapping it to make a tent.\n6. Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F).\n7. Remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, and brush them with some of the sauce.\n8. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes, then flip and brush the ribs and cook another 5 minutes.\n9. Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.\n10. If oven-cooked, remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs, put them in a resealable bag with BBQ sauce, and line the baking pan with heavy-duty foil overlapping it to make a tent."}, {"rollout": 1, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 55149, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 1416, 1667, 264, 39058, 11, 8628, 279, 39058, 311, 11051, 320, 18, 20, 15, 58472, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 568, 10783, 279, 55149, 504, 279, 46399, 11, 1992, 1105, 13041, 88, 24067, 705, 389, 279, 39058, 11, 323, 15625, 1105, 448, 1045, 315, 279, 19187, 13, 17757, 279, 39058, 323, 4296, 369, 220, 20, 4420, 13, 40284, 323, 15625, 279, 55149, 323, 4296, 2441, 220, 20, 4420, 13, 15003, 311, 4296, 11, 64661, 323, 76726, 1449, 220, 20, 4420, 11, 3080, 279, 19187, 702, 12045, 6758, 323, 279, 55149, 525, 31713, 1526, 323, 614, 39058, 15423, 11, 369, 264, 2790, 1081, 9400, 882, 315, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 624, 17, 13, 1416, 1667, 458, 23387, 11, 4057, 279, 38554, 504, 