{"id": "384", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically:\n\nPassage 1 suggests using Kutools for Excel, which provides a Sort Sheets tool to easily sort all worksheets in alphabetical order. However, if you prefer not to use macros or Kutools, Passage 2 provides an alternative method using the built-in Sort feature in Excel.\n\nTo sort an Excel sheet alphabetically using the built-in Sort feature, follow these steps:\n\n1. Select the data you wish to sort by clicking on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings.\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\n3. Click on the Sort option.\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu and select the column you wish to sort by (e.g., Product column in alphabetical order - A to Z).\n5. Click OK.\n\nOnce you have completed these steps, the data in your Excel sheet will be sorted alphabetically.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide sufficient information to clarify how to arrange an Excel sheet numerically.", "pred": "After completing these steps, the data in your Excel sheet will be sorted alphabetically by the selected column.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can follow the steps from the passage provided:\n\n1. **Select All the Data**: First, click on the \"Select All\" button at the intersection of your row and column headings. This ensures that all the data in your worksheet is selected.\n\n2. **Switch to the Data Tab**: Next, switch to the \"Data\" tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon.\n\n3. **Locate and Click on the Sort Option**: In the \"Data\" tab, locate the \"Sort & Filter\" group and click on the \"Sort\" option.\n\n4. **Select the Column to Sort By**: Click on the \"Sort By\" drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data. For example, if you want to sort by the Product column (column B), select \"Product\" from the drop-down menu.\n\n5. **Choose the Sorting Order**: Ensure that the sorting order is set to \"A to Z\" to sort the data alphabetically from A to Z.\n\nAfter completing these steps, the data in your Excel sheet will be sorted alphabetically by the selected column.", "cot": "[\"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can follow the steps from the passage provided:\\n\\n1. **Select All the Data**: First, click on the \\\"Select All\\\" button at the intersection of your row and column headings. This ensures that all the data in your worksheet is selected.\\n\\n2. **Switch to the Data Tab**: Next, switch to the \\\"Data\\\" tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon.\\n\\n3. **Locate and Click on the Sort Option**: In the \\\"Data\\\" tab, locate the \\\"Sort & Filter\\\" group and click on the \\\"Sort\\\" option.\\n\\n4. **Select the Column to Sort By**: Click on the \\\"Sort By\\\" drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data. For example, if you want to sort by the Product column (column B), select \\\"Product\\\" from the drop-down menu.\\n\\n5. **Choose the Sorting Order**: Ensure that the sorting order is set to \\\"A to Z\\\" to sort the data alphabetically from A to Z.\\n\\nAfter completing these steps, the data in your Excel sheet will be sorted alphabetically by the selected column.\", \"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can use the Custom Sort feature. Select the data you want to sort, then click on the Data tab from the toolbar. Click on the Sort button and choose Custom Sort from the popup menu. In the Sort window, select the column you wish to sort by, in this case, column B for the Product column, and choose the sorting order as A to Z. Click on the OK button, and the data in the spreadsheet will be sorted alphabetically.\", \"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select all the data in your worksheet by clicking on the \\\"Select All\\\" button at the intersection of your row and column headings. This will highlight all the cells in your worksheet.\\n\\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the \\\"Sort & Filter\\\" group. Click on the \\\"Sort\\\" option.\\n\\n3. Click on the \\\"Sort By\\\" drop-down menu to select a column by name. Choose the column that you want to sort by, and Excel will arrange the data in alphabetical order based on the values in that column.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can easily sort your Excel sheet alphabetically, making it easier to find and organize data.\", \"Step 1: Identify the method to sort an Excel sheet alphabetically.\\n- From the given passages, the method described involves using the \\\"Sort\\\" feature within Microsoft Excel.\\n\\nStep 2: Understand the specific steps to use the \\\"Sort\\\" feature.\\n- Passage 2 provides a detailed example: \\\"Then select the Data tab from the toolbar at the top of the screen. Then click on the Sort button and select Custom Sort from the popup menu. When the Sort window appears, select the data that you wish to sort by. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z). Click on the OK button.\\\"\\n\\nStep 3: Confirm that the instructions are clear and specific.\\n- The instructions are clear and specific, guiding the user through the process of selecting the Data tab, clicking on the Sort button, choosing Custom Sort, selecting the column to sort by (in this case, column B), and then clicking OK.\\n\\nStep 4: Provide the final answer based on the provided information.\\n- The final answer is to use the \\\"Sort\\\" feature in Excel, specifically by selecting the Data tab, clicking on the Sort button, choosing Custom Sort, selecting the column to sort by, and then clicking OK.\\n\\nAnswer: Use the \\\"Sort\\\" feature in Excel, specifically by selecting the Data tab, clicking on the Sort button, choosing Custom Sort, selecting the column to sort by, and then clicking OK.\"]", "time_sec": 35.994, "generation_time_seconds": 35.9891, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0004, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 11, 498, 646, 1795, 279, 7354, 504, 279, 21085, 3897, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 3379, 2009, 279, 2885, 95518, 5512, 11, 4205, 389, 279, 330, 3379, 2009, 1, 3137, 518, 279, 19246, 315, 697, 2802, 323, 3250, 69452, 13, 1096, 25351, 429, 678, 279, 821, 304, 697, 36636, 374, 4091, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 16837, 311, 279, 2885, 15139, 95518, 9295, 11, 3398, 311, 279, 330, 1043, 1, 5651, 304, 279, 5100, 21029, 44567, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 9152, 349, 323, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 6959, 95518, 758, 279, 330, 1043, 1, 5651, 11, 24523, 279, 330, 10231, 609, 12339, 1, 1874, 323, 4205, 389, 279, 330, 10231, 1, 2999, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 3379, 279, 9332, 311, 15967, 3216, 95518, 9189, 389, 279, 330, 10231, 3216, 1, 5943, 14875, 5022, 311, 3293, 264, 3250, 553, 829, 13, 576, 5036, 7866, 311, 279, 69452, 31969, 304, 279, 1156, 2802, 315, 697, 821, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 421, 498, 1366, 311, 3378, 553, 279, 5643, 3250, 320, 6229, 425, 701, 3293, 330, 4816, 1, 504, 279, 5943, 14875, 5022, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 24051, 279, 77143, 7217, 95518, 29279, 429, 279, 28273, 1973, 374, 738, 311, 330, 32, 311, 1863, 1, 311, 3378, 279, 821, 27790, 2673, 504, 362, 311, 1863, 382, 6025, 26568, 1493, 7354, 11, 279, 821, 304, 697, 21029, 10834, 686, 387, 10615, 27790, 2673, 553, 279, 4091, 3250, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0713, -0.0016, -0.0001, -0.0029, -0.0, -0.0045, 0.0, -0.0127, -0.3644, -0.0032, -0.2542, -2.028, -0.0693, -3.8582, -0.2144, -1.7665, -1.4984, -0.5379, -0.0009, -0.0, -1.8681, -0.0727, -0.699, -1.1322, -0.0352, -0.0405, -3.0006, -0.0, -0.1109, -0.001, -0.0, -