cess and where everything's located.]"}], "input_len": 588, "output_tokens": 639, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 50.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "411", "question": "how to make panko crumbs", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the given passages, here's a step-by-step guide on how to make panko crumbs:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\n2. Push torn pieces of bread or chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet.\n4. Bake in preheated oven until crumbs are dry but not toasted, 6 to 8 minutes. Shake the sheet twice during baking to evenly dry the crumbs.\n5. Remove from the oven and cool completely.\n\nIf you want to store the panko crumbs for later use, you can transfer them to an airtight container and keep them at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "To make panko crumbs, follow these steps:", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "Step 1: Identify the key steps in making panko crumbs from the given passages.\n\n- Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F.\n- Push torn pieces of bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\n- Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet.\n- Bake in preheated oven until crumbs are dry but not toasted (6 to 8 minutes).\n- Shake the sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\n- Remove from the oven and cool completely.\n\nStep 2: Compare the steps from the passages to confirm consistency.\n\nAll passages provide the same key steps for making panko crumbs, with slight variations in the specific details and methods.\n\nStep 3: Formulate the answer based on the identified steps.\n\nAnswer: To make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F.\n2. Use a food processor to shred torn pieces of bread into coarse crumbs.\n3. Spread the crumbs evenly on a baking sheet.\n4. Bake the crumbs in the preheated oven for 6 to 8 minutes, ensuring they are dry but not toasted.\n5. Shake the baking sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\n6. Remove the crumbs from the oven and allow them to cool completely.", "cot": "[\"Step 1: Identify the key steps in making panko crumbs from the given passages.\\n\\n- Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F.\\n- Push torn pieces of bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n- Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet.\\n- Bake in preheated oven until crumbs are dry but not toasted (6 to 8 minutes).\\n- Shake the sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\\n- Remove from the oven and cool completely.\\n\\nStep 2: Compare the steps from the passages to confirm consistency.\\n\\nAll passages provide the same key steps for making panko crumbs, with slight variations in the specific details and methods.\\n\\nStep 3: Formulate the answer based on the identified steps.\\n\\nAnswer: To make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F.\\n2. Use a food processor to shred torn pieces of bread into coarse crumbs.\\n3. Spread the crumbs evenly on a baking sheet.\\n4. Bake the crumbs in the preheated oven for 6 to 8 minutes, ensuring they are dry but not toasted.\\n5. Shake the baking sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\\n6. Remove the crumbs from the oven and allow them to cool completely.\", \"To make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees Fahrenheit (150 degrees Celsius).\\n\\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. The passage specifies that the bread should be white.\\n\\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet.\\n\\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted. The baking time is approximately 6 to 8 minutes.\\n\\n5. Shake the baking sheet twice during the baking process to ensure even drying.\\n\\n6. Once the crumbs are dry but not toasted, remove the baking sheet from the oven and allow it to cool completely.\\n\\nThis process will result in panko crumbs, which are a type of coarse bread crumb that is commonly used in Japanese cuisine.\", \"To make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\\n2. Push torn pieces of bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. \\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet.\\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for about 6 to 8 minutes. Shake the sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\\n5. Remove the baking sheet from the oven and allow the crumbs to cool completely.\\n\\nThese steps will result in panko crumbs that are ready for use in various recipes.\", \"To make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake at 300 degrees F until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes. Shake the sheet twice during baking.\\n4. Be careful not to let the crumbs brown.\\n5. Remove from the oven and cool completely.\\n6. Allow the crumbs to cool on the pans for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n7. Transfer the cooled crumbs to an airtight container and store at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can make panko crumbs that are used in various Japanese-style dishes.\"]", "time_sec": 33.536, "generation_time_seconds": 33.5294, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0004, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 1376, 7354, 304, 3259, 281, 92852, 96577, 504, 279, 2661, 46769, 382, 12, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 12348, 434, 624, 12, 22950, 21145, 9666, 315, 16002, 1526, 279, 52362, 287, 13364, 315, 264, 3607, 17654, 311, 1281, 49247, 96577, 624, 12, 47716, 279, 96577, 389, 264, 27815, 10834, 624, 12, 52074, 304, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 