, -0.0985, -0.7225, -0.0191, 0.0, -0.0009, -0.7788, -0.0749, -5.6289, -0.1117, -0.1038, -1.7462, -3.5864, -0.1591, -0.393, -0.0065], "cumulative_logprob": -33.8887, "norm_logp": -0.1893, "input_len": 597, "output_tokens": 179, "pred": "By following these steps, you can make panko crumbs that are used in various Japanese-style dishes."}], "input_len": 597, "output_tokens": 746, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 5.71, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "425", "question": "what is a upc description", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, an UPDescription is:\n\n1. A barcode symbology used for tracking trade items in stores, consisting of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. (Passage 1)\n2. A process involving receiving a specimen bottle from a member, ensuring it contains a minimum of 30 milliliters of urine, initialing the label in the member's presence, and verifying the information on the label and DD Form 2624 (a military form). (Passage 2)\n3. A barcode partner that provides GS1 Originated UPC and EAN codes, as well as a toll-free number and positive customer reviews. (Passage 3)\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology widely used in various countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is primarily used for scanning trade items at the point of sale, following GS1 specifications.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology widely used in various countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is primarily used for scanning trade items at the point of sale, following GS1 specifications.", "cot": "[\"The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology widely used in various countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is primarily used for scanning trade items at the point of sale, following GS1 specifications.\", \"A Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology widely used for tracking trade items in various countries. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is primarily used for scanning at the point of sale, as specified by GS1.\", \"Step 1: Identify the key information about UPC from the passage.\\n- Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology.\\n- Widely used in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, in Europe, and other countries.\\n- Consists of 12 numeric digits.\\n- Unique assignment to each trade item.\\n- Used for scanning of trade items at the point of sale.\\n- Related to EAN barcode.\\n\\nStep 2: Formulate an answer based on the identified information.\\nA UPC is a barcode symbology used for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits, which are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is widely used in various countries, including the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, in Europe, and other countries. It is primarily used for scanning trade items at the point of sale, in accordance with GS1 specifications.\\n\\nAnswer: A UPC is a barcode symbology used for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits, which are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is widely used in various countries, including the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, in Europe, and other countries. It is primarily used for scanning trade items at the point of sale, in accordance with GS1 specifications.\", \"The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology widely used in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, in Europe and other countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC, along with the related EAN barcode, is the barcode mainly used for scanning of trade items at the point of sale, per GS1 specifications.\"]", "time_sec": 24.235, "generation_time_seconds": 24.2278, "selection_time_seconds": 0.001, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 25500, 56