{"id": "479", "question": "change of address u.s. postal service", "gt": "To change your US postal address, you can visit the official website of the U.S. Postal Service, fill out an online form, or contact their call center. The process is fast and versatile, allowing you to notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the USPS. It's important to note that you can also use this feature to have your business mail forwarded to a new address due to a permanent move or temporary relocation. The process involves submitting either an online form or filling out and submitting a physical form at any U.S. Post Office.", "pred": "The U.S. Postal Service offers a fast, versatile, and secure change of address service that can be completed online or through various contact methods. You can notify up to 100 organizations and use identity validation for $1. The service is important for both personal and business mail forwarding, especially in cases of permanent moves or disaster-related relocations.**", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To answer the question \"change of address u.s. postal service\" based on the provided passages, let's break down the relevant information:\n\n1. **Fast Processing**: The U.S. Postal Service (USPS) allows for a fast change of address service, which can be completed in as little as 1 minute.\n\n2. **Versatility**: You can notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service about your new address.\n\n3. **Secure**: The service uses the latest encryption technologies to ensure the safety of your data.\n\n4. **Online Option**: The USPS offers an online form for completing the official change of address, which is categorized for easy access.\n\n5. **Methods for Change**:\n   - Visit https://moversguide.usps.com/ and use identity validation for $1.\n   - Call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777).\n   - Fill out and submit PS Form 3575, which can be obtained at any U.S. Post Office.\n\n6. **Business Mail Forwarding**: This feature is not only for personal addresses but also applies to business mail forwarding due to permanent moves or temporary relocations.\n\n7. **Disaster Consideration**: It is important to have your mail forwarded if your business has been subjected to a disaster that requires relocation.\n\nBased on the above information, the answer to \"change of address u.s. postal service\" is:\n\n**Answer: The U.S. Postal Service offers a fast, versatile, and secure change of address service that can be completed online or through various contact methods. You can notify up to 100 organizations and use identity validation for $1. The service is important for both personal and business mail forwarding, especially in cases of permanent moves or disaster-related relocations.**", "cot": "[\"To answer the question \\\"change of address u.s. postal service\\\" based on the provided passages, let's break down the relevant information:\\n\\n1. **Fast Processing**: The U.S. Postal Service (USPS) allows for a fast change of address service, which can be completed in as little as 1 minute.\\n\\n2. **Versatility**: You can notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service about your new address.\\n\\n3. **Secure**: The service uses the latest encryption technologies to ensure the safety of your data.\\n\\n4. **Online Option**: The USPS offers an online form for completing the official change of address, which is categorized for easy access.\\n\\n5. **Methods for Change**:\\n   - Visit https://moversguide.usps.com/ and use identity validation for $1.\\n   - Call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777).\\n   - Fill out and submit PS Form 3575, which can be obtained at any U.S. Post Office.\\n\\n6. **Business Mail Forwarding**: This feature is not only for personal addresses but also applies to business mail forwarding due to permanent moves or temporary relocations.\\n\\n7. **Disaster Consideration**: It is important to have your mail forwarded if your business has been subjected to a disaster that requires relocation.\\n\\nBased on the above information, the answer to \\\"change of address u.s. postal service\\\" is:\\n\\n**Answer: The U.S. Postal Service offers a fast, versatile, and secure change of address service that can be completed online or through various contact methods. You can notify up to 100 organizations and use identity validation for $1. The service is important for both personal and business mail forwarding, especially in cases of permanent moves or disaster-related relocations.**\", \"Step 1: Identify the key features of changing an address with the U.S. Postal Service.\\n- Fast: Change of address service in as little as 1 minute.\\n- Versatile: Notify up to 100 organizations.\\n- Secure: Latest encryption technologies ensure data safety.\\n- Easy to complete online.\\n- Three ways to change address: visit https://moversguide.usps.com/, call the USPS Call Center, or fill out and submit PS Form 3575.\\n\\nStep 2: Determine the types of address changes covered.\\n- Permanent move.\\n- Temporary relocation.\\n- Business mail forwarding.\\n\\nStep 3: Consider the importance and urgency of changing an address.\\n- Important to remember to have your mail forwarded if your business has been subjected to a disaster that requires relocation.\\n- It is especially important to remember to have your mail forwarded if your business has been subjected to a disaster that requires relocation.\\n\\nAnswer: The U.S. Postal Service offers a fast, versatile, and secure method for changing your address. To change your address, you can visit https://moversguide.usps.com/, call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or fill out and submit PS Form 3575. The change of address service is available for permanent moves, temporary relocations, and business mail forwarding. It is especially important to remember to have your mail forwarded if your business has been subjected to a disaster that requires relocation.\", \"The U.S. Postal Service offers a change of address service that can be completed in 1 minute or less. The service is versatile, allowing you to notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service. The information is secure, thanks to the use of latest encryption technologies.\\n\\nThe service can be accessed through their website at https://moversguide.usps.com, by calling the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or by filling out and submitting PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office.\\n\\nThere are three ways to change your address:\\n\\n1. Visit https://moversguide.usps.com. Safeguard your personal information with identity validation by a simple $1 charge to your credit or debit card.\\n2. Call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777).\\n3. Fill out and submit PS Form 3575, which you can pick up at any U.S. Post Office, and submit it at the Post Office.\\n\\nThe form may be submitted at any U.S. Post Office, mailed to any Post Office, or provided to any Postal Mail Carrier.\\n\\nAnswer: The U.S. Postal Service offers a change of address service that can be completed in 1 minute or less. The service is versatile, allowing you to notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service. The information is secure, thanks to the use of latest encryption technologies. There are three ways to change your address: 1. Visit https://moversguide.usps.com. Safeguard your personal information with identity validation by a simple $1 charge to your credit or debit card. 2. Call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777). 3. Fill out and submit PS Form 3575, which you can pick up at any U.S. Post Office, and submit it at the Post Office. The form may be submitted at any U.S. Post Office, mailed to any Post Office, or provided to any Postal Mail Carrier.\", \"The US Postal Service offers a change of address service that can be completed in as little as one minute. It allows users to notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service (USPS). The service is versatile and secure, using the latest encryption technologies to protect user data. To change your address, you can visit https://moversguide.usps.com/, call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or fill out and submit PS Form 3575, which can be obtained at any U.S. Post Office. The service is designed to help with business mail forwarding in cases of permanent moves or temporary relocations, especially after disasters that require relocation.\"]", "time_sec": 58.585, "generation_time_seconds": 58.5774, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0008, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 4226, 279, 3405, 330, 3373, 315, 2621, 575, 514, 13, 39754, 2473, 1, 3118, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 1077, 594, 1438, 1495, 279, 9760, 1995, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 32174, 28125, 95518, 576, 547, 808, 13, 54217, 5362, 320, 2034, 5012, 8, 6147, 369, 264, 4937, 2297, 315, 2621, 2473, 11, 892, 646, 387, 8145, 304, 438, 2632, 438, 220, 16, 9383, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 83956, 31156, 95518, 1446, 646, 15456, 705, 311, 220, 16, 15, 15, 11104, 304, 5256, 311, 279, 54217, 5362, 911, 697, 501, 2621, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 49813, 95518, 576, 2473, 5711, 279, 5535, 25463, 14310, 311, 5978, 279, 7149, 315, 697, 821, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 19598, 6959, 95518, 576, 84876, 6081, 458, 2860, 1352, 369, 26568, 279, 3946, 2297, 315, 2621, 11, 892, 374, 70874, 369, 4135, 2615, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 17856, 369, 10388, 334, 510, 256, 481, 19008, 3703, 1110, 76, 8969, 48370, 21916, 1690, 905, 14, 323, 990, 9569, 10519, 369, 400, 16, 624, 256, 481, 7143, 279, 84876, 7143, 5832, 518, 220, 16, 12, 23, 15, 15, 12, 7384, 32340, 5012, 320, 16, 12, 23, 15, 15, 12, 17, 22, 20, 12, 23, 22, 22, 22, 4292, 256, 481, 21979, 700, 323, 9318, 11405, 3377, 220, 18, 20, 22, 20, 11, 892, 646, 387, 12180, 518, 894, 547, 808, 13, 3877, 8246, 382, 21, 13, 3070, 227