atest encryption technologies to protect user data. To change your address, you can visit https://moversguide.usps.com/, call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or fill out and submit PS Form 3575, which can be obtained at any U.S. Post Office. The service is designed to help with business mail forwarding in cases of permanent moves or temporary relocations, especially after disasters that require relocation."}], "input_len": 473, "output_tokens": 1336, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 39.62, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "489", "question": "how can you tell who liked your tweet", "gt": "You can see who liked your tweets by using tracking websites such as Favotter.net and Favstar.fm. These sites can give you an idea of who is favouriting your tweets. Alternatively, you can also set up notifications on Twitter itself. By going to your account settings and clicking on the notifications link, you can arrange to be notified via email whenever someone likes one of your tweets.", "pred": "To tell who liked your tweet, you can use websites like Favotter.net or Favstar.fm.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To tell who liked your tweet, you can use websites like Favotter.net or Favstar.fm.", "cot": "[\"To tell who liked your tweet, you can use websites like Favotter.net or Favstar.fm.\", \"To tell who liked your tweet, you can use a website that allows you to track who favorited your tweets. One such website is Favotter.net or Favstar.fm. These websites can provide you with information about who favorited your tweets and which tweets that you and others are also favoriting. You can also set up your Twitter account to receive email notifications whenever someone marks one of your tweets as a favorite.\", \"To tell who liked your tweet, you can use a website that tracks favorites. One such website mentioned in the passage is Favotter.net. Another option is Favstar.fm. These sites allow you to see who has favorited your tweets or the same tweets as you, giving you insight into other users who might be interested in your content.\", \"To tell who liked your tweet, you can use one of the two websites mentioned in the passages: Favotter.net or Favstar.fm. These websites allow you to track which tweets you and others have favorited. By using these sites, you can get a good idea of who is favoriting your tweets or favored the same tweets as you. This information can help you find other Twitter users to follow or see what tweets people like of yours.\"]", "time_sec": 15.518, "generation_time_seconds": 15.5106, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0004, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 3291, 879, 14915, 697, 11809, 11, 498, 646, 990, 13037, 1075, 80941, 354, 465, 5071, 476, 80941, 11870, 70485, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.2433, -0.734, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0031, -0.0006, -0.0012, -0.0098, -0.0041, -0.0265, -0.756, -0.3073, -0.0025, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0, -1.1946, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0509, -4.9108], "cumulative_logprob": -8.2448, "norm_logp": -0.3748, "input_len": 505, "output_tokens": 22, "pred": "To tell who liked your tweet, you can use websites like Favotter.net or Favstar.fm."}, {"rollout": 1, "token_ids": [1249, 3291, 879, 14915, 697, 11809, 11, 498, 646, 990, 264, 3910, 429, 6147, 498, 311, 3754, 879, 4694, 1608, 697, 23150, 13, 3776, 1741, 3910, 374, 80941, 354, 465, 5071, 476, 80941, 11870, 70485, 13, 4220, 13037, 646, 3410, 498, 448, 1995, 911, 879, 4694, 1608, 697, 23150, 323, 892, 23150, 429, 498, 323, 3800, 525, 1083, 4694, 5853, 13, 1446, 646, 1083, 738, 705, 697, 6271, 2692, 311, 5258, 2551, 21969, 15356, 4325, 15423, 825, 315, 697, 23150, 438, 264, 6930, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.2433, -0.734, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0031, -0.0006, -0.0012, -0.0098, -0.0041, -0.0265, -0.756, -0.0499, -1.0559, -2.2645, -0.0014, -0.0, -0.4349, -0.4334, -0.8171, -0.0007, -0.0014, -0.0001, -0.0133, -0.7868, -0.1156, -0.0444, -0.4303, -0.2031, -0.0003, 0.0, -0.0, -0.7868, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0035, -0.5332, -0.5084, -0.7893, -1.7419, -0.1344, -0.0001, -0.7252, -0.5944, -0.2779, -1.7657, -0.0, -0.001, -0.0024, -1.0266, -0.0677, -0.0006, -1.081, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.0178, -0.0102, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.0074, -4.3979, -0.001, -0.4634, -0.1325, -0.0, -0.1845, -0.173, -0.0001, -0.3617, -0.0763, -0.5065, -0.0, -0.0355, -0.0, -0.0044, -0.0002, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.6241, -0.0, -0.0831, -0.1872], "cumulative_logprob": -25.7401, "norm_logp": -0.3028, "input