 -0.0003, -0.0005, -1.5623, -0.3012, -0.745, -0.08, -0.0006, -0.0139, -0.0001, -0.0192, -2.9565, -0.0116, -0.0424, -0.0605, -0.0188], "cumulative_logprob": -32.9431, "norm_logp": -0.1432, "input_len": 618, "output_tokens": 230, "pred": "Note: The passages mention that small potatoes can be planted whole, but for sprouted potatoes, the instructions are to cut them into cubes as described above."}], "input_len": 618, "output_tokens": 1130, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 47.74, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "656", "question": "how to properly clean your hair", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to properly clean your hair:\n\n1. Rinse your hair completely with water.\n2. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair.\n3. Apply a conditioner and allow it to remain on for a few minutes.\n4. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\n5. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles.\n\nAdditionally, it is recommended to use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair after washing, and to be gentle when handling wet hair to prevent damage.", "pred": "1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "To properly clean your hair, follow these steps:\n\n1. Make sure to select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n2. While in the shower, ensure the water is warm but not too hot, and turn the flow down slightly to avoid splashing.\n3. Thoroughly wet your hair.\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (approximately a nickel-sized amount) to the palm of your hand and work it through your hair. If your hair is long, comb through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if it is longer.\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water.\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion. Avoid rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel to prevent damage.\n\nAnswer: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9", "cot": "[\"To properly clean your hair, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Make sure to select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\\n2. While in the shower, ensure the water is warm but not too hot, and turn the flow down slightly to avoid splashing.\\n3. Thoroughly wet your hair.\\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (approximately a nickel-sized amount) to the palm of your hand and work it through your hair. If your hair is long, comb through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if it is longer.\\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water.\\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion. Avoid rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel to prevent damage.\\n\\nAnswer: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9\", \"To properly clean your hair, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\\n2. Ensure the water is warm, but not too hot. Adjust the flow to avoid splashing.\\n3. Thoroughly wet the hair.\\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about a nickel-sized amount) and work it through the hair. For longer hair, comb through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair.\\n7. Apply conditioner in the same manner as the shampoo. Allow it to remain on for a few minutes.\\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water.\\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion. Avoid rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel as this can cause damage.\", \"To properly clean your hair, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type (as mentioned in passage 2).\\n2. Make sure the water is warm, but not too hot, and turn the flow down to avoid splashing (as mentioned in passage 2).\\n3. Thoroughly wet the hair (as mentioned in passage 2).\\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about a nickel-sized amount) and work it through the hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles (as mentioned in passage 2).\\n5. Rinse the hair completely (as mentioned in passage 1).\\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if the hair is longer (as mentioned in passage 1).\\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner as the shampoo (as mentioned in passage 1).\\n8. Allow the conditioner to remain on for a few minutes (as mentioned in passage 1).\\n9. Rinse the hair with cool water (as mentioned in passage 1).\\n10. Comb through the hair again (as mentioned in passage 1).\\n11. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion instead of rubbing it back and forth or in circles with a towel (as mentioned in passage 1).\\n12. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair (as mentioned in passage 3).\\n\\nAnswer:[Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type, make sure the water is warm, but not too hot, and turn the flow down to avoid splashing, thoroughly wet the hair, apply a small amount of shampoo, work it through the hair, comb through it with your fingers to reduce tangles, rinse the hair completely, use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if the hair is longer, apply a conditioner in the same manner as the shampoo, allow the conditioner to remain on for a few minutes, rinse the hair with cool water, comb through the hair again, dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion instead of rubbing it back and forth or in circles with a towel, and use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair.]\", \"1. Rinse the hair completely and use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair.\\n2. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\\n3. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\\n4. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion. Avoid rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel as this will cause damage to the hair.\\n5. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\\n6. While in the shower, make sure your water is warm, but not too hot. Turn the flow down just a bit so you're not splashing all over the place.\\n7. Thoroughly wet the hair.\\n8. Apply a bit of shampoo into the palm of your hand and work it through the hair. If your hair is longer, comb through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\\n9. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair. Avoid rubbing it with a towel to dry it. Wet hair is weak and such frictions can lead to damage, so handle your hair with proper care to make them beautiful.\"]", "time_sec": 50.51, "generation_time_seconds": 50.5042, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0009, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 10277, 4240, 697, 6869, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 7405, 2704, 311, 3293, 279, 6169, 61932, 323, 64324, 369, 697, 6869, 943, 624, 17, 13, 5976, 304, 279, 17196, 11, 5978, 279, 3015, 374, 8205, 714, 537, 2238, 4017, 11, 323, 2484, 279, 6396, 1495, 10078, 311, 5648, 12503, 19049, 624, 18, 13, 663, 14438, 398, 14401, 697, 6869, 624, 19, 13, 20552, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 61932, 320, 96736, 264, 51249, 27835, 3311, 8, 311, 279, 32452, 315, 697, 1424, 323, 975, 432, 1526, 697, 6869, 13, 1416, 697, 6869, 374, 1293, 11, 3614, 1526, 432, 448, 697, 19225, 311, 7949, 259, 17248, 624, 20, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 6587, 624, 21, 13, 5443, 264, 6884, 4686, 8767, 3614, 311, 4057, 259, 17248, 323, 10876, 279, 6869, 421, 432, 374, 5021, 624, 22, 13, 20552, 264, 64324, 304, 279, 1852, 11566, 498, 9251, 279, 61932, 11, 10693, 432, 311, 7146, 389, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 624, 23, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 448, 7010, 3015, 624, 24, 13, 30841, 279, 6869, 448, 264, 42613, 1667, 264, 3272, 1280, 476, 30411, 10566, 11379, 13, 34006, 55935, 279, 6869, 1182, 323, 13241, 476, 304, 25362, 448, 264, 42613, 311, 5358, 5557, 382, 16141, 25, 220, 16, 11, 220, 17, 11, 220, 18, 11, 220, 19, 11, 220, 20, 11, 220, 21, 11, 220, 22, 11, 220, 23, 11, 220, 24, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.1682