{"id": "735", "question": "what is the difference between sms and mms", "gt": "SMS stands for Short Message Service, commonly referred to as a text message, and allows you to send a text message of up to 160 characters to another device. MMS, which stands for Multimedia Messaging Service, is an evolution of SMS. It allows you to send messages that include pictures, video, or audio content to another device. MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB. SMS is restricted to sending text-only messages, whereas MMS allows a combination of text, pictures, sounds, and videos.", "pred": "The difference between SMS and MMS, as described in the provided passages, lies in the type of content they can transmit. SMS (Short Message Service) allows users to send text-only messages, with a maximum of 160 characters per message. If the message exceeds this limit, it is automatically split into multiple parts. MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is an evolution of SMS and enables users to send messages that include various types of media, such as pictures, video, audio, and text. MMS messages have a larger capacity, up to 300KB, and can include combinations of these different media types. In summary, SMS is limited to text, while MMS offers the capability to send a range of multimedia content.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "The difference between SMS and MMS, as described in the provided passages, lies in the type of content they can transmit. SMS (Short Message Service) allows users to send text-only messages, with a maximum of 160 characters per message. If the message exceeds this limit, it is automatically split into multiple parts. MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is an evolution of SMS and enables users to send messages that include various types of media, such as pictures, video, audio, and text. MMS messages have a larger capacity, up to 300KB, and can include combinations of these different media types. In summary, SMS is limited to text, while MMS offers the capability to send a range of multimedia content.", "cot": "[\"The difference between SMS and MMS, as described in the provided passages, lies in the type of content they can transmit. SMS (Short Message Service) allows users to send text-only messages, with a maximum of 160 characters per message. If the message exceeds this limit, it is automatically split into multiple parts. MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is an evolution of SMS and enables users to send messages that include various types of media, such as pictures, video, audio, and text. MMS messages have a larger capacity, up to 300KB, and can include combinations of these different media types. In summary, SMS is limited to text, while MMS offers the capability to send a range of multimedia content.\", \"SMS allows for text-only messages, while MMS allows for multimedia messages including pictures, sounds, videos, and text. The maximum size for a MMS message is up to 300KB.\", \"SMS (Short Message Service) allows you to send only text messages, while MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows you to send a combination of text, pictures, sounds, and videos.\", \"Step 1: Identify the key differences between SMS and MMS.\\n- SMS (Short Message Service) allows for sending text-only messages.\\n- MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows for sending messages that include pictures, sounds, videos, or any combination of these.\\n\\nStep 2: Compare the content types supported by each service.\\n- SMS supports only text messages.\\n- MMS supports text, pictures, sounds, and videos.\\n\\nStep 3: Consider the size limitations.\\n- SMS has a limit of 160 characters per message.\\n- MMS can carry a larger size of content, up to 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, GIF, etc.\\n\\nStep 4: Note the evolution of services.\\n- SMS is an older service that was the first premium service offered by mobile companies.\\n- MMS is an evolution of SMS, providing additional multimedia capabilities.\\n\\nStep 5: Summarize the differences.\\n- MMS offers more multimedia capabilities than SMS, which is primarily text-based.\\n- SMS is restricted to text-only messages, while MMS can include various multimedia elements.\\n- MMS has a larger content size limit compared to SMS.\\n\\nAnswer: The difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS allows only text messages, while MMS allows for sending text, pictures, sounds, and videos. Additionally, MMS can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, GIF, etc., compared to SMS's 160-character limit.\"]", "time_sec": 29.365, "generation_time_seconds": 29.3581, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0005, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 29909, 323, 386, 4826, 11, 438, 7481, 304, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 15448, 304, 279, 943, 315, 2213, 807, 646, 29282, 13, 29909, 320, 12472, 4856, 5362, 8, 6147, 3847, 311, 3624, 1467, 15382, 6605, 11, 448, 264, 7192, 315, 220, 16, 21, 15, 5766, 817, 1943, 13, 1416, 279, 1943, 35275, 419, 3930, 11, 432, 374, 9463, 6718, 1119, 5248, 5479, 13, 386, 4826, 320, 40404, 26936, 73170, 5362, 8, 374, 458, 15379, 315, 29909, 323, 20081, 3847, 311, 3624, 6605, 429, 2924, 5257, 4494, 315, 3687, 11, 1741, 438, 9185, 11, 2766, 11, 7699, 11, 323, 1467, 13, 386, 4826, 6605, 614, 264, 8131, 8654, 11, 705, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 29862, 11, 323, 646, 2924, 27459, 315, 1493, 2155, 3687, 4494, 13, 758, 12126, 11, 29909, 374, 7199, 311, 1467, 11, 1393, 386, 4826, 6081, 279, 22302, 311, 3624, 264, 2088, 315, 56513, 2213, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.2306, -0.1153, -0.0, -0.0, -0.2091, 0.0, 0.0, -4.7725, -0.2026, -0.2606, -0.0002, -0.0, -1.5848, -0.0068, -0.0046, -1.3574, -0.0433, -0.0083, -1.2684, -0.0527, -0.0533, -0.2132, -0.0576, -0.6621, -0.448, -0.0541, -1.0403, -0.0001, -0.0019, 0.0, -0.0055, -2.596, -0.9826, -0.0, -0.0, -0.1674, -0.8072, -0.0, -0.9549, -0.5768, -0.0329, -0.1506, -1.0058, -0.0024